nt_headline': 'Chaotic Years, With China as Backdrop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qin, Amy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cao Wenxuan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lu Xun (1881-1936)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-01T22:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Qin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/077427f3-6665-5cbc-81a1-3cb2243f0b4e', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/077427f3-6665-5cbc-81a1-3cb2243f0b4e'}, {'abstract': 'Santigold sang of defying constraints even as she was often accompanied by recorded tracks at the Hammerstein Ballroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/02/arts/music/review-santigold-genre-hopping-with-some-nostalgia-and-lots-of-80s-oomph.html', 'snippet': 'Santigold sang of defying constraints even as she was often accompanied by recorded tracks at the Hammerstein Ballroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Healthy self-esteem, relentless self-marketing or cheap, unearned narcissism? Santigold, as the songwriter Santi White calls herself, danced across those distinctions at Hammerstein Ballroom on Saturday night. Early in the set, her two dancers twirled at her side holding selfie sticks; later, they performed in front of a backdrop that turned Santigold’s name and song titles into logos, like a sponsored red-carpet step and repeat at an awards show. By the end, Santigold and the dancers were all wearing sweatsuits patterned with Santigold’s face. It was a show of pride and product, all in one.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/02/arts/02SANTIGOLD/02SANTIGOLD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/02/arts/02SANTIGOLD/02SANTIGOLD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/02/arts/02SANTIGOLD/02SANTIGOLD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/02/arts/02SANTIGOLD/02SANTIGOLD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/02/arts/02SANTIGOLD/02SANTIGOLD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/02/arts/02SANTIGOLD/02SANTIGOLD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/02/arts/02SANTIGOLD/02SANTIGOLD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Santigold, Genre-Hopping With Some Nostalgia and Lots of ’80s Oomph', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Genre-Hopping With a Little Nostalgia and a Lot of ’80s Oomph', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major':