/01/arts/television/fear-the-walking-dead-season-2-episode-4-thomas-abigail.html', 'snippet': 'This week’s “Fear the Walking Dead” finally shed some light on Victor Strand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s episode, “Blood in the Streets,” is all about debt. Owing it. Owning it. Pardoning it, and calling it in. It was Baron Rothschild, the 18th-century nobleman who pronounced “The time to buy is when there’s blood in the streets,” after he’d made a fortune buying up property when Napoleon lost at Waterloo. Naomi Klein in her 2007 book “The Shock Doctrine,” argued that capitalism, in the post-9/11 and Hurricane Katrina era of privatization, monetizes disaster and disproportionately benefits the uber rich. Klein wrote:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01fear/01fear-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01fear/01fear-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01fear/01fear-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01fear/01fear-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01fear/01fear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01fear/01fear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01fear/01fear-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Fear the Walking Dead’ Season 2, Episode 4: Thomas Abigail', 'kicker': 'Fear the Walking Dead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fear the Walking Dead (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-02T02:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By E. A. Hanks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'E.', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Hanks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9369cd2d-9c26-5a15-810c-7078ed826ea4', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9369cd2d-9c26-5a15-810c-7078ed826ea4'}, {'abstract': 'The existential threat of failure has morphed into the nightmare of success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/01/arts/television/silicon-valley-season-3-episode-2-recap.html', 'snippet': 'The existential threat of failure has morphed into the nightmare of success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the lead-up to the third season of “Silicon Valley,” one of its writers, Dan Lyons, published an excerpt in Fortune from “Disrupted,” his new book about his misadventures at a start-up called HubSpot. As a middle-aged man with a background in journalism, Lyons was an odd fit for a company specializing in Internet marketing — a field he admits to knowing nothing about. Once he got started, the experience was even more alienating than he’d imagined. He found himself cast as the “old man” in an office populated by college graduates half his age. He also found a bright, casual work environment that bore “a striking resemblance to the Montessori schools” his children attended:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01silicon/01silicon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01silicon/01silicon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01silicon/01silicon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01silicon/01silicon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01silicon/01silicon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01silicon/01silicon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/arts/01silicon/01silicon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Silicon Valley’ Season 3, Episode 2: Conjoined Triangles of Success', 'kicker': 'Silicon Valley', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (TV Prog