 of confetti as the audience screamed and his family ran on stage. He had won Season 8 of NBC’s reality television show “The Biggest Loser,” shedding more weight than anyone ever had on the program — an astonishing 239 pounds in seven months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/29/science/02BIGGESTLOSER/02BIGGESTLOSER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/04/29/science/02BIGGESTLOSER/02BIGGESTLOSER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/29/science/02BIGGESTLOSER/02BIGGESTLOSER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/29/science/02BIGGESTLOSER/02BIGGESTLOSER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/29/science/02BIGGESTLOSER/02BIGGESTLOSER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/04/29/science/02BIGGESTLOSER/02BIGGESTLOSER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/29/science/02BIGGESTLOSER/02BIGGESTLOSER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After ‘The Biggest Loser,’ Their Bodies Fought to Regain Weight', 'kicker': 'The Science of Fat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Lost Weight? The Body Finds It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kolata, Gina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Obesity (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calories', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cahill, Danny (1969- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Biggest Loser (TV Program)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-02T06:45:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec0276bc-d481-5619-807b-5bb6ecce1b08', 'word_count': 3202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec0276bc-d481-5619-807b-5bb6ecce1b08'}, {'abstract': 'What few gains had been made in maternal health in Sierra Leone have been undone by a health care system decimated by the Ebola outbreak.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/02/how-ebola-destroyed-maternal-health-gains-in-sierra-leone/', 'snippet': 'What few gains had been made in maternal health in Sierra Leone have been undone by a health care system decimated by the Ebola outbreak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When she went into labor last November, 18-year-old Kema James climbed onto the back of a motorbike taxi in her village in eastern Sierra Leone and rode half an hour to the main government hospital in the nearby city of Kenema. When her baby was delivered, he was sickly yellow and stricken with sepsis, an ailment caused by bacteria in the blood, and he hung limply in the hands of the hospital staff. He died five days later before he could be named.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Ebola Destroyed Maternal Health Gains in Sierra Leone', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaques, Monique', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WaterAid', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-02T07:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': "By Finbarr O'Reilly", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Finbarr', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Reilly", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44ba8d95-cd3c-5141-a534-437dc2217444', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44ba8d95-cd3c-5141-a534-437dc2217444'}, {'abstract': 'A retired plumber says the building trades offer a rewarding alternative to going to college.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/02/opinion/a-tradesmans-testimonial.html', 'snippet': 'A retired plumber says the building trades offer a rewarding alternative to going to college.', 'lead_pa