r another Democratic push in the states of vulnerable Republican senators refusing to take up the Supreme Court nomination of Judge Merrick B. Garland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/us/01firstdraftnl-garland/01firstdraftnl-garland-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/01/us/01firstdraftnl-garland/01firstdraftnl-garland-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/us/01firstdraftnl-garland/01firstdraftnl-garland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/us/01firstdraftnl-garland/01firstdraftnl-garland-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/us/01firstdraftnl-garland/01firstdraftnl-garland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/01/us/01firstdraftnl-garland/01firstdraftnl-garland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/01/us/01firstdraftnl-garland/01firstdraftnl-garland-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battles Over Garland Nomination Resume as Senate Enters Recess', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garland, Merrick B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-02T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c8f9f96-3105-51eb-95bc-278e32388c7b', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c8f9f96-3105-51eb-95bc-278e32388c7b'}, {'abstract': 'Chicken with truffles, beef-tamale-chile and smoked duck and collards are among the choices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/04/dining/perfect-pie-bill-yosses.html', 'snippet': 'Chicken with truffles, beef-tamale-chile and smoked duck and collards are among the choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Yosses, best known as a former pastry chef at the White House, is turning out savories as well as sweets. He has started a company, Perfect Pie, that makes and sells pies, including a hearty chicken potpie with truffles, beef-tamale-chile pie in a cornmeal crust, smoked duck and collard pie with several cheeses, an open-faced tomato and cheese tart, and a vegan turmeric tofu and vegetable pie in a millet crust. Pecan, apple and huckleberry are some of the dessert pies. Individual-size ones, $7.50, are sold at Brooklyn Roasting Company’s cafes, most notably the spacious new one in the Flatiron district. By summer, the pies will also be available online and full-size ones will be added, for $40 each: Brooklyn Roasting Company, brooklynroasting.com; Perfect Pie, 212-410-3262, perfectpie.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB/04BURNER_PIE1_WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Savory and Sweet Pies From a Former White House Pastry Chef', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sample: A Presidential Pedigree for Pies Savory and Sweet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yosses, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Perfect Pie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-02T10:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/735f06c8-8297-5210-8360-c5c03847951c', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/735f06c8-8297-5210-8360-c5c03847951c'}, {'abstract': '“Tasting Rome” offers complex bread and curing recipes, and simpler crostini and chicken with tomatoes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/04/dining/tasting-rome-italian-cookbook.html', 'snippet': '“Tasting Rome” offers complex bread and curing recipes, and simpler crostini and chicken with tomatoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’ll see Rome through the eyes and taste buds of Katie Parla and Kristina Gill in this attractive new cookbook. They lightly sketch Roman history via its neighborhoods and their culinary specialties, like offal in Testaccio, Jewish foods from the ghetto and the cooking of Libyan immigrants. Along the way, they describe old recipes that have gone out of fashion and how chefs innovate based on them. Serious cooks may want to tackle the complex bread and pizza recipes and the art of making guanciale at home; others will prefer the simpler crostini slathered with butter and ribbons of anchovy or classic chicken with tomatoes and peppers. I only wish that they had included a list of all the restaurants they mention, wit