'An hour of instruction, followed by afternoon tea at Ladurée SoHo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Learn how to make macarons at home, or give Mom the gift of a baking lesson at Ladurée, followed by a formal afternoon tea. The hourlong classes are for one to six people, including children, on Wednesday, Thursday and Friday afternoons at 2 or 3 p.m. year-round. Extra classes for Mother’s Day will be held this Saturday and Sunday. The cost, $200 per adult, $150 per child, includes the tea, which takes an additional hour, and a gift box: Ladurée SoHo, 398 West Broadway (Spring Street); reservations a week in advance  from salesus@laduree.com. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1502, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB/04BURNER_LESSON1_WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lesson Is Macarons, and Class Is in Session', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Bake: A Gift for Mom, and Dessert, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Laduree', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-02T15:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12cb3b88-ac41-534d-9461-283a6cbde365', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12cb3b88-ac41-534d-9461-283a6cbde365'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Barber and others will show how to cook with ingredients otherwise headed for the landfill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/04/dining/eat-in-global-feedback-union-square-park.html', 'snippet': 'Dan Barber and others will show how to cook with ingredients otherwise headed for the landfill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Global Feedback, an organization that seeks to reduce food waste, has held public eat-ins since 2009. At these events, dishes are prepared by well-known chefs using ingredients that would otherwise have gone to landfills. Next week in Union Square Park, some 5,000 people will be served by chefs like Dan Barber, Jason Weiner and Evan Hanczor, who will also show how to use the ingredients. The organization promises to feed another 5,000 New Yorkers in need: Feeding the 5,000, May 10 from 11 a.m. to 4 p.m., free, feedbackglobal.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/04/dining/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB/04BURNER_EVENT1_WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Reduce Food Waste, an Eat-In at Union Square', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Participate: Turning Food Waste Into Free Meals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Feedback Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Union Square (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barber, Daniel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-02T15:14:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f67a77b8-8033-5383-808c-40fe28a68517', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f67a77b8-8033-5383-808c-40fe28a68517'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Rashid Ali al-Gailani, premier of Iraq, attacks British forces in 1941.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/02/1941-rashid-ali-attacks-british/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Rashid Ali al-Gailani, premier of Iraq, attacks British forces in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON\xa0— Fighting between Iraq troops and British armed forces in Iraq began at dawn today [May 2] at the British airport at Habbaniyah, sixty miles west of Baghdad, Iraq’s capital, and was still in progress late in the day, it was disclosed tonight by official circles here. No details of the fighting were available. Rashid Ali al-Gailani, Premier of Iraq, is reported here to have appealed to Germany for aid against Great Britain, although he was been ostensibly friendly to the British.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, May 3, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Tim