d', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ortved', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58b3379f-029e-5331-a214-baab3d2011c3', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58b3379f-029e-5331-a214-baab3d2011c3'}, {'abstract': 'Health care providers are consolidating. So are insurers. Regulation combined with competition can ensure consumers see the savings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/03/opinion/the-way-to-contain-health-care-costs.html', 'snippet': 'Health care providers are consolidating. So are insurers. Regulation combined with competition can ensure consumers see the savings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE architects of the Affordable Care Act counted on competition in the health insurance market to keep costs down and quality high. While the law has accomplished many of its coverage and cost-containment goals, its vision of a more competitive insurance market seems to be fading.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/03/opinion/03sheffler/03sheffler-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/03/opinion/03sheffler/03sheffler-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/03/opinion/03sheffler/03sheffler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/03/opinion/03sheffler/03sheffler-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1139, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'leg