e-noise-of-time-the-inner-shostakovich.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Barnes’s newest novel imagines the internal emotional battle of the Russian composer Dmitri Shostakovich after Stalin turned against him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 26, 1936, Joseph Stalin attended a performance of Dmitri Shostakovich’s much-acclaimed opera “Lady Macbeth of Mtsensk” at the Bolshoi Theater in Moscow, and the composer was disturbed to see that the Soviet leader and his government companions abruptly left their box before the final act. Two days later, there appeared in Pravda a scathing denunciation of the evening under the headline “Muddle Instead of Music.” The review castigated Shostakovich’s opera as tickling “the perverted taste of the bourgeois with its fidgety, neurotic music.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/03/arts/03BOOKBARNES/03BOOKBARNES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 804, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/03/arts/03BOOKBARNES/03BOOKBARNES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 804}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/03/arts/03BOOKBARNES/03BOOKBARNES-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/03/arts/03BOOKBARNES/03BOOKBARNES-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1958, 'width': 1461, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/03/arts/03BOOKBARNES/03BOOKBARNES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'t