eals-details-of-ordeal.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bae, a missionary freed after two years, said he was never beaten but was verbally abused and was billed $300,000 for hospital care. (He didn’t pay.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kenneth Bae says his North Korean captors interrogated him up to 15 hours a day for the first four weeks of his incarceration and yelled with impatience until he wrote a confession to their liking. But they would later allow Mr. Bae to read his Bible and permit him to pray.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenneth Bae, Longest-Held U.S. Prisoner of North Korea, Reveals Details of Ordeal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Jailed in North Korea Discusses His Ordeal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bae, Kenneth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Not Forgotten: The True Story of My Imprisonment in North Korea (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richardson, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-03T00:32:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06212c0b-38dc-5adf-8c7a-7bb99ee4dfa3', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06212c0b-38dc-5adf-8c7a-7bb99ee4dfa3'}, {'abstract': 'Once a chapel for the city’s gentry, the Cathedral of St. Sa