Metropolitan Museum of Art’s Anna Wintour Costume Center in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The theme of the exhibit at the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s Costume Institute this year was fashion in an age of technology. This meant that people like Andrew Bolton, the institute’s new head curator, along with Jonathan Ive of Apple — who served as a sponsor — spoke in lofty tones about the dichotomies of man versus machine, haute couture versus ready-to-wear, hand-sewn versus mass produced.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Met Gala, Minimalism Is a Relative Term', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Night When Minimalism Means Fur Boleros and Dresses of Bone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Jacob (1978- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-03T03:02:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b26f6091-90b4-5c82-ad89-7d4dc57d2439', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b26f6091-90b4-5c82-ad89-7d4dc57d2439'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s one more reason pregnant women should get a flu shot: It not only protects mothers, but a large study suggests it prevents flu in the infant, too.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/03/flu-shots-protect-babies-too/', 'snippet': 'Here’s one more reason pregnant women should get a flu shot: It not only protects mothers, but a large study suggests it prevents flu in the infant, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s one more reason pregnant women should get a flu shot: It not only protects mothers, but a large study suggests it prevents flu in the infant, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/29/health/well-childbirth/well_childbirth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/29/health/well-childbirth/well_childbirth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/29/health/well-childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/05/29/health/well-childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/29/health/well-childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flu Shots Protect Babies, Too', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swine Influenza', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-03T04:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0917d43-76d6-52d8-bd95-856e13f6082a', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0917d43-76d6-52d8-bd95-856e13f6082a'}, {'abstract': 'New York was rough in the 1970s, which was a mighty lure for Carrie Boretz, who found moments of grace and humor ready for the taking.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/03/carrie-boretz-real-life-on-new-yorks-streets/', 'snippet': 'New York was rough in the 1970s, which was a mighty lure for Carrie Boretz, who found moments of grace and humor ready for the taking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once upon a time, there was a city where people looked at each other or their surroundings instead of their cellphones. Where they spoke to one another, rather than making some clever online comment. Back then, in the 1970s, Manhattan was still rough, and not just on the edges, but through and through, it seemed. And so it was a time when street photographers could roam the streets and find inspiration all around, engaging with their subjects to capture moments of subtlety, beauty and serendipity. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Life on New York’s Streets', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boretz, Carrie', 'rank'