 Dollinger and Rick Rojas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dollinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5541990d-e9e9-5a0c-a63f-cb618f3c29c1', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5541990d-e9e9-5a0c-a63f-cb618f3c29c1'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. MacFarquhar, a scholar at Harvard, discusses how that era may have shaped Chinese leaders who came of age then, such as President Xi Jinping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/04/world/asia/china-cultural-revolution-macfarquhar.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. MacFarquhar, a scholar at Harvard, discusses how that era may have shaped Chinese leaders who came of age then, such as President Xi Jinping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chaos and brutality of the Cultural Revolution, unleashed by Mao Zedong 50 years ago, have received little public examination in China. After the fall of the Gang of Four, the Communist Party and much of the Chinese public chose to move on, as market-oriented policy changes took root. In recent years, however, interest in revisiting this time has grown. Some Chinese have perceived echoes of the Cultural Revolution in the “red culture” campaign in Chongqing under the since-disgraced Bo Xilai or in President Xi Jinping’s anticorruption campaign and have argued that history must be confronted more openly to avoid repeating its mistakes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/world/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/09/world/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/world/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/world/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/world/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/09/world/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/world/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR/09CHINAMACFARQUHAR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Roderick MacFarquhar on the Cultural Revolution and China Today', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cultural Revolution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacFarquhar, Roderick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-03T22:00:16+0000', 'docu