 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Grit: The Power of Passion and Perseverance (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-04T09:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Shulevitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shulevitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5daf80a0-c218-5f8c-bc67-24ebcd71ee20', 'word_count': 1326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5daf80a0-c218-5f8c-bc67-24ebcd71ee20'}, {'abstract': 'My nom de plume protects me from enemies as numerous as they are mysterious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/08/books/review/also-known-as.html', 'snippet': 'My nom de plume protects me from enemies as numerous as they are mysterious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For nearly a decade, I have been writing children’s books under the ridiculous name Pseudonymous Bosch. When my readers ask about it, I usually tell them that Pseudonymous is an old family name and that Bosch is the brand of my dishwasher. (Rarely do I mention Hieronymus Bosch, whose paintings, though edifying in their own way, are not altogether appropriate for my target audience.) If pressed, I admit that, yes, it is a pseudonym. My nom de plume, I explain, is a nom de guerre; it protects me from enemies as numerous as they are mysterious.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '41', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/books/review/08bosch-sub/08bosch-sub-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/08/books/review/08bosch-sub/08bosch-sub-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xl