+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46f5cec4-b248-58c9-94c0-c7efbfa64f56', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46f5cec4-b248-58c9-94c0-c7efbfa64f56'}, {'abstract': 'A wildfire that began last weekend in Alberta remained out of control on Wednesday. Its speed and shifting direction have made it too dangerous to tackle from the ground.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/world/americas/fort-mcmurray-canada-fire.html', 'snippet': 'A wildfire that began last weekend in Alberta remained out of control on Wednesday. Its speed and shifting direction have made it too dangerous to tackle from the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — Walls of flame driven by strong, shifting winds raged out of control on Wednesday in and around the evacuated city of Fort McMurray, Alberta, where firefighters were helpless to stop the destruction and where about 88,000 people had fled their homes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fort McMurray Blaze, Fast and Unpredictable, Keeps Firefighters at a Distance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Volatile Blaze in Alberta Keeps Firefighters at a Distance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort McMurray (Alberta)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBERTA (CANADA)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-04T14:11:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c5776bd-1beb-54ee-935d-6e714d1a3707', 'word_count': 1274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c5776bd-1beb-54ee-935d-6e714d1a3707'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: British troops attack Irak forces in 1941.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/04/1941-british-hit-basra-and-baghdad/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: British troops attack Irak forces in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The fighting in Irak between British forces and Irak troops loyal to Rashid Ali al-Gailani, who seized power in that country a month ago, has now spread to the Basra and Bagdad areas and is growing more violent, it was learned in London tonight [May 4]. The Irak government has halted the flow of oil from the Mosul oil fields through the desert pipe line to Haifa, Palestine, according to a Vichy report of the Reuters (British) news agency quoted by The Associated Press. — New York Herald Tribune, May 5, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/blogs/05iht-oldmay05-baghdad/05iht-oldmay05-baghdad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/0