d to recent reviews of Charles Bock’s “Alice & Oliver,” Stevie Smith’s poems and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Painful Task', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-04T21:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b7c757a-f1cd-570c-98e3-36b777e23189', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b7c757a-f1cd-570c-98e3-36b777e23189'}, {'abstract': 'The second season of this Netflix series keeps on exploring issues of loneliness, love and friendship among the aging.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/arts/television/review-grace-and-frankie-fonda-and-tomlin-continue-to-shine.html', 'snippet': 'The second season of this Netflix series keeps on exploring issues of loneliness, love and friendship among the aging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marta Kauffman was one of the creators of “Friends,” which was among the last great money-minting multicamera sitcoms. When you create and shepherd a “Friends” for 10 seasons, you’ve already had a successful career in television. After that show went off the air in 2004, Ms. Kauffman focused on television movies and documentaries for a decade. But last year, she got back in the sitcom game with “Grace and Frankie” on Netflix, which she created with Howard J. Morris.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/arts/05FRANKIE1/05FRANKIE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 