of music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Through the crackle of an old phonograph recording, the tenor’s voice sounds musky and slightly metallic, but the German words ring out sharp and clear. The soprano’s tone is warm, opulent and heady.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/arts/05HOLOCAUSTSUB/05HOLOCAUSTSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/05/arts/05HOLOCAUSTSUB/05HOLOCAUSTSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/arts/05HOLOCAUSTSUB/05HOLOCAUSTSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/arts/05HOLOCAUSTSUB/05HOLOCAUSTSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1669, 'width': 1335, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/arts/05HOLOCAUSTSUB/05HOLOCAUSTSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/05/arts/05HOLOCAUSTSUB/05HOLOCAUSTSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/arts/05HOLOCAUSTSUB/05HOLOCAUSTSUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love and Loss, Set to Music, During the Holocaust', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love and Loss, Set to Music, During the Holocaust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Hermann', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buchenwald Concentration Camp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-04T21:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d18dfd0-8bd9-5a64-879c-68ad8fcc3871', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d18dfd0-8bd9-5a64-879c-68ad8fcc3871'}, {'abstract': 'The Danish-born model turned actress was married to the French director and was his muse and leading lady.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/movies/anna-karina-jean-luc-godard.html', 'snippet': 'The Danish-born model turned actress was married to the French director and was his muse and leading lady.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the American cinephile circles of the 1960s, each new film from the French director Jean-Luc Godard was an event. Vital film critics like Manny Farber, Andrew Sarris and Pauline Kael and public intellectuals like Susan Sontag weighed in, creating a near-constant colloquy on how this director was reinventing cinema. The buzz and argument were equally fevered in Paris, Mr. Godard’s home at the time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{