 'Charles Gatewood, a boundary-pushing photographer who mapped, provocatively and disturbingly, the subcultures of strippers, sex-club devotees, bikers, body piercers and fetishists, died on Thursday in San Francisco. He was 73.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charles Gatewood, Photographer of Extremes, Dies at 73', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charles Gatewood, Photographer of Rock Stars and Cultural Extremes, Is Dead at 73', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gatewood, Charles (1942-2016)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T01:13:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc9e618b-8810-5754-866a-2c1bff7c9867', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc9e618b-8810-5754-866a-2c1bff7c9867'}, {'abstract': 'News and updates from around the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/us/national-briefing.html', 'snippet': 'News and updates from around the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A state court judge on Wednesday temporarily blocked state authorities from licensing as a child care facility a federal immigration detention center holding migrant children and their mothers. The Texas Department of Family and Protective Services was preparing to issue a child care license to the center, located in Dilley, where families seeking asylum, including very young children, are detained. Ruling on an emergency request by Grassroots Leadership, a prison advocacy group, Judge Karin Crump of Travis County found it was “probable” that new regulations adopted by the department to support the license were inconsistent with state law. On Friday, Texas issued a child care license to a similar detention center nearby in Karnes City. JULIA PRESTON', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Briefing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ku Klux Klan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T01:15:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba1b3327-c7c5-5edc-a4f4-b3a36c6c219b', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba1b3327-c7c5-5edc-a4f4-b3a36c6c219b'}, {'abstract': 'He shared the prize in 1996 for discovering a new form of carbon, nicknamed the buckyball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/science/harold-kroto-nobel-prize-winning-chemist-is-dead-at-76.html', 'snippet': 'He shared the prize in 1996 for discovering a new form of carbon, nicknamed the buckyball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harold Kroto, who shared the 1996 Nobel Prize in Chemistry for discovering a new arrangement of carbon known as the buckyball, died on Saturday in East Sussex, England. He was 76.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New Y