rticle/bc88076d-f3e2-52f1-a8a4-c088c7a5e911'}, {'abstract': 'The denim line M.i.h debuts a monthlong residency, where the brand’s greatest hits will be sold alongside a series of collaborations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/t-magazine/fashion/mih-jeans-pop-up-london.html', 'snippet': 'The denim line M.i.h debuts a monthlong residency, where the brand’s greatest hits will be sold alongside a series of collaborations.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s not a pastiche of the 1970s,” says Chloe Lonsdale, the founder of the nostalgia-infused women’s denim line M.i.h Jeans, which this week marks its 10th anniversary with a just-opened pop-up shop in London’s Soho. “We could have sourced shag-pile rugs and gone all Austin Powers — but that’s not what we’re about. Denim grounds us and keeps us more real.” The space has a light and airy feel that’s true to the way the brand balances old with new: The 1950s wicker hanging chairs in the window are offset by a contemporary Tobi-Ishi table by B&B Italia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-mihlondon-06/05tmag-mihlondon-06-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-mihlondon-06/05tmag-mihlondon-06-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-mihlondon-06/05tmag-mihlondon-06-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-mihlondon-06/05tmag-mihlondon-06-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo',