etary-policy-but-not-on-debt.html', 'snippet': 'He made an offhand comment that, if taken literally, would amount to threatening to undermine the United States’ creditworthiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump emphasizes his business savvy as a reason to make him president. In a phone interview with CNBC on Thursday, he showed both the strengths and limitations of this background as he talked about the Federal Reserve, the dollar and the national debt in more detail than he has before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/upshot/06UP-Fed/06UP-Fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/06/upshot/06UP-Fed/06UP-Fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/upshot/06UP-Fed/06UP-Fed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/upshot/06UP-Fed/06UP-Fed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/upshot/06UP-Fed/06UP-Fed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/06/upshot/06UP-Fed/06UP-Fed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/upshot/06UP-Fed/06UP-Fed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump Is Coherent on Monetary Policy, but Not on Debt', 'kicker': 'The 2016 Race', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T17:31:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Irwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Irwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8f5a189-a40c-5ca7-b937-4e3e779d8290', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8f5a189-a40c-5ca7-b937-4e3e779d8290'}, {'abstract': 'The legendary French New Wave actress and muse sat down with T in advance of an appearance, and a weeklong series of screenings, at Film Forum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/t-magazine/entertainment/anna-karina-actress-interview-film-forum.html', 'snippet': 'The legendary French New Wave actress and muse sat down with T in advance of an appearance, and a weeklong series of screenings, at Film Forum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anna Karina was only 19 years old when she met the director Jean-Luc Godard. In the two years since she had moved to Paris from Copenhagen, where she was born, Karina had gone from being penniless on the streets to an in-demand model. After Godard cast her in “Le Petit Soldat,” she quickly became an emblem of the French New Wave through her performances in Godard’s films — and also his wife and muse. Their relationship was, by all accounts, tumultuous, and they divorced in 1965. But the films, and especially Karina’s performances, have only gained in esteem over time. “I could be their grandmother,” she says with a smile about the fans that still approach her. In a recent conversation before an event in her honor at the Brooklyn Academy of Music earlier this week (she’ll also appear at Film Forum tomorrow to kick off a series dedicated to her work with Godard), Karina talked about her early days modeling, how she got her name and the pleasure and pain of her time with Godard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-karina-01/05tmag-karina-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-karina-01/05tmag-karina-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-karina-01/05tmag-karina-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-karina-01/05tmag-karina-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1146, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-karina-01/05tmag-karina-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-karina-01/05tmag-karina-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/t-magazine/05tmag-karina-01/05tmag-karina-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anna Karina Reflects on Life With Godard — and Getting Her Name From Coco Chanel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Forum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karina, Anna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T17:32:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Entertainment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig Hubert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d86ef89a-1bcc-5df9-8cf2-0f8cee886536', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d86ef89a-1bcc-5df9-8cf2-0f8cee886536'}, {'abstract': '“Captain America: Civil War” does not in any way transcend the conventions of the genre. On the contrary: it succeeds because it doesn’t really try.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/06/movies/captain-america-civil-war-review-chris-evans.html', 'snippet': '“Captain America: Civil War” does not in any way transcend the conventions of the genre. On the contrary: it succeeds because it doesn’t really try.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you release a movie called “Captain America: Civil War” to an ideologically polarized nation in the midst of a notably contentious presidential campaign, you can expect to reap a whirlwind of think pieces. In spite of occasional public scolding about the rampant misuse of allegorical interpretation, hard-pressed, click-seeking cultural journalists and political pundits can be counted on to take up the hard work of finding echoes, resonances and subtexts in a big pop-cultural pseudo-event. If you hybridized Donald J. Trump and Elon Musk, would you get Tony Stark? Would Captain America’s endorsement have made a difference for John Kasich? Is Ant-Man a Bernie Bro?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06CAPTAIN/06CAPTAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06CAPTAIN/06CAPTAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06CAPTAIN/06CAPTAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06CAPTAIN/06CAPTAIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1076, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06CAPTAIN/06CAPTAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06CAPTAIN/06CAPTA