palestinian-youths-in-jail.html', 'snippet': 'A reader says he was “appalled” by the sympathetic tone of an article about youths who had attacked Israelis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Youths in Jail', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Palestinian Youths in Jail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T18:35:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/103d068f-a3fc-5fe9-a93f-fba3f047c312', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/103d068f-a3fc-5fe9-a93f-fba3f047c312'}, {'abstract': 'In his chairs for Cappellini, the Swedish designer shows off an affection for needlepoint.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/style/johan-lindsten-furniture-design-chairs.html', 'snippet': 'In his chairs for Cappellini, the Swedish designer shows off an affection for needlepoint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Geography is destiny, or at least it was for Johan Lindsten. Mr. Lindsten, 34, grew up in a forested part of Sweden called the “furniture kingdom,” which is home to Ikea and dozens of other housewares companies. Today, lo and behold, he designs furniture, including chairs with needlepoint nature scenes that have put him on an international stage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/garden/05HOMEjohan/05HOMEjohan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/05/garden/05HOMEjohan/05HOMEjohan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/garden/05HOMEjohan/05HOMEjohan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/garden/05HOMEjohan/05HOMEjohan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/garden/05HOMEjohan/05HOMEjohan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/05/garden/05HOMEjohan/05HOMEjohan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/garden/05HOMEjohan/05HOMEjohan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Johan Lindsten: A Different Kind of Sampler', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chairs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T18:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68f8eea4-f549-56af-8683-795bc7761e78', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68f8eea4-f549-56af-8683-795bc7761e78'}, {'abstract': 'The long-missing manuscript of a Federalist Paper written by John Jay has been found at the Brooklyn Historical Society.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/better-than-a-hamilton-shout-out-john-jay-manuscript-surfaces/', 'snippet': 'The long-missing manuscript of a Federalist Paper written by John Jay has been found at the Brooklyn Historical Society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Jay may have written only five of the 85 articles in the Federalist Papers, as students of early American history — and the legions who have memorized the “Hamilton” cast album — know. But Jay was also the only one of the authors known to have kept his manuscripts, all but one of which have been studied by scholars.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Better Than a ‘Hamilton’ Shout-Out? John Jay Manuscript Surfaces', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hailing Another Patriot: John Jay Is on a Roll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federalist Papers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miranda, Lin-Manuel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Historical Society', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T18:42:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e36f73bf-ddbd-51f8-b74b-5fcabd2aa5ad', 'word_count': 553, 'uri':