7ce-5db2-b941-37afb3fdb266'}, {'abstract': 'A show at David Zwirner focuses on the works he made after he spent 1980 wandering the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/08/arts/design/informed-by-travel-sigmar-polke-painted-playful-journeys.html', 'snippet': 'A show at David Zwirner focuses on the works he made after he spent 1980 wandering the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1980, the German artist Sigmar Polke traveled the world, from Indonesia to Tasmania to Thailand. The trip informed Polke’s subsequent work — his use of unconventional materials and brilliant, sometimes chemically toxic, colors. Now the David Zwirner Gallery is presenting a show, “Eine Winterreise (Winter Journey),” that focuses on the theme of travel in Polke’s work, from his playful take on 1960s tourist scenes to his layered paintings from the 1980s that explore intellectual as well as physical journeys.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE3/08GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE3/08GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 767}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE3/08GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE3/08GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1603, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE3/08GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75,