ion of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T20:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer and Alexander Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f7aaaf8-6564-55a0-a5a1-a28d727c663b', 'word_count': 1307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f7aaaf8-6564-55a0-a5a1-a28d727c663b'}, {'abstract': 'The IFC Center will screen the film as the last in a Streep series; it includes a talk with the director Robert Benton and the author Michael Schulman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/08/movies/meryl-streep-in-kramer-vs-kramer-an-early-and-defiant-role.html', 'snippet': 'The IFC Center will screen the film as the last in a Streep series; it includes a talk with the director Robert Benton and the author Michael Schulman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meryl Streep has rarely played a role as fiercely defiant as that of Joanna in Robert Benton’s 1979 film, “Kramer vs. Kramer,” in which her character abruptly leaves her husband (Dustin Hoffman), an advertising executive, and young son to find herself. More than a year after the father and son have grown close, Joanna returns to claim the boy, and the couple become involved in a brutal custody battle. Ms. Streep won her first Academy Award for the role, which inspired one of her strongest, if not always sympathetic, performances. The movie, based on a novel by Avery Corman, reflected the feminist struggles of the period, and Ms. Streep didn’t shy away from playing Joanna as an angry, self-assertive woman.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE9/08GUIDE9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE9/08GUIDE9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE9/08GUIDE9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE9/08GUIDE9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE9/08GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE9/08GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE9/08GUIDE9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Meryl Streep in ‘Kramer vs. Kramer’: An Early (and Defiant) Role', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film; Streep in an Early (and Defiant) Role', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Kramer vs. Kramer (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IFC Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benton, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schulman, Michael (Author)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Her Again: Becoming Meryl Streep (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T20:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ad4feb4-5136-5b2b-8b94-d613d89c774a', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ad4feb4-5136-5b2b-8b94-d613d89c774a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Lang is a soloist with the Philadelphia Orchestra, and Ms. Wang performs at a recital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/08/arts/music/lang-lang-and-yuja-wang-stars-from-china-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Lang is a soloist with the Philadelphia Orchestra, and Ms. Wang performs at a recital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two superstar Chinese pianists of the same generation but with quite different personalities, Lang Lang, 33, and Yuja Wang, 29, come to Carnegie Hall this week. On Wednesday, May 11, Mr. Lang, who combines stupendous technique with theatrical flair, is soloist with the Philadelphia Orchestra, conducted by its dynamic music director Yannick Nézet-Séguin, playing Rachmaninoff’s less-heard, youthful First Concerto. After intermission, Mr. Nézet-Séguin conducts Mahler’s Symphony No. 10 in Deryck Cooke’s much-debated performing edition that includes the British scholar’s completion of the last three movements, which were left in sketchy states by the composer.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 550}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 939, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1879, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lang Lang and Yuja Wang, Stars From China, at Carnegie Hall', '