ious drama to the cable channels, this CBS series competed with them backward, in heels and twice as fast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/06/arts/television/the-good-wife-a-broadcast-gem-fades-away.html', 'snippet': 'While the broadcast networks had all but ceded ambitious drama to the cable channels, this CBS series competed with them backward, in heels and twice as fast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The final season of “The Good Wife” found Alicia Florrick (Julianna Margulies), after a failed stint in politics, rebooting her law career by working in the Chicago bond court. Serving the indigent, she had scant seconds to consult with clients, get the facts, make a plan. Then it was on to the next — bang bang, no time to fuss or look back.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06WIFE/06WIFE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06WIFE/06WIFE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06WIFE/06WIFE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06WIFE/06WIFE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1004, 'width': 1504, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06WIFE/06WIFE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06WIFE/06WIFE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06WIFE/06WIFE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Good Wife’: A Broadcast Gem Fades Away', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Good Wife,’ a Broadcast Gem, Fades Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Margulies, Julianna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Michelle (Screenwriter)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Robert (Screenwriter)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Good Wife (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T21:42:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Poniewozik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poniewozik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae369bec-5c30-5e04-996e-85a9b793f943', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae369bec-5c30-5e04-996e-85a9b793f943'}, {'abstract': 'The department store enlisted the artist and gallery owner to work on its latest windows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/t-magazine/fashion/barneys-margaret-lee-windows.html', 'snippet': 'The department store enlisted the artist and gallery owner to work on its latest windows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In talking about Dennis Freedman, the creative director of Barneys New York, the artist Margaret Lee immediately mentions his avant-garde furniture collection — such a boundary-pushing sight to behold that it informed parts of her 2014 show “Closer to Right Than Wrong/ Closer to Wrong Than Right,” specifically the size and arrangement. Now, the pair is picking up the dialogue again, collaborating on a series of windows for Barneys and bringing New Yorkers into the conversation. “What you see downtown,” Freedman explains, referring to the pair of dioramas on Seventh Avenue, “started with a discussion of spaces that people live in — and the spaces they create to present themselves in a certain way — and we focused on the kitchen.” He and Lee explored, and exaggerated, the idea that in some homes, the room is rarely used for cooking (which Freedman describes as neither right nor wrong, rather, “it is what it is”). Scroll over the photographs above and below to learn more about their concept.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Conceptual Kitchen With Barneys and Margaret Lee', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barneys New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-05T21:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d984a92-1f8f-5412-821f-998b330279f1', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d984a92-1f8f-5412-821f-998b330279f1'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Trump seems to think praising taco bowls on Cinco de Mayo will help him with Latino voters.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/05/dear-donald-trump-they-dont-love-you/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Trump seems to think praising taco bowls on Cinco de Mayo will help him with Latino voters.', 'lead_paragraph': '*In other words, polls suggest that Latinos are not inclined to support  the presumptive Republican presidential nominee, no matter what he eats, or what public displays of affection he attempts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/opinion/5downesWEB2/5downesWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/05/opinion/5downesWEB2/5downesWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/opinion/5downesWEB2/5downesWEB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/opinion/5downesWEB2/5downesWEB2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1449, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/opinion/5downesWEB2/5downesWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/05/opinion/5downesWEB2/5downesWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/05/opinion/5downesWEB2/5downesWEB2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear Donald Trump: They Don’t Love You*', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker'