0de040'}, {'abstract': 'An idol group trades heavily in kawaii, the Japanese concept of cuteness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/06/arts/music/review-babymetal-melds-metal-with-a-large-dose-of-cuteness.html', 'snippet': 'An idol group trades heavily in kawaii, the Japanese concept of cuteness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In ponytail or pigtails, pleatherlike tops with puffy shoulders and iridescent black tulle skirts, the singers of Babymetal stood on individual six-inch risers so the crowd could see them properly. Behind them, onstage at the PlayStation Theater on Wednesday night, were the band’s musicians: two guitarists, a bassist and a drummer, all in white robes and white-painted faces, smiling broadly. The singers (Suzuka Nakamoto, Yui Mizuno and Moa Kikuchi) spoke in English with slight catches in their voices. What they said was, in order, “You make me happy!” And, “I’m happy because of you!” And, “I will never forget today!”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06BABYMETAL/06BABYMETAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06BABYMETAL/06BABYMETAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06BABYMETAL/06BABYMETAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/06BABYMETAL/06BABYMETAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 1237, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i