_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson and Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/435292dd-b8ca-5624-a98c-c78249cd6ad0', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/435292dd-b8ca-5624-a98c-c78249cd6ad0'}, {'abstract': 'Mythical creatures and media blindness.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/06/paul-ryan-and-the-trump-fail/', 'snippet': 'Mythical creatures and media blindness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been a lot of navel-gazing in the news media about how everyone — well, *cough*, almost everyone — wrote off Donald Trump’s chance of getting the nomination. The thing is, the polls pointed to Trump strength right from the beginning, and it should have been clear by early fall at the latest that Trump wasn’t going to be a bubble story like the various not-Romneys of 2012. So why did most of the commentariat get it so wrong for so long?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '“Paul Ryan” and the Trump Fail', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-05-06T17:22:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c2dec5e-a360-5f49-905c-27343cc2df47', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c2dec5e-a360-5f49-905c-27343cc2df47'}, {'abstract': 'The Philippines’ democracy is choked by oligarchs, and the people have had enough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/07/opinion/why-filipinos-are-voting-for-a-new-dictator.html', 'snippet': 'The Philippines’ democracy is choked by oligarchs, and the people have had enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANILA — A carnival-like atmosphere has descended on this country ahead of the presidential election on Monday: dancing showgirls at campaign events, candidates inviting one another to “slap me,” and reports of cash distributed in exchange for cheers. The Philippine system of government, inherited from our American colonizers, is unique, with its raucous collection of political parties based not on ideology but on personality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07Syjuco-INYTb/07Syjuco-INYTb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07Syjuco-INYTb/07Syjuco-INYTb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07Syjuco-INYTb/07Syjuco-INYTb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07Syjuco-INYTb/07Syjuco-INYTb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07Syjuco-INYTb/07Syjuco-INYTb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbna