.nytimes.com/2016/05/07/books/louise-erdrich-on-her-new-novel-larose-and-the-psychic-territory-of-native-americans.html', 'snippet': 'Interviewed in Minneapolis, where she runs her own bookstore, the author spoke about her conception of family, ancestors and storytelling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — Louise Erdrich is, along with Garrison Keillor and Ann Patchett, among the handful of American writers crazy enough to want to own a bookstore. Hers, in the Kenwood neighborhood here, is in what used to be a dentist’s office, though perhaps not a very busy one. Neighbors remember that the dentist was often asleep in his own chair.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/arts/07ERDRICH1/07ERDRICH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/07/arts/07ERDRICH1/07ERDRICH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/arts/07ERDRICH1/07ERDRICH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/arts/07ERDRICH1/07ERDRICH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/arts/07ERDRICH1/07ERDRICH1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/07/arts/07ERDRICH1/07ERDRICH1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/arts/07ERDRICH1/07ERDRICH1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Louise Erdrich on Her New Novel, ‘LaRose,’ and the Psychic Territory of Native Americans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obsessively Mining a Familial Landscape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Charles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdrich, Louise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'LaRose (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-06T19:07:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/627be75b-a3b3-5269-b5ea-46687682de66', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/627be75b-a3b3-5269-b5ea-46687682de66'}, {'abstract': 'Pamela Paul — joined by Dwight Garner, Sam Tanenhaus and Gary Shteyngart — discusses the ins and outs of The Times’s longest-running podcast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2016/05/09/insider/events/09-Insider-Book-Audio.html', 'snippet': 'Pamela Paul — joined by Dwight Garner, Sam Tanenhaus and Gary Shteyngart — discusses the ins and outs of The Times’s longest-running podcast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pamela Paul — joined by Dwight Garner, Sam Tanenhaus and Gary Shteyngart — discusses the ins and outs of The Times’s longest-running podcast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pamela Paul: Talking Books at The Times', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-05-06T19:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'subsection_name': 'Insider Events', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/87d0f416-41fd-520a-b7c2-a821370d143a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/87d0f416-41fd-520a-b7c2-a821370d143a'}, {'abstract': 'Josh Kline’s “Unemployment” uses a variety of media to explore the effects of the mortgage crisis and recession on real people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/06/t-magazine/art/josh-kline-unemployment-art.html', 'snippet': 'Josh Kline’s “Unemployment” uses a variety of media to explore the effects of the mortgage crisis and recession on real people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As an artist who matured during the rise of the so-called “attention economy” — which has rewarded practices that combine a miscellany of ingredients into sometimes tenuous works of art — Josh Kline’s anticipated new solo show at 47 Canal gallery demonstrates how a little editing and restraint can elevate unnerving sculptures to an indelible mise-en-scène. Titled “Unemployment,” Kline’s exhibition begins in the gallery foyer, where the stuffing of an easy chair upholstered in clear vinyl is in plain view: shredded financial data, credit card offers and mortgage contracts formerly belonging to the artist — and to the unemployed persons represented in his show. In the main exhibition space, amid illuminated shopping carts replete with empty plastic bottles custom-molded in the shape of human hands and discarded computer keyboards silicone-cast in a full spectrum of skin tones, life-size individuals in business attire lay on the polyester sandstone carpet. They are curled in the fetal position and bagged in plastic like yesterday’s recycling — because, in a sense, they have been recycled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kline01/06tmag-kline01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kline01/06tmag-kline01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kline01/06tmag-kline01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kline01/06tmag-kline01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1454, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kline01/06tmag-kline01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kline01/06tmag-kline01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/t-magazine/06tmag-kline01/06tmag-kline01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Art Show That Addresses the Economic Collapse Head-On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-0