, '_id': 'nyt://article/bba79fc3-1e39-5671-9629-ec7932f2c7e1', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bba79fc3-1e39-5671-9629-ec7932f2c7e1'}, {'abstract': 'As his predecessors did, New York’s mayor will hold a weekly on-air conversation with his constituents, signaling a shift in his communications strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/07/nyregion/taking-calls-on-radio-de-blasio-now-embraces-a-mayoral-tradition.html', 'snippet': 'As his predecessors did, New York’s mayor will hold a weekly on-air conversation with his constituents, signaling a shift in his communications strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the weekly call-in radio show with the mayor was a New York City tradition. It provided a chance for Sal from Brooklyn or anyone else from the five boroughs to get on the line directly with the city’s chief executive, and for the mayor at the time to reveal, inadvertently or deliberately, his personality and style of thinking.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/nyregion/07MAYOR/07MAYOR-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/07/nyregion/07MAYOR/07MAYOR-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/nyregion/07MAYOR/07MAYOR-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/nyregion/07MAYOR/07MAYOR-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag