e theater makes as grand an entrance as it is possible to make while being propped up by minders. On a recent Friday, Ms. Alonso, the 95-year-old director of the Ballet Nacional de Cuba, was ushered to her balcony seat. She opened her ballerina arms to the audience, who stood and cheered as if at a royal appearance. Ms. Alonso, blind or nearly blind for decades, has reigned over Cuban ballet for more than 60 years, longer than her stalwart supporter Fidel Castro lasted as head of state.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuban Ballet: Proud Past, Promising Future', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuban Ballet: Proud Past, Promising Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Havana (Cuba)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALONSO, ALICIA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ballet Nacional de Cuba', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-06T22:10:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0150bcb-adc8-57aa-bcad-b9289f49b0ec', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0150bcb-adc8-57aa-bcad-b9289f49b0ec'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know at the end of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/06/nytnow/your-friday-evening-briefing-fort-mcmurray-donald-trump-kentucky-derby.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know at the end of the day.', 'le