': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/b97623c0-fa83-5255-8a79-e8f77b8ae6b0', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b97623c0-fa83-5255-8a79-e8f77b8ae6b0'}, {'abstract': 'The notion that patients would not become addicted to opioids has proved to be one of the biggest mistakes in modern medicine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/07/opinion/the-opioid-epidemic-we-failed-to-foresee.html', 'snippet': 'The notion that patients would not become addicted to opioids has proved to be one of the biggest mistakes in modern medicine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEGINNING in the late 1990s, pharmaceutical companies selling high-dose opioids seized upon a notion, based on flimsy scientific evidence, that regardless of the length of treatment, patients would not become addicted to opioids.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07kesslerWeb/07kesslerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07kesslerWeb/07kesslerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07kesslerWeb/07kesslerWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07kesslerWeb/07kesslerWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07kesslerWeb/07kessle