gh this is a depressed economy, the trailer homes are worth about $500,000 each. Even in Canadian currency that’s a lot.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07thorntonWeb/07thorntonWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07thorntonWeb/07thorntonWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07thorntonWeb/07thorntonWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07thorntonWeb/07thorntonWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1512, 'width': 2016, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07thorntonWeb/07thorntonWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07thorntonWeb/07thorntonWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07thorntonWeb/07thorntonWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fleeing Fire in Canada’s Oil Country', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trying  to Outrun the Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort McMurray (Alberta)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBERTA (CANADA)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-07T02:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Thornton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thornton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6899e069-c0a9-57d3-88a9-bf6be0854e38', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6899e069-c0a9-57d3-88a9-bf6be0854e38'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate has failed to confirm dozens of uncontroversial nominees to fill vacancies in the federal trial courts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/07/opinion/americas-trial-court-judges-our-front-line-for-justice.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate has failed to confirm dozens of uncontroversial nominees to fill vacancies in the federal trial courts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE outcry over the Senate’s failure to hold hearings on Judge Merrick Garland’s nomination to the Supreme Court is fully justified. But that isn’t the only judiciary scandal on Capitol Hill. Even as the spotlight shines on the high court, the Senate has refused to confirm dozens of uncontroversial nominees to fill vacancies in the federal trial courts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/07/opinion/07scheindlin/07scheindlin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 