, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6343b48d-5858-5c5a-887b-48784c626259', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6343b48d-5858-5c5a-887b-48784c626259'}, {'abstract': 'This past week, in a move that was long expected, Fairway’s parent company, Fairway Group Holdings, filed for bankruptcy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/08/nyregion/no-longer-a-market-like-no-other-fairway-fades.html', 'snippet': 'This past week, in a move that was long expected, Fairway’s parent company, Fairway Group Holdings, filed for bankruptcy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past week, in a move that was long expected, if no less mourned among those who nervously keep record of the disappearing New York of Woody Allen and Nora Ephron, Fairway’s parent company, Fairway Group Holdings, filed for bankruptcy. This shouldn’t necessarily occasion a eulogy; the grocery chain will continue its operations as it restructures and reduces its debt load. At the same time, it is hard to feel optimistic about the future of the endearingly chaotic, unpolished New York retail style that Fairway has embodied.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/nyregion/08BIGCITY1SUB/08BIGCITY1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/08/nyregion/08BIGCITY1SUB/08BIGCITY1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/nyregion/08BIGCITY1SUB/08BIGCITY1SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag