 gentrified, the store has changed by expanding its stock of traditional Middle Eastern products to include specialty items from around the globe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a blustery spring Saturday in Brooklyn Heights, and the customers shopping at Sahadi’s Importing Company on Atlantic Avenue had their heads covered — hijabs, snapbacks, church derbies, pork pies, bandannas, kufi skull caps — and their hands full of products, samples and numbered tickets. The tickets are needed to keep order and flow at this foodie dreamscape, which resembles an active bazaar with a jumble of containers and barrels, crowded counters and overstocked shelves. The action is all inside, but the store’s primary advocate was out front, telling stories.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sahadi’s Offers a World of Things That Can Be Put in a Jar', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fresh and Frozen, Candied and Brined', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Heights (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-07T21:10:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Cotto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26ab7799-eb07-52a7-816f-a97a622e18df', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26ab7799-eb07-52a7-816f-a97a622e18df'}, {'abstract': 'The actor and comed