20-5423f8ade359', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/048ddaba-b657-503f-ac20-5423f8ade359'}, {'abstract': 'In this, the best episode of the season so far, the guys are in perfect step.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/08/arts/television/silicon-valley-season-3-episode-3-recap.html', 'snippet': 'In this, the best episode of the season so far, the guys are in perfect step.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s one for the popular Twitter hashtag #ExplainAFilmPlotBadly: “It’s a 2001 casino heist film starring Julia Roberts and 11 men.” That’s Jared on “Ocean’s Eleven,” the inspiration for a devious ruse that would allow Richard and his original Pied Piper team to work on their consumer platform while fooling Jack into believing that they’re making his awful data storage box. And with that, the overarching plot for Season 3 of “Silicon Valley” seems to lock into place, something akin to the fifth season of “The Wire,” which had a journalist from The Baltimore Sun making up a serial killer to boost his profile. What an exciting, inspired idea!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/08SILICON/08SILICON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/08SILICON/08SILICON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/08SILICON/08SILICON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/06/arts/08SILICON/08SILICON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio