 of five successive spring evening auctions, at first seemed reckless, filling a catalog with challenging, even disturbing work. With a kneeling Hitler and a wooden grid of potatoes, it was a far cry from the auction staples that can be counted on to command high prices.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/nyregion/09AUCTION1sub/09AUCTION1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/09/nyregion/09AUCTION1sub/09AUCTION1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/nyregion/09AUCTION1sub/09AUCTION1sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/nyregion/09AUCTION1sub/09AUCTION1sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1234, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/nyregion/09AUCTION1sub/09AUCTION1sub-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/09/nyregion/09AUCTION1sub/09AUCTION1sub-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/nyregion/09AUCTION1sub/09AUCTION1sub-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie’s Sale Opens Spring Auction Season Amid Predictions of a Softening', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christie’s Sale Calms Predictions of a Soft Market', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyburn, Scott', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Phillips Auctioneers LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Basquiat, Jean-Michel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Twombly, Cy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-09T03:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin and Scott Reyburn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reyburn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d84924e2-8e13-5d6f-86ef-5356e3365fcf', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d84924e2-8e13-5d6f-86ef-5356e3365fcf'}, {'abstract': 'Yankees starter Luis Severino pitched well for the most part but gave up a first-inning home run to Dustin Pedroia and two subsequent shots to David Ortiz as Boston won on the road.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/09/sports/baseball/david-ortiz-and-boston-red-sox-jump-on-yankees-mistakes-in-win.html', 'snippet': 'Yankees starter Luis Severino pitched well for the most part but gave up a first-inning home run to Dustin Pedroia and two subsequent shots to David Ortiz as Boston won on the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For long stretches\xa0on Sunday\xa0night, Yankees starter Luis Severino befuddled the Red Sox lineup. Whisking along with machine-like efficiency, Severino set an unusually brisk pace for a Yankees-Red Sox game at Yankee Stadium, affairs known to play out like Leo Tolstoy novels, especially when broadcast on national television.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/sports/09YANKEES1/09YANKEES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/09/sports/09YANKEES1/09YANKEES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/sports/09YANKEES1/09YANKEES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/sports/09YANKEES1/09YANKEES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/sports/09YANKEES1/09YANKEES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/09/sports/09YANKEES1/09YANKEES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/sports/09YANKEES1/09YANKEES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David Orti