 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lyft Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fingerprinting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-09T21:07:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike McPhate', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McPhate', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/950cdb48-0541-59c4-8e17-5c23e15ef2fd', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/950cdb48-0541-59c4-8e17-5c23e15ef2fd'}, {'abstract': 'Analyzing 16,000 comments on a fraternity culture website for insight into how fraternity brothers talk about women.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/09/is-sexist-rhetoric-a-total-frat-move/', 'snippet': 'Analyzing 16,000 comments on a fraternity culture website for insight into how fraternity brothers talk about women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the gender-segregated world of college fraternities, sexist rhetoric isn’t exactly astonishing. There are numerous allegations of sexism against\xa0fraternities, and studies show men who join are\xa0far more likely\xa0to\xa0commit assault\xa0after joining even when controlling for factors like prior history of assault and alcohol use. This makes you wonder just how fraternity men talk about women.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/opinion/9kristof_blog/9kristof_blog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,