tings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thevenin, Edson A (d 2016)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Troy (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'French, Randall C (1981- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelove, Joel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'District Attorneys', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rensselaer County (NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T01:10:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0de5fae-79a1-5fb4-a0a2-c1431949ce10', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0de5fae-79a1-5fb4-a0a2-c1431949ce10'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Tuesday, May 10, 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/10/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Tuesday, May 10, 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We see you. We stand with you. We will do everything we can to protect you going forward.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T01:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2bdc792-8d20-5bf3-aacd-01b55e419ee1', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2bdc792-8d20-5bf3-aacd-01b55e419ee1'}, {'abstract': 'Jane just wants to give Mateo a nice party for his first birthday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/09/arts/television/jane-the-virgin-season-2-episode-21-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Jane just wants to give Mateo a nice party for his first birthday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the next to last episode of this season, “Chapter 43” has a lot of work to do. And, because this is “Jane the Virgin,” there are a lot of loose ends to tie up: Jane’s coming wedding, Derek’s blackmail attempt on Rafael, Petra’s evil twin, etc. Before any of that, however, there is the adorable matter of Mateo’s first birthday. A child’s first birthday is more for the parents and family than it is for the child. Mateo won’t remember any of the details, but that doesn’t stop Jane from wanting to have the perfect entertainer for the party. She settles on Bobby, the Beyoncé of kid performers, but that plan falls through because nothing is ever easy on “Jane the Virgin.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/arts/television/09JANE/10JANE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/09/arts/television/09JANE/10JANE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/arts/television/09JANE/10JANE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/arts/television/09JANE/10JANE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/arts/television/09JANE/09JANE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/09/arts/television/09JANE/09JANE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/arts/television/09JANE/09JANE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jane the Virgin’ Season 2, Episode 21: Birthday Party Woes', 'kicker': 'Jane the Virgin', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Jane the Virgin (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T02:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilot Viruet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viruet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/061ff2bd-817d-5ac2-8da0-b38ec609317f', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/061ff2bd-817d-5ac2-8da0-b38ec609317f'}, {'abstract': 'David Kwong flies back in for a visit.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/09/best-picture/', 'snippet': 'David Kwong flies back in for a visit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY PUZZLE — If you can hear me over all of the chirping, I’d like to say that today’s puzzle by David Kwong is a great example of a theme that seems easy on the first pass, but which has additional gifts for the solver after the puzzle is completed. For me, the best gift of all was the fact that this theme is a tribute to “BIRDMAN,” my favorite movie of 2014. If you haven’t seen it, please give it a try. Not only is the acting and the storytelling extraordinary, but the award-winning techniques used in filming were amazing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Best Picture', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T02:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf6ab46-13fe-54df-bd3f-6dab357fb513', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf6ab46-13fe-54df-bd3f-6dab357fb513'}, {'abstract': 'Federal officials at a public meeting in the West Village heard from members of the public who spoke in favor of national recognition near the tavern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/10/nyregion/dozens-testify-in-support-of-monument-to-gay-rights-near-stonewall-inn.html', 'snippet': 'Federal officials at a public meeting in the West Village heard from members of the public who spoke in favor of national recognition near the tavern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day as Gil Horowitz, 80, passes by the Stonewall Inn near his home in the West Village, he is transported back to the early morning hours of June 28, 1969. He was in his early 30s then, a bisexual man still living largely in the shadows, when, he said, he was arrested by a police officer as part of a protest outside the bar and taken to the Sixth Precinct station house. Overnight in jail, he said, he witnessed dozens of lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender people chained to radiators and beaten with nightsticks.', 'print