er': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a960cc54-13d4-5c36-a288-a16f1ad1cc03', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a960cc54-13d4-5c36-a288-a16f1ad1cc03'}, {'abstract': 'It’s naïve to think that leaving a relationship or signing a peace treaty will result in a fresh start.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/10/opinion/of-dating-and-diplomacy.html', 'snippet': 'It’s naïve to think that leaving a relationship or signing a peace treaty will result in a fresh start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, while I was boarding a plane to Europe, a close friend called to tell me she had just walked out on her life partner of more than 25 years. My heart dropped. I was headed to a secluded location to conduct a negotiation training for Israeli and Palestinian diplomats, and I didn’t have much time to talk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Of Dating and Diplomacy', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel L. Shapiro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Shapiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd5d9bb7-7776-5a54-bb61-da0b4ef107a4', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd5d9bb7-7776-5a54-bb61-da0b4ef107a4'}, {'abstract': 'He is an equal opportunity bully, and it wins him fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/10/opinion/campaign-stops/the-women-who-like-donald-trump.html', 'snippet': 'He is an equal opportunity bully, and it wins him fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Women don’t like Donald J. Trump. Or at least that’s what hacks in the news media like myself say, right? But don’t take it from me. Take it from female voters themselves. A CNN/ORC poll conducted in March found that 73 percent of women from both parties say they don’t like him, an increase from 59 percent in December. Among Republican women, this number is much lower but still significant: 39 percent said they had a negative view of him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/opinion/10rollerWeb/10rollerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/10/opinion/10rollerWeb/10rollerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/opinion/10rollerWeb/10rollerWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/opinion/10rollerWeb/10rollerWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/opinion/10rollerWeb/10rollerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/10/opinion/10rollerWeb/10rollerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': Non