-8348-f9815a0c2e9c'}, {'abstract': 'The Hallett Nature Sanctuary, a four-acre peninsula, had been mostly closed to the public since the 1930s, left to migrating birds and invasive plants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/nyregion/a-secret-section-of-central-park-reopens.html', 'snippet': 'The Hallett Nature Sanctuary, a four-acre peninsula, had been mostly closed to the public since the 1930s, left to migrating birds and invasive plants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the days when Fiorello H. La Guardia was mayor and Franklin D. Roosevelt was president, it has been a well-kept secret of New York City — to people, if not to migrating birds, the occasional wandering coyote and annoying, invasive plants like wisteria: a four-acre peninsula in Central Park that the groundskeepers did not bother with and that was off limits to the public.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/nyregion/09CENTRALPARK2/09CENTRALPARK2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/08/nyregion/09CENTRALPARK2/09CENTRALPARK2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/nyregion/09CENTRALPARK2/09CENTRALPARK2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/nyregion/09CENTRALPARK2/09CENTRALPARK2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/08/nyregion/09CENTRALPARK2/09CENTRALPARK2