ial race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANILA — As mayor of Davao City in the southern Philippines, Rodrigo Duterte sometimes drove a taxi at night, to see firsthand what was happening in his city. On other occasions, when his car got stuck in a traffic jam, he would jump out and try to untangle the mess personally, according to Luzviminda Ilagan, a former member of Davao’s city council.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodrigo Duterte’s Rivals Concede in Philippine Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, State Legislature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duterte, Rodrigo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manila (Philippines)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T10:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard C. Paddock and Floyd Whaley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Paddock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Whaley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3de4a15c-7a55-5210-8710-b1a1f33e7409', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3de4a15c-7a55-5210-8710-b1a1f33e7409'}, {'abstract': 'Hedge Fund Chiefs Cashed In Despite Choppy Waters in 2015 | Lending Club Stumbles and the Industry Faces Skepticism', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/10/morning-agenda-donald-trumps-contradictory-pick-for-fund-raiser/', 'snippet': 'Hedge Fund Chiefs Cashed In Despite Choppy Waters in 2015 |