ne, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/travel/15UPDATE/15UPDATE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/travel/15UPDATE/15UPDATE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/travel/15UPDATE/15UPDATE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Go in Europe, and How to Stay Safe', 'kicker': 'Update', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where to Go in Europe, and How to Stay Safe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brussels (Belgium)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T10:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/206f7031-5359-58b4-b2d6-9b2bbc723286', 'word_count': 1329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/206f7031-5359-58b4-b2d6-9b2bbc723286'}, {'abstract': 'Venture capitalists still deny they’re in a bubble. But the signs — and the potential consequences — are becoming harder to ignore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/magazine/bubble-indemnity.html', 'snippet': 'Venture capitalists still deny they’re in a bubble. But the signs — and the potential consequences — are becoming harder to ignore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Silicon Valley venture capitalists get themselves into image trouble, it’s usually because they’ve been too candid with their low estimate of other people’s intelligence. For example, after India recently prevented Facebook from offering free Internet service there, Marc Andreessen suggested in a tweet that the subcontinent might be better off had it remained under colonial administration. It’s much less common for V.C.s to soil their own nests in public. So it came as something of a surprise when Chamath Palihapitiya — Sri Lankan war refugee, early Facebook employee, investor in Slack and Box, part owner of the Golden State Warriors — told Vanity Fair in March that if we are in fact in the early stages of a second tech collapse, venture capitalists have only their own mediocre, clubby selves to blame. They should, he said, “focus on using capital as a way to take really big bets on things that just seem totally audacious. Right now we haven’t done enough of that, and the result is that most of the things we’ve funded are mostly crap and largely worthless.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15onmoney1/15mag-15onmoney-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15onmoney1/15mag-15onmoney-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 570}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15onmoney1/15mag-15onmoney-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15onmoney1/15mag-15onmoney-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1483, 'width': 1561, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15onmoney1/15mag-15onmoney-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15onmoney1/15mag-15onmoney-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15onmoney1/15mag-15onmoney-t_CA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bubble Indemnity', 'kicker': 'On Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bubble Indemnity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis-Kraus, Gideon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appraisals and Valuation (Property)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T11:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gideon Lewis-Kraus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gideon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis-Kraus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ef4fb56-427d-5eca-abaa-41b4199cf4d6', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ef4fb56-427d-5eca-abaa-41b4199cf4d6'}, {'abstract': 'The digital self-portraits we choose on various platforms are a window on ourselves and our intentions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/magazine/what-do-our-online-avatars-reveal-about-us.html', 'snippet': 'The digital self-portraits we choose on various platforms are a window on ourselves and our intentions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every time I send an email, I see myself staring back at me. I always have a slight, knowing smile on my face, even if the content of my email is confused, distressed or brimming with unrestrained glee. I chose the image (maybe unconsciously) because it seemed professional and direct, and also because my hair looked good. Smug email me is not my only online incarnation. There are dozens more of my avatars scattered across the web.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 566}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 966, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15firstwords/15mag-15firstwords-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1590, 'sub