lag a very considerable number of air bases in this important sector, which will soon be reorganized in the new field of totalitarian economy.’’\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, May 11, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1941: Italy Annexes Three Greek Isles', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyclades Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T14:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ffe02f8-7f55-5443-846b-e88ca9534d39', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ffe02f8-7f55-5443-846b-e88ca9534d39'}, {'abstract': 'Human Rights Watch says the guards killed five refugees and wounded 14 others as they tried to cross the border. Turkey denied the accusation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/world/europe/turkey-syria-immigrants-human-rights-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Human Rights Watch says the guards killed five refugees and wounded 14 others as they tried to cross the border. Turkey denied the accusation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — Turkish border guards have killed or injured more than a dozen Syrian refugees as they tried to cross into Turkey, Human Rights Watch said in a report issued on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/world/11Turke