ty of time to assess their options.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/05/10/ted-cruz-declines-to-support-donald-trump-and-muses-about-re-entering-race/', 'snippet': 'In his first interview since leaving the Republican presidential race last week, Senator Ted Cruz of Texas declined to throw his support behind Donald J. Trump, suggesting that he and other conservatives had plenty of time to assess their options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his first interview since leaving the Republican presidential race last week, Senator Ted Cruz of Texas declined on Tuesday to throw his support behind Donald J. Trump, suggesting that he and other conservatives had plenty of time to assess their options.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/us/10firstdraft-cruz2/10firstdraft-cruz2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/10/us/10firstdraft-cruz2/10firstdraft-cruz2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/us/10firstdraft-cruz2/10firstdraft-cruz2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/us/10firstdraft-cruz2/10firstdraft-cruz2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/us/10firstdraft-cruz2/10firstdraft-cruz2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/10/us/10firstdraft-cruz2/10firstdraft-cruz2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/10/us/10firstdraft-cruz2/10firstdraft-cruz2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ted Cruz Muses About Re-entering Race', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Endorsements; Cruz Says He Will Wait to Decide on Backing Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T17:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e1a3f03-6248-59fd-bb20-f3ae8fe4dc5e', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e1a3f03-6248-59fd-bb20-f3ae8fe4dc5e'}, {'abstract': 'Also, the sprawling Union Fare moves into a former Barnes & Noble, Passage Irish Bar and Kitchen comes to Astoria, Queens, and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/dining/restaurants-suvir-saran-tapestry.html', 'snippet': 'Also, the sprawling Union Fare moves into a former Barnes & Noble, Passage Irish Bar and Kitchen comes to Astoria, Queens, and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tapestry After the Indian chef Suvir Saran left the elegant Union Square restaurant Devi in 2012, he moved to San Francisco to open American Masala, inspired by the cross-cultural recipes in his book of the same name. But the sprawling 400-seat restaurant never opened. “It was a lucky thing,” Mr. Saran said. “It was difficult to fill all those seats. San Francisco is dead after 9 p.m.” So he is back in New York, in partnership with Roni Mazumdar, an entrepreneur in art and entertainment who owns MasalaWala restaurants with his father. Joel Corona, a former private chef in California, and Aarti Mehta are chefs de cuisine. The white brick restaurant, with a swath of white quartz bar and polished woodwork, is hung with pieces by Indian artists. Mr. Saran’s food is a mix of Mexican, North African, French and Italian, all liberally exploiting the Indian spice cabinet. “When you think about it, Mexico and India both have a lot of cumin in common,” Mr. Saran said. Some ingredients, including pork and eggs, come from his upstate farm. (Opens Friday): 60 Greenwich Avenue (Perry Street), 212-373-8900, tapestryrestaurant.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/dining/11OFF/11OFF-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/11/dining/11OFF/11OFF-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/dining/11OFF/11OFF-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/dining/11OFF/11OFF-super