ration of this 1930 musical revue starring the bandleader Paul Whiteman is thought by some to be among the most expensive ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A significant movie restoration not only can return a film’s patina of newness but its place in film history as well. That may be the case when the musical revue “King of Jazz” (1930), brought back to something of its original splendor, emerges from the vaults in the soft, shimmering red and green tones of early Technicolor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11RESTORATION1/11RESTORATION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11RESTORATION1/11RESTORATION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 469}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11RESTORATION1/11RESTORATION1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11RESTORATION1/11RESTORATION1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 908, 'width': 1161, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11RESTORATION1/11RESTORATION1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11RESTORATION1/11RESTORATION1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11RESTORATION1/11RESTORATION1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘King of Jazz’ Is Back, Burnished for Movie Fans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘King of Jazz’ Is Back, Burnished for a New Generation of Movie Fans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, John Murray (1886-1954)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whiteman, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'King of Jazz (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T21:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Hoberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbe559b8-2fbe-525a-9830-0e53566cc028', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbe559b8-2fbe-525a-9830-0e53566cc028'}, {'abstract': 'Margaret de Heinrich de Omorovicza shares her warm-weather tips for glowing skin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/10/t-magazine/omorovicza-beauty-advice.html', 'snippet': 'Margaret de Heinrich de Omorovicza shares her warm-weather tips for glowing skin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent, particularly busy weeknight on Bergdorf Goodman’s Beauty Level, I stood at the Omorovicza counter as shoppers swarmed around me. A woman approached briefly to ask about the line — “I’ve never heard of it” — but otherwise, I had the products to myself. Weeks later, when I talked on the phone with Margaret de Heinrich de Omorovicza, who co-founded the Budapest-based brand with her husband 10 years ago this summer, even she admitted that Omorovicza is not that well-known in America — which is surprising, given that it essentially epitomizes the inspired-by-nature-yet-super-luxe stuff beauty dreams are made of these days.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/09tmag-omorovicza-01/09tmag-omorovicza-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/09tmag-omorovicza-01/09tmag-omorovicza-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/09tmag-omorovicza-01/09tmag-omorovicza-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/09tmag-omorovicza-01/09tmag-omorovicza-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/09tmag-omorovicza-01/09tmag-omorovicza-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/09tmag-omorovicza-01/09tmag-omorovicza-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/09tmag-omorovicza-01/09tmag-omorovicza-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Skincare Advice From a Budapest-Based Beauty Founder', 'kicker': 'On Beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Hungarian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T21:21:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c9cb64d-7495-5c6b-be43-d32bf0f81472', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c9cb64d-7495-5c6b-be43-d32bf0f81472'}, {'abstract': 'This Frederick Ashton work at the Metropolitan Opera House features a heroine who is multifaceted and modern, even though the plot is set in antiquity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/arts/dance/review-american-ballet-theaters-sylvia-is-a-rich-harmony.html', 'snippet': 'This Frederick Ashton work at the Metropolitan Opera House features a heroine who is multifaceted and modern, even though the plot is set in antiquity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Ballet Theater, the only dance company to appear at the Metropolitan Opera House these days, is taking admirable box-office risks this spring, the kind that come from core beliefs. Traditionally, the company’s seasons at the huge Met, impelled by the need to be popular, have relied overmuch on guest stars and full-length war horses that are mostly from the 19th century and too often artistically thin. But the eight-week season that the troupe opened on Monday with Frederick Ashton’s three-act “Sylvia” is the most enterprising it has offered in decades. It brings new hope to Lincoln Center and to ballet. It also shows Ballet Theater as a true company.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11SYLVIA/11SYLVIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11SYLVIA/11SYLVIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 580}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11SYLVIA/11SYLVIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 991, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11SYLVIA/11SYLVIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1981, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11SYLVIA/11SYLVIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11SYLVIA/11SYLVIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11SYLVIA/11SYLVIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: American Ballet Theater’s ‘Sylvia’ Is a Rich Harmony', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harmony, With a Heroine at the Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashton, Frederick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sylvia (Ballet)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T21:23:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/075d5289-e6e7-5f7e-8773-943c10645996', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/075d5289-e6e7-5f7e-8773-943c10645996'}, {'abstract': 'The jazz composer-arranger shows no sign of creative fatigue, having just released a ravishing album and planning another due in October.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/arts/music/carla-bley-still-improvising-and-inspiring-as-she-turns-80.html', 'snippet': 'The jazz composer-arranger shows no sign of creative fatigue, having just released a ravishing album and planning another due in October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WILLOW, N.Y. — The narrow study where Carla Bley does her composing, upstairs in her rustic-modern house here, was the picture of tidy efficiency one recent afternoon. Handwritten sheet music covered a writing stand and the rack of an upright piano. A blank legal pad sat on a desk. Bookshelves held scores in labeled folders: “Healing Power.” “Liver of Life.” “Ups and Downs.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11BLEY/11BLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2