is the focal point of this Rodrigo Plá film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mounting frustrations of Sonia Bonet (Jana Raluy), a middle-aged Mexican woman with a gravely ill husband, as she navigates the impenetrable bureaucracy of an insurance company in “A Monster With a Thousand Heads” add up to a nightmare of bureaucratic stonewalling. Sonia is determined to secure her dying husband, Guillermo, an expensive pain medication to which he’s entitled but that the company is reluctant to provide. Her struggle is an enraging depiction of the plight of an individual fighting a corrupt, greedy system.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11MONSTER/11MONSTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11MONSTER/11MONSTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11MONSTER/11MONSTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11MONSTER/11MONSTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11MONSTER/11MONSTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11MONSTER/11MONSTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/arts/11MONSTER/11MONSTER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Health Care Bureaucracy Runs Amok in ‘A Monster With a Thousand Heads’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'And You Thought You Were Fed Up With Health Care Bureaucracy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pla, Rodrigo (1968- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Monster With a Thousand Heads (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-10T21:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cc977a9-bb27-5334-bd10-fcd976af657d', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cc977a9-bb27-5334-bd10-fcd976af657d'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Cooper, the English pianist, played Schumann’s “Ghost” Variations and other works in a recital at the Frick Collection that gradually grew more assured.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/arts/music/review-imogen-cooper-grappling-with-schumanns-ghosts.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Cooper, the English pianist, played Schumann’s “Ghost” Variations and other works in a recital at the Frick Collection that gradually grew more assured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The English pianist Imogen Cooper is a valued performer of wide experience. But on Sunday afternoon, she seemed to have difficulty adjusting to the small concert space of the Frick Collection and the Steinway piano that occupied it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mu