: 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0a59d4a-83b6-5f54-91bf-76d290116515', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0a59d4a-83b6-5f54-91bf-76d290116515'}, {'abstract': 'Sheri G. Lederman alleged that the growth score portion of the evaluation system was biased against teachers whose students were consistently high scorers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/nyregion/court-vacates-long-island-teachers-evaluation-tied-to-student-test-scores.html', 'snippet': 'Sheri G. Lederman alleged that the growth score portion of the evaluation system was biased against teachers whose students were consistently high scorers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A New York State court on Tuesday threw out a teacher’s evaluation for the 2013-14 school year, based on a controversial state rating system, saying that it had been “arbitrary and capricious.” But the court stopped short of ruling on the evaluation system more broadly because the state has already begun replacing it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Vacates Long Island Teacher’s Evaluation Tied to Test Scores', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Throws Out Long Island Teacher’s Evaluation Linked to Test Scores', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T00:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'n