iers customers could choose from.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/sports/espn-and-verizon-settle-lawsuit-over-cable-package.html', 'snippet': 'ESPN filed suit last April after Verizon moved some channels off Fios’s basic cable offering and separated them into tiers customers could choose from.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ESPN and Verizon announced Tuesday the settlement of a lawsuit that accused Verizon of breaching its contract with the sports network when it created a new cable package for its Fios television service last year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ESPN and Verizon Settle Lawsuit Over Cable Package', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ESPN Settles Suit Over Bundling by Verizon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T01:06:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd2f484a-d34f-579e-8891-98e4968d5d22', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd2f484a-d34f-579e-8891-98e4968d5d22'}, {'abstract': 'Most people in Japan believe the city was a victim of unnecessary brutality, but for Americans of the World War II generation, Hiroshima is at the center of a very different narrative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/world/asia/hiroshima-atomic-bomb.html', 'snippet': 'Most people in Japan believe the city was a victim of unnecessary brutality, but for Americans of the World War II generation, Hiroshima is at the center of a very different narrative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For decades, visitors to the ghostly dome in Hiroshima that stands like a sole survivor from the dropping of the atomic bomb there more than 70 years ago entered a world that mixed unspeakable tragedy with historical amnesia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/world/11hiroshimaessay-web/11hiroshimaessay-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/11/world/11hiroshimaessay-web/11hiroshimaessay-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/world/11hiroshimaessay-web/11hiroshimaessay-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/world/11hiroshimaessay-web/11hiroshimaessay-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1395, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/11/world/11hiroshimaessay-web/11hiroshimaessay-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/11/world/11hiroshimaessay-web/11hiroshimaessay-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':