heir picks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/theater/tony-award-winner-predictions.html', 'snippet': 'Ben Brantley and Charles Isherwood of The Times make their picks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Brantley and Charles Isherwood, the theater critics for The New York Times, make their Tony Award choices. For the Should Have Been Nominated category, the critics were allowed to expand the potential nominees to Off Broadway productions, which are ineligible for the Tonys.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tony Awards: Who Will Win (and Who Should)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Tony Awards: Who Will Win (and Who Should Win)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T10:55:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley and Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9a544d4-856b-5644-afc7-4ebae8c1c928', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9a544d4-856b-5644-afc7-4ebae8c1c928'}, {'abstract': 'Think of them not as cartographic abstractions, but as incredibly affordable Pollocks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-usgs-topographical-maps.html', 'snippet': 'Think of them not as cartographic abstractions, but as incredibly affordable Pollocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the close of the Second World War, the United States government embarked on an enormous artistic enterprise. It is estimated to have cost nearly $3 billion and, at its height, employed more than 2,000 people. I am talking about the topographic mapping program of the United States Geological Survey. It was an opus of Whitmanesque proportion, a heroic rendering of the American landscape; every last whorl and hachure and dotted line of actual topography — not to mention the name of every last desert wash, old mine or glorified goat track — was exhaustively cataloged. This 54,000-tile mosaic was not, of course, done in the cause of aesthetics, but it nevertheless represents as gorgeous and complete a depiction of the country as any ever made.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15lor-copy/15mag-15lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15lor-copy/15mag-15lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15lor-copy/15mag-15lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15lor-copy/15mag-15lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15lor-copy/15mag-15lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15lor-copy/15mag-15lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15lor-copy/15mag-15lor-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: U.S.G.S. Topographical Maps', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S.G.S. Topographical Maps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vanderbilt, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smithson, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Geological Survey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Vanderbilt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vanderbilt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b7e10fd-1ea0-5a9c-977c-ac3350bccdc9', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b7e10fd-1ea0-5a9c-977c-ac3350bccdc9'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on the implications of wanting only a purebred and whether a child should always be told who his biological father is.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/magazine/is-it-ok-to-get-a-dog-from-a-breeder-not-a-shelter.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on the implications of wanting only a purebred and whether a child should always be told who his biological father is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I got my wonderful, loving dog from a reputable breeder about eight years ago, but sometimes I feel guilty that I didn’t adopt a shelter dog instead. When I consider that her life span is already more than half over, I suspect that I will eventually get another dog. When I do, I’m sure I will go to a breeder again. (I won’t get into the reasons for this, although there are many.) Is this ethical? Is it relevant that I have taken in strays in the past and given them a loving home for the rest of their lives? Is it relevant that I have never abandoned or failed to neuter or spay a pet? Is it relevant that, given a choice between a shelter dog and no dog, I would choose no dog at all? What if I give money to shelters for neutering stray dogs? What if I give money for education to prevent people from adopting puppies without properly training or socializing them, thus preventing those dogs from ending up in shelters? How much money must I give to justify getting a dog from a breeder? Or should breeders donate a certain amount for each puppy sold either to shelters or to education programs? Is such a trade-off ethical? Name Withheld', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 417, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 417, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It O.K. to Get a Dog From a Breeder, Not a Shelter?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is It O.K. to Get a Dog From a Breeder, Not a Shelter?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cameroon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ghana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ca9fe43-a193-5dcd-9128-6fb10c878dd4', 'word_count': 1337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ca9fe43-a193-5dcd-9128-6fb10c878dd4'}, {'abstract': 'The hip-hop producer and record-label executive talks about his keys to success, relaxing in his garden and staying moisturized.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/magazine/dj-khaled-is-extra-careful-around-beyonce.html', 'snippet': 'The hip-hop producer and record-label executive talks about his keys to success, relaxing in his garden and staying moisturized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’re a prolific hip-hop multihyphenate: producer, radio host and record-label executive. But you also make your own albums, and it seems as if one of your many gifts is persuading other rappers to appear on your albums. How does that work? I put the right people in the room together to make magic. Basically, I’m one of the greatest producers ever. And I’m also one of the greatest D.J.s ever. And I’m also one of the best executives ever.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '82', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15talk/15mag-15talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 998, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15talk/15mag-15talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 998}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15talk/15mag-15talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 616, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15talk/15mag-15talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1202, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/