count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73600c8c-3f10-5a95-a5e8-ed5a25021d05'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The European Economic Community reaches broad accord on economic union in 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/1966-eec-agrees-on-economy-union/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The European Economic Community reaches broad accord on economic union in 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The Common Market cleared a major hurdle today [May 11] when the six member states reached a package deal that will chart the completion of their economic union. The agreement settles the thorny issue of farm financing and sets July 1, 1968 as the date when all goods will circulate duty-free within the European Economic Community, the official name for the Common Market. The deal was hailed here as the biggest step forward taken by the EEC in the last three years. It was reached at 4:30 a.m. after 17 hours of nonstop negotiations.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, May 12, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: EEC Agrees on Economy Union', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brussels (Belgium)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T14:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5335dd20-ad06-5e5d-a4a9-c6b90e7029dc', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'n