 'WASHINGTON — The director of the F.B.I. reignited the factious debate over a so-called “Ferguson effect” on Wednesday, saying that he believed less aggressive policing was driving an alarming spike in murders in many cities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/us/12fbi-web/12fbi-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/12/us/12fbi-web/12fbi-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/us/12fbi-web/12fbi-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/us/12fbi-web/12fbi-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/us/12fbi-web/12fbi-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/12/us/12fbi-web/12fbi-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/us/12fbi-web/12fbi-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'F.B.I. Director Says ‘Viral Video Effect’ Blunts Police Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.B.I Director Says ‘Viral Video Effect’ Is Leading to Less Aggressive Policing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T19:41:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lichtblau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lichtblau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/761a62e7-a71f-54c6-a3b2-9b1f61cd6fd3', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/761a62e7-a71f-54c6-a3b2-9b1f61cd6fd3'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Wilson collaborated with the fashion house on “Here Elsewhere,” an immersive installation filling five themed rooms in Chelsea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/11/t-magazine/art/hermes-robert-wilson-here-elsewhere.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Wilson collaborated with the fashion house on “Here Elsewhere,” an immersive installation filling five themed rooms in Chelsea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The theater and visual artist Robert Wilson, fondly regarded as a master of light and shadow, strikes again this week in New York — in an unexpected location. Hermès tapped him to create a surreal universe for its 2016 Maison furniture and housewares collection, which over the next two days will be installed at Cedar Lake’s space in the Chelsea arts district of New York. Titled “Here Elsewhere,” the immersive installation eschews any of the expected notions of a “dream house,” evoking instead the emotional, dizzying, heady visions of a dream itself. “It is an abstract time/space construction. What we hear, see and smell can counterpoint and complement one another,” Wilson says. “Without light, there is no space. Einstein said, ‘Light is the measure of all things.’”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Visionary Artist Creates a Surreal Universe for Hermès', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T19:50:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a83d556c-0d03-52f9-844b-8b99df181a76', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a83d556c-0d03-52f9-844b-8b99df181a76'}, {'abstract': 'The law, opposed by the Vatican, stops short of gay marriage but brings Italy more in line with other Western European countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/12/world/europe/italy-gay-same-sex-unions.html', 'snippet': 'The law, opposed by the Vatican, stops short of gay marriage but brings Italy more in line with other Western European countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — After decades of struggle by gay rights groups, and months of contested political negotiations, the Italian Parliament on Wednesday evening gave final approval to a law recognizing civil unions of same-sex couples.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy Approves S