dge, Brooklyn, was damaged after one season, and some have criticized it for being poorly designed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is not exactly accurate to say no one uses the $1.1 million public dock that was installed off the shoreline of Bay Ridge, Brooklyn, two and a half years ago. It was praised by city officials for the access it would give local residents to the shore and for the resiliency of its construction, but it closed after one season when the gangway snapped off and was never repaired. Then the pilings holding it to the bay floor started bending. Today, it sits more than seven miles away in Sheepshead Bay, where it was towed for storage, lashed to a bulkhead and kept behind a gate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/nyregion/12ECODOCK/12ECODOCK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/12/nyregion/12ECODOCK/12ECODOCK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/nyregion/12ECODOCK/12ECODOCK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/nyregion/12ECODOCK/12ECODOCK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/nyregion/12ECODOCK/12ECODOCK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/12/nyregion/12ECODOCK/12ECODOCK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/nyregion/12ECODOCK/12ECODOCK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '$1.1 Million Brooklyn Dock, Built for Public Use, Sits in Storage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Damaged After One Season, a Public Dock in Brooklyn Is Now Used Only by Birds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nir, Sarah Maslin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bay Ridge (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sheepshead Bay (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coastal Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-11T23:58:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f9dd548-b850-5a64-974a-629b0df59811', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f9dd548-b850-5a64-974a-629b0df59811'}, {'abstract': 'The blood-testing company, which is under criminal investigation, is replacing its chief operating officer and expanding its board.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/12/business/embattled-blood-lab-theranos-makes-a-bid-to-regain-confidence.html', 'snippet': 'The blood-testing company, which is under criminal investigation, is replacing its chief operating officer and expand