': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76c07736-d8ad-5511-9e1a-2bf83663bdfb'}, {'abstract': 'News and updates from around the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/12/us/national-briefing.html', 'snippet': 'News and updates from around the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Doug Ducey on Wednesday signed into law a bill asserting Arizona’s ownership over a herd of horses that roams the banks of the Salt River in the Tonto National Forest northeast of Phoenix. The bill also criminalized the unauthorized killing of the horses, which Mr. Ducey described in a statement as “beautiful, majestic and a treasure to our state.” The horses came under threat last year when federal officials announced their imminent capture, in part because of the risk of accident they could pose to drivers and passengers who go tubing in the river, a popular summer attraction. The new law also creates a private-public partnership to manage the herd, estimated at about 100 horses. FERNANDA SANTOS', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Couch, Ethan (1997- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-12T02:20:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {