one, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5f3cd68-520a-5af9-9bb6-8ecd72057d81', 'word_count': 3669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5f3cd68-520a-5af9-9bb6-8ecd72057d81'}, {'abstract': 'Most clinical trials for cancer drugs are failures. But for a handful of patients, a drug proves to be nearly a cure. What can science learn from these “exceptional responders”?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/magazine/exceptional-responders-cancer-the-lazarus-effect.html', 'snippet': 'Most clinical trials for cancer drugs are failures. But for a handful of patients, a drug proves to be nearly a cure. What can science learn from these “exceptional responders”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Grace Silva had experienced odd episodes with her throat — bouts of swelling and radiating pain that seemed to resolve with antibiotics — but her doctors couldn’t explain what was wrong. Finally, after a flare-up in the summer of 2010, Grace was referred to a specialist, an ear doctor who felt something amiss on the left side of her throat: a lump. The Silva family agreed that it was time to get Grace, then 54, to a thyroid specialist. Grace’s daughter Melanie tracked down the name of one at Brigham and Women’s Hospital, a 90-\xadminute drive from Grace’s brown clapboard split-\xadlevel near New Bedford, Mass. In September 2010, the specialist delivered the diagnosis: anaplastic thyroid cancer. It was bad, he warned her, and she would need surgery. Grace’s other daughter, Karrie, was marrying in a few weeks. “Can’t it wait?” Grace asked. It could not. “And whatever you do,” the specialist said, “please don’t look it up on the Internet.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '48', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15responders1/15responders1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15responders1/15responders1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 700}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15responders1/15responders1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 878, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15responders1/15responders1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1714, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15responders1/15mag-15responders-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15responders1/15mag-15responders-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15responders1/15mag-15responders-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Learning From the Lazarus Effect', 'kicker': 'The Health Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lazarus Effect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cook, Gareth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-12T09:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gareth Cook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gareth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cook', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad27ff83-e4b5-5ae9-8f75-2e53600314c4', 'word_count': 6120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad27ff83-e4b5-5ae9-8f75-2e53600314c4'}, {'abstract': 'President Maithripala Sirisena, chosen by a coalition because he was agreeable and self-effacing, is trying to forge a political solution that for decades has been out of reach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/13/world/asia/sri-lanka-maithripala-sirisena.html', 'snippet': 'President Maithripala Sirisena, chosen by a coalition because he was agreeable and self-effacing, is trying to forge a political solution that for decades has been out of reach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLOMBO, Sri Lanka — Leaders of Sri Lanka, an island nation at the foot of India, have repeatedly promised a political solution to the ethnic strife that has caused heartache and bloodshed for much of its nearly 70-year history since independence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/world/12LANKA-WEB/12LANKA-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/12/world/12LANKA-WEB/12LANKA-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/world/12LANKA-WEB/12LANKA-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/world/12LANKA-WEB/12