 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/d93cadfb-1c3c-5379-84f6-cf8cbc0e1d8c', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d93cadfb-1c3c-5379-84f6-cf8cbc0e1d8c'}, {'abstract': 'Roasting creates an edible tapestry, crisp and yielding all at once.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/magazine/kale-coconut-and-grace-in-a-salad.html', 'snippet': 'Roasting creates an edible tapestry, crisp and yielding all at once.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It looked like the makings of dinner at a yoga retreat. There was a sheet pan filled with cherry tomatoes, glistening with olive oil, dusted in lime zest, showered in salt and pepper. Beside it, another pan: a soy-drizzled mound of ripped kale and dried shaved coconut. There were the ingredients for a dressing as well: miso paste from Japan; tahini from the Levant; local honey; a knob of ginger; a bright red pepper. All of this was very beautiful. But I didn’t see how it was going to come together.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 