 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-12T13:59:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e51259c5-9233-503c-991e-2a3ef0179a83', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e51259c5-9233-503c-991e-2a3ef0179a83'}, {'abstract': 'The actress, nominated for a Tony for playing an office manager and mother from Scranton, Pa., knew from an early age that she wanted to be onstage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/theater/in-the-humans-jayne-houdyshell-embodies-mom.html', 'snippet': 'The actress, nominated for a Tony for playing an office manager and mother from Scranton, Pa., knew from an early age that she wanted to be onstage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her dressing room at the Helen Hayes Theater, Jayne Houdyshell keeps two pages from her diary enclosed in a silver frame. The entry, from April 1969, describes a high school production of “Blithe Spirit,” in which the 15-year-old Ms. Houdyshell played the elderly medium Madame Arcati. After a brief appraisal of the show (“I was completely satisfied with my performance”), the entry ends, in jubilant capitals, “OH I LOVE TO ACT. OH I LOVE THE THEATER.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15HOUDYSHELL/15HOUDYSHELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15HOUDYSHELL/15HOUDYSHELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 924}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15HOUDYSHELL/15HOUDYSHELL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 666, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15HOUDYSHELL/15HOUDYSHELL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1331, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15HOUDYSHELL/15HOUDYSHELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15HOUDYSHELL/15HOUDYSHELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15HOUDYSHELL/15HOUDYSHELL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In ‘The Humans,’ Jayne Houdyshell Embodies Mom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She’s Mom Onstage, and So Much More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houdyshell, Jayne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mantello, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Humans (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-12T14:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7da4d707-efad-5363-b5bd-6f99fdb98230', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7da4d707-efad-5363-b5bd-6f99fdb98230'}, {'abstract': 'In 1951, at the height of the polio epidemic, I knew about my limp before I knew much else about myself.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/12/learning-to-walk-in-my-60s/', 'snippet': 'In 1951, at the height of the polio epidemic, I knew about my limp before I knew much else about myself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I knew about my limp before I knew much else about myself. It was 1951, at the height of the polio epidemic, and I was a 4-year-old in Beverly Hills, Calif. My father took me swimming in the pool of a club where he played tennis. Sometime later, a woman who’d swum in the pool a week or two before me was stricken with polio. A few days after that, while we were on vacation, I began limping and developed a fever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/27/health/wellpolio/wellpolio-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/04/27/health/wellpolio/wellpolio-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/27/health/wellpolio/wellpolio-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr