b75-3ac0079f8cdd'}, {'abstract': 'A rash of protests over job losses stems from lax enforcement in a country purportedly ruled by law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/13/opinion/refusing-to-honor-labor-rights-backfires-on-china.html', 'snippet': 'A rash of protests over job losses stems from lax enforcement in a country purportedly ruled by law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Just before the Chinese New Year in February, the Stella Xing Ang shoe factory in Dongguan, China, became a casualty of the country’s economic slowdown. Declining orders and higher production costs meant that after 13 years of producing shoes for major international brands, the business would close, and 2,000 employees would lose their jobs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Refusing to Honor Labor Rights Backfires on China', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-12T15:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoffrey Crothall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crothall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d9522b1-6bb1-5ea3-814d-5aac641b12a9', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d9522b1-6bb1-5ea3-814d-5aac641b12a9'}, {'abstract': 'The social media network suspended an account on Thursday after private information about governmen