6-05-12T21:03:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fdbb889-af6c-5c6c-83e8-f92fb6d62e75', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fdbb889-af6c-5c6c-83e8-f92fb6d62e75'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Kigawa will play Ligeti’s complete Piano Études and the cellist Michael Nicolas will perform in a pop-up concert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/arts/music/taka-kigawa-ligeti-in-mind-returns-to-le-poisson-rouge.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Kigawa will play Ligeti’s complete Piano Études and the cellist Michael Nicolas will perform in a pop-up concert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pianist Taka Kigawa has demonstrated insightful musicianship and impressive stamina during myriad marathon performances at Le Poisson Rouge, including Pierre Boulez’s complete works for solo piano and Bach’s “The Art of Fugue.” On Monday, May 16, he tackles another major work: the 18 pieces of Ligeti’s complete Piano Études. Ligeti was inspired by Chopin, Liszt, Debussy, jazz and the complex polyphony of sub-Saharan African music while writing his series of rhythmically complicated and virtuosic character pieces. (7 p.m., lepoissonrouge.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 492}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1680, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE2/15GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taka Kigawa, Ligeti in Mind, Returns to Le Poisson Rouge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical: A Feast of Ligeti at Le Poisson Rouge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kigawa, Taka', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicolas, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miller Theater at Columbia University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-12T21:04:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a0f9c14-d5c1-5252-82c5-1b0a9e08ac4a', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a0f9c14-d5c1-5252-82c5-1b0a9e08ac4a'}, {'abstract': 'Three exhibitions in New Paltz showcase creations from the worlds of furniture, light and urban street life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/nyregion/dorsky-museum-highlights-works-that-elevate-the-mundane-into-art.html', 'snippet': 'Three exhibitions in New Paltz showcase creations from the worlds of furniture, light and urban street life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixty-nine small wooden spoons hang along a gallery wall near the entrance to the Samuel Dorsky Museum of Art. All hand carved from different types of wood and mounted on a narrow horizontal board, they include long-handled mixing spoons, two-sided ladles and a spoon so tiny its scoop is barely a quarter inch across.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE3/15ARTSWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE3/15ARTSWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE3/15ARTSWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 430, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE3/15ARTSWE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 859, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15A