pet': 'The director and co-writer of the film discusses a sequence featuring Colin Farrell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dark satire “The Lobster” imagines a world where single people are devalued. From the Greek director Yorgos Lanthimos (“Dogtooth”), the movie follows a recently divorced man who is sent to a resort where he must either find a mate or be turned into an animal. In this scene, the lead character, David, played by Colin Farrell, arrives at breakfast and must face the seating area of the happily coupled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yorgos Lanthimos Narrates a Scene From ‘The Lobster’', 'kicker': 'Anatomy of a Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lanthimos, Yorgos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farrell, Colin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Lobster (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-12T21:05:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79312435-4b97-535e-ac06-bd56e9557b43', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79312435-4b97-535e-ac06-bd56e9557b43'}, {'abstract': '“Spotlight on Screenwriting,” aims to honor the contributions of a group historically overlooked in Hollywood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/movies/the-academy-highlights-movie-screenwriters.html', 'snippet': '“Spotlight on Screenwriting,” aims to honor the contributions of a group historically overlooked in Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Historically, Hollywood has denied screenwriters their proper due, which the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences tries to rectify with “Spotlight on Screenwriting,” a series at Film Forum and the SVA Theater. It runs Sunday, May 15, and Monday, with “Hollywood’s Happiest Couple,” a program honoring the team of Billy Wilder (1906-2002) and Charles Brackett (1892-1969).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE7/15GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE7/15GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE7/15GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE7/15GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1452, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE7/15GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE7/15GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/arts/15GUIDE7/15GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Academy Highlights Movie Screenwriters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': 