'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SIMS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/27609920-4dd9-505d-943d-1efb3f21f4ca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/27609920-4dd9-505d-943d-1efb3f21f4ca'}, {'abstract': 'The Russians were accused of hosting a party to siphon off attendance for “Gaslight.” And a filmmaker fretted that United States entries depicted Americans as “acquisitive half-wits.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/13/movies/recalling-the-first-cannes-film-festival-as-a-cold-war-brewed-in-1946.html', 'snippet': 'The Russians were accused of hosting a party to siphon off attendance for “Gaslight.” And a filmmaker fretted that United States entries depicted Americans as “acquisitive half-wits.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The international film festival at Cannes meant to make its debut in September 1939. The French were sick of the Mussolini-tainted Venice festival and decided to invite the world to their own cinephile party. A short article in The New York Times that July said there would be a prize for best director, named for the French film pioneer Louis Lumière.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13FRIDAYFILE/13FRIDAYFILE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 464, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13FRIDAYFILE/13FRIDAYFILE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 464, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13FRIDAYFILE/13FRIDAYFILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13FRIDAYFILE/13FRIDAYFILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13FRIDAYFILE/13FRIDAYFILE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recalling the First Cannes Film Festival, as a Cold War Brewed in 1946', 'kicker': 'Friday File', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '70 Years Ago', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Mary Jo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-12T21:08:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Jo Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Jo', 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf9fff92-9b1c-5e34-951d-4ac064d9819d', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf9fff92-9b1c-5e34-951d-4ac064d9819d'}, {'abstract': 'Visitors to “Impressionism: American Gardens on Canvas” can admire paintings of peonies, roses and zinnias alongside the real, fragrant, living things.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/13/arts/design/at-new-york-botanical-garden-time-to-smell-the-impressionists-roses.html', 'snippet': 'Visitors to “Impressionism: American Gardens on Canvas” can admire paintings of peonies, roses and zinnias alongside the real, fragrant, living things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMERICAN IMPRESSIONISTS dabbed and flicked paint on their canvases to suggest spires of purplish blue hollyhocks and cascades of poppies. For its spring show, the New York Botanical Garden has lined a gallery with about 20 artworks produced around 1900 and filled a conservatory corridor with the kinds of living plants that appeared in the paintings. The effect of the two-part exhibition “Impressionism: American Gardens on Canvas,” which opens on Saturday, is as jolting as the moment in any show — “Sunday in the Park With George,” for instance — when portrait subjects come to life.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13NYBGJP5/13NYBGJP5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13NYBGJP5/13NYBGJP5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13NYBGJP5/13NYBGJP5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13NYBGJP5/13NYBGJP5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13NYBGJP5/13NYBGJP5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/13/arts/13NYBGJP5/13NYBGJP5-thumbStandard