ction': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'States Move Toward Treating 17-Year-Old Offenders as Juveniles, Not Adults', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moving Away From Treating 17-Year-Old Offenders as Adults', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-13T12:07:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a14d92-8c74-51fe-bcd8-5b75a6014616', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a14d92-8c74-51fe-bcd8-5b75a6014616'}, {'abstract': 'Archaeologists are excavating the grounds of the home where the poet lived in hopes of restoring her botanical treasures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/17/science/emily-dickinson-lost-gardens.html', 'snippet': 'Archaeologists are excavating the grounds of the home where the poet lived in hopes of restoring her botanical treasures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That orchard was real: a medley of apple, pear, plum and cherry trees tended by the Dickinson family during their lifetimes. Over the decades, subsequent owners of the Dickinson house, known as the Homestead, removed the orchard, replaced extensive flower and vegetable gardens with lawn, and even installed a tennis court; and a devastating hurricane in 1938 damaged the grounds.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/science/12DICKINSON/12DICKINSON-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/12/science/12DICKINSON/12DICKINSON-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 304}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/science/12DICKINSON/12DICKINSON-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 519, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/science/12DICKINSON/12DICKINSON-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1037, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/science/12DICKINSON/12DICKINSON-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/12/science/12DICKINSON/12DICKINSON-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/12/science/12DICKINSON/12DICKINSON-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lost Gardens of Emily Di