humanity,’’ according to reports in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Rudolf Hess, who fled Germany in a fantastic solo flight on Saturday and startled and puzzled the world by parachuting down in Scotland, came to Great Britain ‘‘to save humanity,’’ he was quoted today [May 13] as telling authorities at the military hospital in Glasgow to which he was taken as a prisoner, according to one agency report. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/blogs/14iht-retrospective-Hess/14iht-retrospective-Hess-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 526, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/blogs/14iht-retrospective-Hess/14iht-retrospective-Hess-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 526, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/blogs/14iht-retrospective-Hess/14iht-retrospective-Hess-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/14/blogs/14iht-retrospective-Hess/14iht-retrospective-Hess-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/blogs/14iht-retrospective-Hess/14iht-retrospective-Hess-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1941: Fugitive Nazi Talks To British', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's