tchens-was-shaky-in-his-atheism-new-book-suggests.html', 'snippet': 'A new book says the impious author of “God Is Not Great” might have been exploring faith before he died in 2011. Mr. Hitchens’s secular friends disagree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all that can transpire in a bedroom, nothing can be as titillating to the religious, or those of us who write about them, as a dying man’s conversion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/us/14beliefs-web1/14beliefs-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/13/us/14beliefs-web1/14beliefs-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/us/14beliefs-web1/14beliefs-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/us/14beliefs-web1/14beliefs-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/us/14beliefs-web1/14beliefs-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/13/us/14beliefs-web1/14beliefs-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/13/us/14beliefs-web1/14beliefs-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christopher Hitchens Was Shaky in His Atheism, New Book Suggests', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Famous Atheist’s Non-Faith Is Questioned in Friend’s Book', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchens, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atheism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Finish Line Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-13T16:28:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c9aaed7-28ee-55ba-af76-7b9a6e5d9348', 'word_count': 1178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c9aaed7-28ee-55ba-af76-7b9a6e5d9348'}, {'abstract': 'The series, which ran for just 11 episodes in 1990, is being released on DVD; watching it shows a series that was occasionally ahead of its time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/14/arts/television/how-cop-rock-called-the-tune-that-some-shows-still-dance-to.html', 'snippet': 'The series, which ran for just 11 episodes in 1990, is being released on DVD; watching it shows a series that was occasionally ahead of its time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The television industry in 1990 was facing problems much like those it confronts today. Viewers, especially younger ones, were turning away from network TV and toward new entertainment options: video games, VCRs, outliers like MTV. An anything-goes mind-set was in the air, as networks looked for something new and exciting. And so it was that for 11 infamous episodes that fall, ABC offered up a police drama in which criminals rapped, officers sang, and jurors announced their verdict by bursting into a rousing gospel tune.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14COPROCK1/14COPROCK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14COPROCK1/14COPROCK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14COPROCK1/14COPROCK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14COPROCK1/14COPROCK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14COPROCK1/14COPROCK1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14COPROCK1/14COPROCK1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14COPROCK1/14COPROCK1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legac