e in the Bronx.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dan Feig, 59, had just begun his early-morning rounds in the fish market when a man with a longshoreman’s hook sidled up and discreetly described a sweet shipment of sea bass.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15character/15character-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15character/15character-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15character/15character-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15character/15character-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15character/15character-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15character/15character-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15character/15character-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fish Market Fishmonger', 'kicker': 'Character Study', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Home in a World of Fish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feig, Daniel J (1956- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Fulton Fish Market Cooperative (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-13T19:14:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/273b9cae-d908-500a-ae26-7b3307bd40b8', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/273b9cae-d908-500a-ae26-7b3307bd40b8'}, {'abstract': 'An author of five books about the hotel industry, Mr. Turkel is a “progressive guy.” He recently picked up cooking and enjoys watching MSNBC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/nyregion/how-stanley-turkel-90-spends-his-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'An author of five books about the hotel industry, Mr. Turkel is a “progressive guy.” He recently picked up cooking and enjoys watching MSNBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hotel consultant and historian Stanley Turkel, 90, lives in a single-family home in Flushing, Queens, with walls that are covered with photos of his family, including his wife, Rima Sokoloff, a modern dancer and professor who died in 2014, his four children and his five grandchildren. Mr. Turkel, who grew up in the Bronx and graduated from New York University, served in the Army Air Force during World War II before becoming the general manager of the Drake Hotel, now demolished, on Park Avenue. He then traveled the world for the International Telephone and Telegraph Company, overseeing development and operations on behalf of the Sheraton Corporation during its global expansion. An avid collector and writer, Mr. Turkel recently donated 670 items to the Smithsonian’s new National Museum of African-American History and Culture, and has published five books on the hotel industry.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1-SUB/15ROUTINE1-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1-SUB/15ROUTINE1-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1-SUB/15ROUTINE1-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1-SUB/15ROUTINE1-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1-SUB/15ROUTINE1-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1-SUB/15ROUTINE1-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1-SUB/15ROUTINE1-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge'