re breathtaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even at a time when new scandals erupt with dismaying regularity in big-money sports, the revelations about Russia’s elaborate doping scheme at the Winter Olympics in Sochi in 2014 are breathtaking. In a plot straight out of a spy thriller, Russian antidoping experts and government agents worked through the night passing urine samples through a hole in the wall, replacing drug-tainted samples with clean ones taken months before from the same athletes and somehow replacing tamper-proof caps.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/14sat1/14sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/14sat1/14sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 785}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/14sat1/14sat1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/14sat1/14sat1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1143, 'width': 874, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/14sat1/14sat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/14sat1/14sat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/14sat1/14sat1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 1