'lead_paragraph': '”People compare the legislature to the ‘House of Cards,’ but I disagree. ‘House of Cards’ is actually more believable.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: May 15, 2016', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-05-15T00:46:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1bdfe55-7593-5113-aa79-4416455f8f56', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1bdfe55-7593-5113-aa79-4416455f8f56'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Dunn’s third novel, “Geek Love,” which revolves around a married couple who breed mutant children as sideshow freaks, has sold hundreds of thousands of copies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/books/katherine-dunn-author-of-geek-love-dies-at-70.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Dunn’s third novel, “Geek Love,” which revolves around a married couple who breed mutant children as sideshow freaks, has sold hundreds of thousands of copies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katherine Dunn began writing the comic novel “Geek Love” in the late 1970s after her young son refused to join her on a stroll through the famous hybrid rose garden in Portland, Ore. Inspired by the diverse blooms there, Ms. Dunn wondered, What if she could have bred a more obedient boy?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14dunn-obit-1/14dunn-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/14/arts/14dunn-obit-1/14dunn-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 60