ca points to a persistence of macho attitudes in the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — In Argentina, former President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner has been indicted, accused of endangering the nation’s finances. In Brazil, President Dilma Rousseff is facing an impeachment trial, and her interim successor has appointed only male ministers. In Chile, President Michelle Bachelet, once hugely popular, has seen her approval ratings plunge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/world/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/world/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/world/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/world/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 1875, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/world/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/world/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/world/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'South America’s Powerful Women Are Embattled. Is Gender a Factor?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As South America’s Powerful Women  Struggle, Gender’s Part Is Pondered  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rousseff, Dilma', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachelet, Michelle', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-15T02:06:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Gilbert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9df256ab-5352-5fb9-a221-06574ebc8083', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9df256ab-5352-5fb9-a221-06574ebc8083'}, {'abstract': 'Experts say the $100,000 environmental venture is the first substantial one in the West Bank to be financed by a group involving Muslims and Jews in the U.S.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/15/world/middleeast/solar-project-pairs-muslims-and-jews-to-aid-west-bank-farmers.html', 'snippet': 'Experts say the $100,000 environmental venture is the first substantial one in the West Bank to be financed by a group involving Muslims and Jews in the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUJA, West Bank — Samer Atiyat, a