el “Manuscript Found in Accra.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fierce, multilingual chanteuse Ute Lemper is a teacher as much as she is a singer. And at Symphony Space on Friday evening, she performed most of her remarkable new album, “The 9 Secrets,” for which she set lyrics by the Brazilian author Paulo Coelho to original music. A song cycle based on his novel “Manuscript Found in Accra,” it is an auspicious collaboration.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/16LEMPER/16LEMPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/16LEMPER/16LEMPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/16LEMPER/16LEMPER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/16LEMPER/16LEMPER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/16LEMPER/16LEMPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/16LEMPER/16LEMPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/16LEMPER/16LEMPER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Ute Lemper Seeks Truth and Justice in a Collaboration With Paulo Coelho', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Truths in a Collaboration Both Literary and Musical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coelho, Paulo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Symphony Space', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The 9 Secrets (Album)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Manuscript Found in Accra (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lemper, Ute', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-15T21:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/88bd8a7d-51d5-5517-b381-58ed17caa23a', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88bd8a7d-51d5-5517-b381-58ed17caa23a'}, {'abstract': 'The director, in Cannes with “The BFG,” discusses the original author’s anti-Semitism and explains why “Jaws” remains a painful memory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/17/movies/a-word-with-steven-spielberg.html', 'snippet': 'The director, in Cannes with “The BFG,” discusses the original author’s anti-Semitism and explains why “Jaws” remains a painful memory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France — “The BFG,” the latest from Steven Spielberg, is based on the 1982 book of the same title by Roald Dahl. It’s the story of young Sophie (the newcomer Ruby Barnhill), who one night is plucked from her bed by a giant hand. She soon discovers that the hand belongs to the BFG — voiced with an ache by Mark Rylance — or the Big Friendly Giant. The girl and the giant bond, naturally, and soon enough this funny, creepy, quirky child-snatching story turns into an odd-couple tale about two lonely souls who set out to vanquish a gang of giant hooligans who snack on “human beans” — people.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/17spielberg/16spielberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/17spielberg/16spielberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/17spielberg/16spielberg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/17spielberg/16spielberg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/17spielberg/16spielberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/17spielberg/16spielberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/arts/17spielberg/16spielberg-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Word With: Steven Spielberg', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cinematic Magic and the Soul',