nk': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/92fe4f23-64ab-5892-95c9-0113f64b73a6', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92fe4f23-64ab-5892-95c9-0113f64b73a6'}, {'abstract': 'We don’t know enough about the nature of physical stuff to know that conscious experience can’t be physical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/opinion/consciousness-isnt-a-mystery-its-matter.html', 'snippet': 'We don’t know enough about the nature of physical stuff to know that conscious experience can’t be physical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, it seems, some verifiably intelligent person tells us that we don’t know what consciousness is. The nature of consciousness, they say, is an awesome mystery. It’s the ultimate hard problem. The current Wikipedia entry is typical: Consciousness “is the most mysterious aspect of our lives”; philosophers “have struggled to comprehend the nature of consciousness.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/opinion/16stoneWeb/16stoneWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 476, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/16/opinion/16stoneWeb/16stoneWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 476}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/opinion/16stoneWeb/16stoneWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/opinion/16stoneWeb/16stoneWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1625, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/opinion/16stoneWeb/16stoneWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/16/opinion/16stoneWeb/16stoneWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/opinion/16stoneWeb/16stoneWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Consciousness Isn’t a Mystery. It’s Matter.', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Senses and Sensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Galen Strawson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Galen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strawson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/984ca9c6-b4d3-5729-be9c-9a7da6c39399', 'word_count': 1569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/984ca9c6-b4d3-5729-be9c-9a7da6c39399'}, {'abstract': 'A New York City plan to charge for shopping bags brings to a reader’s mind the image of bags littering the Grand Canyon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/opinion/plastic-bags-in-the-grand-canyon.html', 'snippet': 'A New York City plan to charge for shopping bags brings to a reader’s mind the image of bags littering the Grand Canyon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plastic Bags in the Grand Canyon', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plastic Bags in the Canyon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastic Bags', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Canyon National Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c677b1cf-ec30-5770-92c0-7cc8ea567936', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c677b1cf-ec30-5770-92c0-7cc8ea567936'}, {'abstract': 'Bioengineered food products are safe. So why do we try to hide the facts about them?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/opinion/i-run-a-gmo-company-and-i-support-gmo-labeling.html', 'snippet': 'Bioengineered food products are safe. So why do we try to hide the facts about them?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boston — MY first exposure to biotechnology was from my father. He grew up with juvenile diabetes, and for most of his life had taken daily injections of insulin from pigs, even though it came with a risk of side effects. That changed in 1982 when Eli Lilly introduced Humulin. I remember the Humulin box with “human insulin (recombinant DNA origin)” proudly displayed on the label: Biological engineers had transferred human DNA-encoding insulin into bacteria, and that meant my dad could get the real thing and no longer had to make do with insulin from animals.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/16kelly/16kelly-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/16kelly/16kelly-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/16kelly/16kelly-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/16kelly/16kelly-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1150, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/16kelly/16kelly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/16kelly/16kelly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/14/opinion/16kelly/16kelly-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Run a G.M.O. Company — and I Support G.M.O. Labeling', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Make G.M.O. Food. Label It.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels (Product)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biotechnology and Bioengineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T07:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b6ec957-a0ed-56be-bf9e-8ea41e073628', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b6ec957-a0ed-56be-bf9e-8ea41e073628'}, {'abstract': 'The candidate’s string of failures and dealings with unions in the New Jersey city give a glimpse into his methods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/opinion/what-atlantic-city-casino-workers-know-about-the-trump-brand.html', 'snippet': 'The candidate’s string of failures and dealings with unions in the New Jersey city give a glimpse into his methods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTIC CITY — As a cocktail waitress for 27 years in this city’s Xanadu of a casino industry, Valerie McMorris learned the hard way that Donald Trump’s art of the deal too often proved to be the art of bankruptcy. “I’ve been through three bankruptcies with Mr. Trump,” she said, recalling how the fast years of gambling growth here degenerated into a crushing excess of casinos. She watched as Mr. Trump hurried to remove “TRUMP” from the facades of suddenly failing casinos, lest they undermine his claims to financial i