pring, one writer escapes to the deserted island of Gotland seeking solitude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I ARRIVED ON GOTLAND, an island 200 kilometers south of Stockholm in the Baltic Sea, late in the afternoon at the end of March. From the airplane window I saw tall pine trees, mist. Toy cars chugged through brown farmlands along black ribbons of road. I picked up my car, a red Volvo, from a local retailer specializing in used cars — not used in the sense that all rental cars are, but in the more pedestrian sense of “old” — and drove up Route 149, a shady, gently curving road that took me to the manor where I would be staying that night. There were ponies at the manor. These were not the wild ponies that roam the south of Gotland, but they were ponies nonetheless. I petted them in the company of Ulrika, who runs the property with her partner, Berra.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '159', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/t-magazine/22tmag-gotland-slide-NXD9/22tmag-gotland-slide-NXD9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/t-magazine/22tmag-gotland-slide-NXD9/22tmag-gotland-slide-NXD9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 863}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/t-magazine/22tmag-gotland-slide-NXD9/22tmag-gotland-slide-NXD9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 713, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/t-magazine/22tmag-gotland-slide-NXD9/22tmag-gotland-slide-NXD9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1425, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 