', 'snippet': 'Who should decide about restroom access for transgender students in U.S. public schools?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, the Obama administration sent a letter to every public school district in the country stating that transgender students should be allowed to use the bathrooms that match their gender identity. The letter also implied that schools that do not comply with the directive could face lawsuits or a loss of federal aid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Student Question | Who Should Decide Which School Restroom Transgender Students Can Use?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T09:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff8da751-61be-5dc4-8110-f7a0b359800e', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff8da751-61be-5dc4-8110-f7a0b359800e'}, {'abstract': 'Mount Chimborazo in Ecuador rises about 20,500 feet above sea level, far short of Everest’s 29,029 feet. But it’s a different story when you measure from the center of the Earth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/17/world/what-in-the-world/the-mountain-that-tops-everest-because-the-earth-is-fat.html', 'snippet': 'Mount Chimborazo in Ecuador rises about 20,500 feet above sea level, far short of Everest’s 29,029 feet. But it’s a different story when you measure from the center of the Earth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What in the World offers you glimpses of what our journalists are observing around the globe. Let us know what you think: whatintheworld@nytimes.com', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', '