d Washington on a nativist platform to “purify” national politics by stopping the influx of Irish and German Catholics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbLarge-v6.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Know-Nothing Tide', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Know Nothing Wins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T10:40:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/15637ec1-9cea-5021-b56e-79d16e7ea667', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15637ec1-9cea-5021-b56e-79d16e7ea667'}, {'abstract': 'Though parents may be worried, the need for a diagnosis depends on whether the child is actually struggling.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/clumsiness-as-a-diagnosis/', 'snippet': 'Though parents may be worried, the need for a diagnosis depends on whether the child is actually struggling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years ago, I took care of a little girl whose mother worried tremendously about her clumsiness. When she was 4 or 5, my patient was still tripping and falling more than other children her age, her mother thought. She had trouble with the clapping games in her preschool. The mother was visibly distressed when she talked about this. She told me that she herself had been “that kid,” the clumsy one, the last one chosen for every team.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/health/well_klass/well_klass-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/16/health/well_klass/w