'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Russian forces head toward Baghdad in 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/1916-russians-close-in-on-baghdad/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Russian forces head toward Baghdad in 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PETROGRAD — The advance guards of General Baratov are now less than 120 miles distant from Bagdad. The Russian forces have already entered Mesopotamia and the occupation of the region of Revanduz represents an important success. This advance gives the Turks little breathing space, for all their efforts to retard the Russian offensive toward Bagdad by the reinforcement of the Khanikin detachment have proved absolutely unavailing. The sixth Turkish army, which is now opposing the British force on the Tigris, in the neighborhood of Kut-el-Amara, is now seriously inconvenienced by the presence of Russian troops on the Persian frontier.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, May 17, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/17/blogs/17iht-oldmay17-russia/17iht-oldmay17-russia-jumbo.png', 'height': 595, 'width': 527, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/17/blogs/17iht-oldmay17-russia/17iht-oldmay17-russia-superJumbo.png', 'height': 595, 'width': 527, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/17/blogs/17iht-oldmay17-russia/17iht-oldmay17-russia-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/17/blogs/17iht-oldmay17-russia/17iht-oldmay17-russia-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/17/blogs/17iht-oldmay17-russia/17iht-oldmay17-russia-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Russians Close In on Baghdad', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T13:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/217b11cd-5395-500d-b08c-bf1995528c19', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/217b11cd-5395-500d-b08c-bf1995528c19'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The Royal Air Force attacks German planes in Syria in 1941.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/1941-royal-air-force-bombs-syria/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The Royal Air Force attacks German planes in Syria in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The British forces in the Middle East have taken the offensive on a limited scale in Syria, where the German threat has recently become serious, and for the first time the Royal Air Force has attacked German planes at Syrian airdromes. The use of these bases had been accorded t