count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/0ef96b6f-dcc7-5ff3-885d-d346ec6cd203'}, {'abstract': 'The first lady has become adept at transforming what has traditionally been a decorative job (hostess) into a piece of diplomatic art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/fashion/michelle-obama-nordic-state-dinner.html', 'snippet': 'The first lady has become adept at transforming what has traditionally been a decorative job (hostess) into a piece of diplomatic art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s pretty clear at this point that whatever Michelle Obama wears is going to be greeted with shouts of excitement. That when she appears in a gown for a formal occasion, the effect will be described with words like “stuns” and “glistens” and “sparkles.” And so it was indeed last Friday at the Nordic state dinner, where David Letterman and Snapchat’s Evan Spiegel and his girlfriend, Miranda Kerr (among others), dined with the heads of five Nordic states, Demi Lovato sang, and Mrs. Obama wore a draped bodice off-the-shoulder peach-toned Naeem Khan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michelle Obama, Nordic State Dinner and Missed Opportunity', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nordic Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T14:11:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'n