ce Archer uses digital programming to produce her heavily embellished women’s wear pieces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/16/t-magazine/london-fashion-designer-embroidery-technology-alice-archer.html', 'snippet': 'Alice Archer uses digital programming to produce her heavily embellished women’s wear pieces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While many young British designers are known to focus on the avant-garde, the London-based Alice Archer, 31, is building a modern women’s wear business around a very traditional art: embroidery. But her intricate threadwork — which she applies to every dress, skirt and coat she designs — is more high-tech than her customers might imagine.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/09/t-magazine/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ/Alice-Archer-slide-U3EZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Person to Know: The Designer Transforming Embroidery With Technology', 'kicker': 'On the Verge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hand-Embroidered, the Digital Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Saint Martins College of Art and Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-16T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hattie Crisell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hattie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crisell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/677dcd34-34d2-57a0-aaff-48d00a8d27d7', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/677dcd34-34d2-57a0-aaff-48d00a8d27d7'}, {'abstract': 'The recipes are real. Pizza starts with dough, not an English muffin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/18/dining/culinary-institute-of-america-young-chef-kids-cookbook.html', 'snippet': 'The recipes are real. Pizza starts with dough, not an English muffin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recipes in the Culinary Institute of America’s new cookbook for children are not dumbed down. Pizza starts with dough, not an English muffin. And the book opens with good habits for kitchen safety — for the food as well as the chef. (It is recommended for children ages 10 to 14, but an adult who has never really cooked could learn a few lessons, too.) This bright and engaging book explains equipment, knife work, cooking methods and how to taste and create flavor. Sidebars headed “Think Like a Chef” offer variations and tips, and strewn throughout are notes about ingredients and their histories: “The Young Chef: Recipes and Techniques for Kids Who Love to Cook,” by Mark Ainsworth and the Culinary Institute of America (Houghton Mifflin Harcourt, $23, paperback).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/dining/15BURNER-BOOK_web/15BURNER-BOOK_web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 855, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/15/dining/15BURNER-BOOK_web/15BURNER-BOOK_web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 855}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/dining/15BURNER-BOOK_web/15BURNER-BOOK_web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/dining/15BURNER-BOOK_web/15BURNER-BOOK_web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1571, 'width': 1102, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/15/dining/15BURNER-BOOK_web/15BURNER-BOOK_web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/15/dining/15BURNER-BOOK_web/15BURNER-BOOK_web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbn