k-passing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/18/opinion/shamelessly-ashamed-in-moscow.html', 'snippet': 'The “apology” for the doping of Russian athletes issued by Russia’s minister of sports is an exercise in buck-passing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the things Vitaly Mutko, Russia’s minister of sports, wrote in his “apology” for what he described as Russia’s “problem” with doping, one is true: “It cannot be right that clean athletes should suffer for the behavior of others.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shamelessly ‘Ashamed’ in Moscow', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shamelessly Ashamed in Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-17T13:52:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/caf3a04b-68a6-5d04-b897-648c4ce3e88d', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caf3a04b-68a6-5d04-b897-648c4ce3e88d'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A national seamen’s strike begins in Britain in 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/17/1966-strike-starts-to-hurt-britain/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A national seamen’s strike begins in Britain in 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The two-day-old national seamen’s strike began to tighten its stranglehold on Britain’s economy today [May 17]. It caused prices to rise and the pound to slide to its lowest level in nine months. The Bank of England reportedly supported the pound for the second day running after it slumped to $2.7904. By the close of trading tonight the currency had rallied somewhat to $2.7913. Dockers also gave their first active backing to the striking seamen today when they refused to handle a Lisbon-bound freighter.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, May 18, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Strike Starts to Hurt Britain', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-17T14:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a9c2232-3d85-5e4c-8d4c-741729401904', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a9c2232-3d85-5e4c-8d4c-741729401904'}, {'abstract': 'The actor from “The Wire” was arrested over the weekend after a woman said he struck her at an Atlanta hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/18/us/wendell-pierce-atlanta-hotel-attack.html', 'snippet': 'The actor from “The Wire” was arrested over the weekend after a woman said he struck her at an Atlanta hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actor Wendell Pierce took to Twitter late Monday to dispute reports that he tried to force his way into a woman’s room after a political discussion turned ugly at an Atlanta hotel over the weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/us/17xp-pierce/17xp-pierce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarg