', 'value': 'Unbroken: A World War II Story of Survival, Resilience, and Redemption (Book)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Boys in the Boat (Movie)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Quiet Power: The Secret Strengths of Introverts (Book)', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-18T09:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Burleigh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burleigh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe86c8d8-4c21-5430-ba95-a42d6d3f62e7', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe86c8d8-4c21-5430-ba95-a42d6d3f62e7'}, {'abstract': 'Listening in as three movers and shakers offer advice on taking companies to the top.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/books/review/zero-to-one-good-profit-and-team-of-teams.html', 'snippet': 'Listening in as three movers and shakers offer advice on taking companies to the top.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ignore the scent of self-congratulation that wafts from nearly every book in the How to Succeed category and what remains is largess, priced to move. The subtext reads something like this: “I made it big, and if you follow my advice, sold here for a fraction of what it cost me, you can, too.” But pure altruism rarely explains much, and the ulterior motives behind these works are often as interesting as their catechisms.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22segal-span/22segal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 210, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22segal-span/22segal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 210}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22segal-span/22segal-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22segal-span/22segal-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22segal-span/22segal-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22segal-span/22segal-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22segal-span/22segal-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Zero to One,’ ‘Good Profit’ and ‘Team of Teams’', 'kicker': 'Audiobooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paths of Glory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audiobooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thiel, Peter A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Masters, Blake (1986- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Charles G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McChrystal, Stanley A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michael, Paul', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Good Profit: How Creating Value for Others Built One of the World's Most Successful Companies (Book)", 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Zero to One: Notes on Startups, or How to Build the Future (Book)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Team of Teams: New Rules of Engagement for a Complex World (Book)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-18T09:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Segal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Segal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/03e517dd-7cf5-570d-a3b8-6d4434fb94b0', 'word_count': 1343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03e517dd-7cf5-570d-a3b8-6d4434fb94b0'}, {'abstract': 'Two recordings give voice to classic tales from the children’s canon. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/books/review/alices-adventures-in-wonderland-and-grimms-fairy-tales.html', 'snippet': 'Two recordings give voice to classic tales from the children’s canon. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Being read to is one of life’s best small luxuries, but it was until very recently reserved for children and a few select adults. Now any grown-up with a smartphone has tens of thousands of audiobooks readily at her disposal in the car, gym, kitchen or bed. The appeal of listening to a book is still, however, much entangled with deep memories of slipping under a parent’s arm to have a story unfolded for you in a beloved voice. Is it any wonder, then, that the most celebrated audiobook narrators — in particular, Jim Dale, who has read the Harry Potter series for at least three generations of fans — acquire their own devout followings? The peculiar intimacy of modern audiobook narration (with earbuds, the narrator’s voice seems to emanate from inside the listener’s head) intensifies the old association with cozying up with Mom or Dad and a bedtime book. These performers may be unknown to the culture at large, but among the initiated they are adored; they could teach psychotherapists a thing or two about \xadtransference.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22MILLER/22Miller-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22MILLER/22Miller-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22MILLER/22Miller-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22MILLER/22Miller-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22MILLER/22Miller-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22MILLER/22Miller-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/books/review/22MILLER/22Miller-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scarlett Johansson’s Latest: Narration of ‘Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland’', 'kicker': 'Audiobooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lilt of Make-Believe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audiobooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johansson, Scarlett', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimm, Jacob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimm, Wilhelm', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carroll, Lewis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "ALICE'S ADVENTURES IN WONDERLAND (BOOK)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Grimm's Fairy Tales (Book)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-18T09:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/665cff16-e4b2-5cbd-9fbb-6167694ae285', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/665cff16-e4b2-5cbd-9fbb-6167694ae285'}, {'abstract': 'We ought to put every object of child desire through its own wants-versus-needs test, one that inevitably ends with a question about how much is enough.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/18/what-should-you-pay-for-a-childs-guitar-or-any-musical-instrument/', 'snippet': 'We ought to put every object of child desire through its own wants-versus-needs test, one that inevitably ends with a question about how much is enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It should have been a simple enough request. My 10-year-old, after several years of piano and voice lessons, had asked for a guitar. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/health/wellhand/wellhand-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/16/health/wellhand/wellhand-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/health/wellhand/wellhand-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/health/wellhand/wellhand-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/health/wellhand/wellhand-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/16/health/wellhand/wellhand-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/16/health/wellhand/wellhand-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Should You Pay for a Child’s Guitar (Or Any Musical Instrument)?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-18T09:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c804eed-f002-58ed-94ba-e06ba9baa54d', 'word_count': 1079, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c804eed-f002-58ed-94ba-e06ba9baa54d'}, {'abstract': 'The potential cancer-fighting benefits of exercise seem to hold true even if someone is overweight, a comprehensive new study found.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/18/exercise-tied-to-lower-risk-for-13-types-of-cancer/', 'snippet': 'The potential cancer-fighting benefits of exercise seem to hold true even if someone is overweight, a comprehensive new study found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone who still needs motivation to move more may find it in a new study showing that, in addition to its other health benefits, exercise appears to substantially reduce the risk of developing 13 different varieties of cancer. That is far more types than scientists previously thought might be impacted by exercise. The comprehensive study also suggests that the potential cancer-fighting benefits of exercise seem to hold true even if someone is overweight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/17/health/well_run/well_run-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/17/health/well_run/well_run-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption'