4704-5ea3-b7a6-f7edcf37cc33', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ae0e95-4704-5ea3-b7a6-f7edcf37cc33'}, {'abstract': 'A former Washington Post editor and current editor in chief of The Columbia Journalism Review, Ms. Spayd succeeds Margaret Sullivan, who left last month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/19/business/media/new-york-times-names-elizabeth-spayd-its-6th-public-editor.html', 'snippet': 'A former Washington Post editor and current editor in chief of The Columbia Journalism Review, Ms. Spayd succeeds Margaret Sullivan, who left last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Spayd, the editor in chief and publisher of The Columbia Journalism Review and a longtime editor at The Washington Post, will become the next public editor at The New York Times, the company announced on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/19/business/media/19spayd/19spayd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/19/business/media/19spayd/19spayd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/19/business/media/19spayd/19spayd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/19/business/media/19spayd/19spayd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/19/business/media/19spayd/19spayd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Times Names Elizabeth Spayd Its 6th Public Editor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Times Names Longtime Journalist Public Editor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spayd, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Editor (Times Column)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-18T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c1d638f-2a72-5a34-825e-b521894df6e7', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c1d638f-2a72-5a34-825e-b521894df6e7'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to break the news of a new love affair to a faraway partner, fund-raisers who double dip and what to do when you suspect malpractice in your pet’s death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/magazine/must-i-tell-my-long-distance-boyfriend-i-met-someone-else.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to break the news of a new love affair to a faraway partner, fund-raisers who double dip and what to do when you suspect malpractice in your pet’s death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have been with my boyfriend for several years, and I love him very much. We each decided to study abroad for the spring semester of our junior year and have found ourselves on opposite ends of the globe. We will be apart for almost six months, with only intermittent access to the phone and Internet. Before we left, we agreed that it would be best to temporarily open our relationship. We wanted to fully enjoy our respective experiences and take the opportunity to explore being with other people. We decided that we would not discuss our flings with each other, at least until we returned. We did this, I believe, with the implicit assumption that we would not fall in love with anyone else.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ethicist/22mag-22ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ethicist/22mag-22ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 862}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ethicist/22mag-22ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 713, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ethicist/22mag-22ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1139, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ethicist/22mag-22ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ethicist/22mag-22ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ethicist/22mag-22ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Must I Tell My Long-Distance Boyfriend I Met Someone Else?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Must I Tell My Long-Distance Boyfriend I Met Someone Else?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterinary Medicine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-18T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4df48c7b-2c40-5e15-b9df-ad825e30227e', 'word_count': 1432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4df48c7b-2c40-5e15-b9df-ad825e30227e'}, {'abstract': 'The app can be confusing for people over a certain age, but it returns something vital to our correspondence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/magazine/how-i-learned-to-love-snapchat.html', 'snippet': 'The app can be confusing for people over a certain age, but it returns something vital to our correspondence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mid-’80s, a German engineer named Friedhelm Hillebrand helped devise a way for cellphones to send and receive text messages. Back then, mobile bandwidth was extremely limited, which meant that the messages needed to be as lightweight as possible. The story goes that Hillebrand experimented with a variety of greetings and phrases and concluded, in very German fashion, that most things that needed saying could be done so in an economical 160 characters or fewer. “This is perfectly sufficient,” he said of his findings. Eventually the infrastructure improved so that there were no limits to how much text we could transmit at once. And by 2007, texting had surpassed voice calls as the preferred, if not default, mode of communication.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ontech1/22mag-22ontech-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ontech1/22mag-22ontech-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 661}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ontech1/22mag-22ontech-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 930, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ontech1/22mag-22ontech-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1860, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ontech1/22mag-22ontech-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/22/magazine/22ontech1/22mag-22ontech-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank