 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcd332a8-fc2f-5887-9d9e-ffa24aa5558b', 'word_count': 1214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcd332a8-fc2f-5887-9d9e-ffa24aa5558b'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The U.S. secretary of defense calls for stronger relations with China in 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/18/1966-building-bridges-to-peace/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The U.S. secretary of defense calls for stronger relations with China in 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTREAL — Secretary of Defense Robert S. McNamara called today [May 18] for steps to ‘‘build bridges’’ toward Communist China as a means of avoiding war. ‘‘We can do so with properly balanced trade relations, diplomatic contacts, and in some cases even by exchanges of military observers,’’ Mr. McNamara said. His statement was the strongest yet in a series of pronunciations by top U.S. officials indicating a change in attitude toward China. Vice-President Hubert Humphrey recently advocated the ‘‘containment without isolation’’ of China. Mr. McNamara said there were practical alternatives to the current U.S. relationships with both China and the Soviet Union.\xa0—\xa0New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, May 19, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Building Bridges to Peace', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNamara, Robert S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-18T14:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': '