t injustices remain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/18/opinion/in-italy-and-germany-victories-for-gay-rights.html', 'snippet': 'Italy will allow same-sex civil unions and Germany will clear the records of men convicted decades ago under anti-gay laws, but injustices remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Italy and Germany took long overdue steps toward justice for gay and lesbian citizens. On May 11, Italy’s Parliament approved a bill recognizing same-sex civil unions. The same day, the German government announced it would overturn convictions handed down decades ago under a law that criminalized homosexuality. But more must be done before gay and lesbian Italians and Germans enjoy the equal rights they deserve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Italy and Germany, Victories for Gay Rights', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-18T14:28:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9c10484-9457-5dd3-8e9f-0bbbedf1416c', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9c10484-9457-5dd3-8e9f-0bbbedf1416c'}, {'abstract': 'The social media platform has served Mr. Trump’s bombast and provocations well, but such behavior may be poison to a general election campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.