{'abstract': 'A program by the Mark Morris Dance Group includes two new works: “The,” set to one of the “Brandenburg” Concertos, and “A Forest,” set to a Haydn piano trio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/19/arts/dance/review-a-mark-morris-premiere-features-singular-theater-poetry.html', 'snippet': 'A program by the Mark Morris Dance Group includes two new works: “The,” set to one of the “Brandenburg” Concertos, and “A Forest,” set to a Haydn piano trio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No choreographer alive has built up a stronger reputation for musicality than Mark Morris. In his finest works, he taps both our most primal and our most sophisticated responses to music. That’s not the only reason he has been recognized since the 1980s as one of the very few great choreographers of our day — there are also his exceptional imagination; his phenomenal wit; the profundity of his view of society; his insistence on live music; and his exceptionally honest, natural dancers — but it’s fundamental.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/19/arts/19MORRIS1/19MORRIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/19/arts/19MORRIS1/19MORRIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 587}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/19/arts/19MORRIS1/19MORRIS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1001, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/19/arts/19MORRIS1/19MORRIS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2003, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cred