e': None, 'lastname': 'WONG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/14ab0fa8-d388-52aa-bbc3-22074589724e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/14ab0fa8-d388-52aa-bbc3-22074589724e'}, {'abstract': 'The musical, at La MaMa, uses songs from Kid Creole and the Coconuts and tells an old-fashioned tale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/theater/dapper-as-ever-kid-creole-dresses-up-his-songs-for-a-new-musical.html', 'snippet': 'The musical, at La MaMa, uses songs from Kid Creole and the Coconuts and tells an old-fashioned tale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actors who were singing and dancing their way through “Cherchez La Femme: The Musical” in a rehearsal room on Great Jones Street were in street clothes and gymwear. The show’s co-author, songwriter and inspiration, who kept a close eye on the proceedings, was far more dapper. When asked, August Darnell proudly itemized his outfit: black-and-white wingtip shoes, dark gray three-piece pinstripe suit with pleated pants, white shirt, vintage necktie, pocket handkerchief folded just so and a classic Fedora. “Once I discovered this mode of attire, I never gave it up,” Mr. Darnell said.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22DARNELL1/22DARNELL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22DARNELL1/22DARNELL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 675}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22DARNELL1/22DARNELL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 910, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo',