 current agreement with Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — A senior Chinese official closed his three-day visit to Hong Kong on Thursday with a strong statement against local calls for greater autonomy and even independence from China, a movement that has persisted amid fears that the city’s liberties are eroding.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/world/20chinahong02/20chinahong02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/20/world/20chinahong02/20chinahong02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/world/20chinahong02/20chinahong02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/world/20chinahong02/20chinahong02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/world/20chinahong02/20chinahong02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/20/world/20chinahong02/20chinahong02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/world/20chinahong02/20chinahong02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Official Condemns Calls for Greater Autonomy in Hong Kong', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Official Says Hong Kong Needs Beijing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wong, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Dejiang', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National People's Congress (China)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wong, Joshua (1996- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-19T12:53:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c49eb66-bb65-5a5d-b192-ff1fbd6bf2d4', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c49eb66-bb65-5a5d-b192-ff1fbd6bf2d4'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Police tapped phone lines at J. P. Morgan and Co. in 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/19/1916-police-tapped-phone-lines/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Police tapped phone lines at J. P. Morgan and Co. in 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — Mr. Swann, District Attorney, caused a sensation today when, decrying legislative investigation of the charges that the police and city officials had ‘‘tapped’’ telephone wires, he announced that one of the lines was ‘‘tapped’’ in an endeavor to catch a thief at Messrs. J. P. Morgan and Co. who was stealing confidential information relating to the prices of munitions to be furnished to France, thus enabling the conspirators to under bid legitimate bidders. One reason for ‘‘tapping’’ the telephones was, according to Mr. John Purroy Mitchel, the Mayor, to foil a German plot to ship munitions to the Mexican bandits at the time of the Mexican invasion. — The New York Herald, European Edition, May 20, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Police Tapped Phone Lines', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchel, John Purroy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-19T13:11:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1abca87c-1a3d-5132-a4e1-4c169e8de568', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1abca87c-1a3d-5132-a4e1-4c169e8de568'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Trump, who has pledged to get rid of gun-free school zones on his first day in office, will address the N.R.A. on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/19/donald-trump-checks-in-with-the-n-r-a/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Trump, who has pledged to get rid of gun-free school zones on his first day in office, will address the N.R.A. on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although he once supported a ban on assault weapons on the home front, Donald Trump has shown no hesitation in readjusting as a presidential candidate to pander to the gun industry, fervidly vowing in January to end gun-free zones in schools and on military bases on his first day in the White House. “My first day, it gets signed, okay?” he told a rally in gun-friendly Vermont. “My first day. There’s no more gun-free zones.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/18/opinion/18clinesWEB/18clinesWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/18/opinion/18clinesWEB/18clinesWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/18/opinion/18clinesWEB/18clinesWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/18/opinion/18clinesWEB/18clinesWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/18/opinion/18clinesWEB/18clinesWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/18/opinion/18clinesWEB/18clinesWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/18/opinion/18clinesWEB/18clinesWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump Checks In With the N.R.A.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisville (Ky)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newtown (Conn)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-19T13:25:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6592167b-2353-58ce-85c3-5797f317a8bf', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6592167b-2353-58ce-85c3-5797f317a8bf'}, {'abstract': 'Separately, in the southern province of Zabul, an attack by two Taliban infiltrators left at least eight policemen dead, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/world/asia/helmand-plane-crash-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Separately, in the southern province of Zabul, an attack by two Taliban infiltrators left at least eight policemen dead, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANDAHAR, Afghanistan — A civilian cargo plane carrying supplies for NATO troops in the southern Afghan province of Helmand crashed this week, killing seven crew members, officials said on Thursday.', 'pri