 original music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, the makers of “The Colorado,” a new eco-documentary, could have gone the easy route and used Barber’s Adagio for Strings as the soundtrack for its elegiac shots of parched landscapes punished by drought and insufficiently fed by what they charge is an “overused, over-promised” Colorado River. And something suitably reflective by Arvo Part might have been dug up to accompany the vintage footage showing the chromatic sandstone caverns of Glen Canyon that have long since been inundated to create Lake Powell.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20TEETH/20TEETH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20TEETH/20TEETH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20TEETH/20TEETH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20TEETH/20TEETH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20TEETH/20TEETH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20TEETH/20TEETH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20TEETH/20TEETH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Colorado,’ a Music-Driven Eco-Documentary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A River, a Film and Sound to Match', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eyuboglu, Murat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Colorado (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado River', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'deBuys, William (1949- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kotche, Glenn (1970- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeigler, Jeffrey', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roomful of Teeth (Music Group)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-19T21:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/952e710a-4a63-5872-8ec7-27513fbb694e', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/952e710a-4a63-5872-8ec7-27513fbb694e'}, {'abstract': 'Planetary scientists report finding the shoreline of an ocean that might have once covered much of Mars’s northern hemisphere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/science/mars-ancient-ocean-tsunamis.html', 'snippet': 'Planetary scientists report finding the shoreline of an ocean that might have once covered much of Mars’s northern hemisphere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tsunamis waves tall enough to swallow the Statue of Liberty washed away the shorelines of Mars’s ancient ocean, according to a study published Thursday.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/TB20-tsunami5/TB20-tsunami5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/06/science/TB20-tsunami5/TB20-tsunami5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/TB20-tsunami5/TB20-tsunami5-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/TB20-tsunami5/TB20-tsunami5-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/TB20-tsunami5/TB20-tsunami5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/06/science/TB20-tsunami5/TB20-tsunami5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/TB20-tsunami5/TB20-tsunami5-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mega-Tsunamis Wiped Away Shoreline of a Martian Ocean', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Martian Mystery: A Shoreline Hidden Under Ice for Millenniums', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tidal Waves and Tsunamis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meteors and Meteorites', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scientific Reports (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, J Alexis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-19T21:22:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas St. Fleur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'St', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c80d10a-d6f1-5f6c-95a7-c9345fa7a98a', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c80d10a-d6f1-5f6c-95a7-c9345fa7a98a'}, {'abstract': 'The show at MoMA PS1 is an enthralling survey of this Chinese artist’s career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/arts/design/cao-fei-captures-modern-malaise-in-a-series-of-inventive-videos.html', 'snippet': 'The show at MoMA PS1 is an enthralling survey of this Chinese artist’s career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a truism of modern life that despite fast and cheap communication technologies, demoralizing alienation is as widespread as ever in the developed world. The Chinese artist Cao Fei, 37, has based on this apparent contradiction a series of stirringly plangent and imaginative videos that have been seen in numerous international exhibitions starting when she was a 21-year-old student at the Guangzhou Academy of Fine Arts. “Cao Fei” (pronounced TSOW fay) at MoMA PS1 in Long Island City, Queens, is an enthralling survey of Ms. Cao’s precocious career, organized by PS1’s director, Klaus Biesenbach, and Jocelyn Miller, a curatorial associate.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20CAOFEI1/20CAOFEI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20CAOFEI1/20CAOFEI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20CAOFEI1/20CAOFEI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20CAOFEI1/20CAOFEI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20CAOFEI1/20CAOFEI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20CAOFEI1/20CAOFEI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20CAOFEI1/20CAOFEI1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cao Fei Captures Modern Malaise in a Series of Inventive Videos', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline