 one of the most viewed television series in history, but numbers are a feeble measure. It was the national water cooler; Americans took long, thirsty drafts, and lingered, sometimes looking one another in the eye and sometimes not.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20FRIDAYFILE/20FRIDAYFILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 317, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20FRIDAYFILE/20FRIDAYFILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 317}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20FRIDAYFILE/20FRIDAYFILE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20FRIDAYFILE/20FRIDAYFILE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1055, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20FRIDAYFILE/20FRIDAYFILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20FRIDAYFILE/20FRIDAYFILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/20FRIDAYFILE/20FRIDAYFILE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Roots,’ the Series That Had Everyone Talking', 'kicker': 'Friday File', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Mary Jo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haley, Alex', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Roots (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-19T21:47:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Jo Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Jo', 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/481acf1c-ea6a-5add-a3e2-910ecc421b29', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/481acf1c-ea6a-5add-a3e2-910ecc421b29'}, {'abstract': 'Starring Adrien Brody as a tabloid columnist, this film deploys conventions evoking “Chinatown” and older classics but ends up feeling prosaic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/movies/-manhattan-night-review-adrien-brody.html', 'snippet': 'Starring Adrien Brody as a tabloid columnist, this film deploys conventions evoking “Chinatown” and older classics but ends up feeling prosaic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adrien Brody is an actor who knows what he’s good at. And in “Manhattan Night,” a classic film noir set in contemporary New York, his character, Porter Wren, is a scuttling tabloid columnist ensnared in an elaborate story of deception, blackmail, murder and sexual duplicity. In its complexity and zest for evil, the plot rivals that of “Chinatown.” The story even has its own Maltese falcon, in