ttorneys General', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Competitive Enterprise Institute', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenpeace', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '350.org', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockefeller Family', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-19T23:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e32889f7-c81c-5df4-a04f-11f06405f860', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e32889f7-c81c-5df4-a04f-11f06405f860'}, {'abstract': 'The House voted to provide only about half of the emergency funds that the Senate did, and took the money away from other important programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/opinion/stealing-from-ebola-to-fight-zika.html', 'snippet': 'The House voted to provide only about half of the emergency funds that the Senate did, and took the money away from other important programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nobody should be surprised when the present House of Representatives, dominated by penurious reactionaries, produces a stingy response to a danger that calls for compassionate largess. But for sheer fecklessness it’s hard to top the House’s response this week to the Zika virus. The salient feature is that in providing money to fight one health menace, it steals from other funds meant to fight an even more dangerous threat — the Ebola virus.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/opinion/20fri1/20fri1-articleLarge.jp