t includes teachings about the caste system and uses the term India rather than South Asia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California to Revise How India Is Portrayed in Textbooks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caste Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-20T01:37:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fc51cb2-c6d0-5ecb-ab7c-3a77cee1c1d3', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fc51cb2-c6d0-5ecb-ab7c-3a77cee1c1d3'}, {'abstract': 'Attendees of a science fair and a musical festival near Citi Field will compete for space thanks to conflicting scheduling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/nyregion/nerds-and-rockers-to-face-off-in-a-queens-parking-lot.html', 'snippet': 'Attendees of a science fair and a musical festival near Citi Field will compete for space thanks to conflicting scheduling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once a year, like an alarm clock that goes berserk on schedule, a thing called Maker Faire sets up in Queens. The Faire is science, dressed up as carnival and art and cartwheeling. There is, for instance, a life-size mousetrap arranged in a giant circle. A bowling ball drops, as it must, from a platform. It lands on a trigger, which flips another level, and 700 feet and a dizzying array of simple machines later, a bank safe drops onto a taxicab.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/nyregion/20ABOUT/20ABOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/20/nyregion/20ABOUT/20ABOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/nyregion/20ABOUT/20ABOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/nyregion/20ABOUT/20ABOUT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/nyregion/20ABOUT/20ABOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/20/nyregion/20ABOUT/20ABOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/nyregion/20ABOUT/20ABOUT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nerds and Rockers to Face Off in a Queens Parking Lot', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nerds and Rockers to Face Off in a Queens Parking Lot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing Meadows-Corona Park (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking Garages and Lots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Hall of Science', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-20T01:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5facc23-f125-5575-a2fb-a5c7191e513f', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5facc23-f125-5575-a2fb-a5c7191e513f'}, {'abstract': 'Many of Ms. Tolchin’s books were written in collaboration with her husband, a journalist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/books/susan-tolchin-political-scientist-who-foresaw-tide-of-voter-anger-dies-at-75.html', 'snippet': 'Many of Ms. Tolchin’s books were written in collaboration with her husband, a journalist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Susan J. Tolchin, a political scientist who explored the workings of political patronage, women in politics and, most presciently, the electoral power of voter anger in several popular books, most of them written with her husband, Martin Tolchin, died on Wednesday at her home in Washington. She was 75.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '