orial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eecbc1a-8804-5311-8571-2bea3353c480', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5eecbc1a-8804-5311-8571-2bea3353c480'}, {'abstract': 'Outrage at police killings of unarmed civilians is justified, but it’s wrong to dismiss Brooklyn D.A. Ken Thompson’s entire tenure because of one case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/opinion/critics-of-brooklyn-da-miss-the-big-picture.html', 'snippet': 'Outrage at police killings of unarmed civilians is justified, but it’s wrong to dismiss Brooklyn D.A. Ken Thompson’s entire tenure because of one case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the two-plus years since he took office, Ken Thompson, the district attorney for Brooklyn, has become a national leader among reform-minded prosecutors. He has stopped prosecuting over low-level marijuana offenses, ramped up his office’s efforts to identify and reverse wrongful convictions, and spearheaded a program to help more than a million New Yorkers erase outstanding warrants for small offenses.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/opinion/20fri2web/20fri2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/20/opinion/20fri2web/20fri2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/opinion/20fri2web/20fri2web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/opinion/20fri2web/20fri2web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 