 that made “Mad Men” great?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/21/arts/television/review-preacher-goes-to-heaven-hell-and-texas.html', 'snippet': 'This new AMC show follows “The Walking Dead” playbook. Can it also deliver the kind of characters that made “Mad Men” great?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jesse Custer (Dominic Cooper) is going through hell. Or rather, hell — or heaven, or some combination of the two — is going through him. Whatever it is, a supernatural force has rudely taken up residence in his body, giving him great power and a tremendous headache.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/21preacher/21preacher-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/21preacher/21preacher-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/21preacher/21preacher-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/21preacher/21preacher-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/21preacher/21preacher-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/21preacher/21preacher-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/arts/21preacher/21preacher-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Less You Know About ‘Preacher’ the Better. Just Watch It.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apocalypse, With a Wink', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMC (TV Network)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Preacher (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Dominic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldberg, Evan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogen, Seth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catlin, Sam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ennis, Garth (1970- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dillon, Steve (1962- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-20T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Poniewozik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poniewozik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/33880713-219f-553d-b8cc-687adce27a9c', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33880713-219f-553d-b8cc-687adce27a9c'}, {'abstract': 'The author doubles down on his life in the Netherlands by getting engaged in the cubicle of a government clerk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/magazine/proposing-marriage-to-save-citizenship.html', 'snippet': 'The author doubles down on his life in the Netherlands by getting engaged in the cubicle of a government clerk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I arriv