, 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME consumers who bought universal life insurance policies decades ago are now facing premium increases in the double-digit percentages to maintain the policies. The policyholders have limited options, since finding affordable replacement policies would probably be difficult now that they are much older.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rising Premiums for Universal Life Insurance Draw Scrutiny', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Life Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transamerica Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Watchdog', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-20T11:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddfffff5-80a0-5d19-b7f7-bc82bb328a95', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddfffff5-80a0-5d19-b7f7-bc82bb328a95'}, {'abstract': 'The Class AA team has turned to fans to find a replacement name with greater links to the area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/21/sports/baseball/will-binghamton-mets-become-binghamton-stud-muffins-the-internet-will-decide.html', 'snippet': 'The Class AA team has turned to fans to find a replacement name with greater links to the area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets’ Class AA affiliate has been located in Binghamton, N.Y., since 1992. Throughout that time it has had a logical, informative and slightly bland name: the Binghamton Mets.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/sports/22BMETSweb1/22BMETSweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/20/sports/22BMETSweb1/22BMETSweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/sports/22BMETSweb1/22BMETSweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/sports/22BMETSweb1/22BMETSweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/sports/22BMETSweb1/22BMETSweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/20/sports/22BMETSweb1/22BMETSweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/20/sports/22BMETSweb1/22BMETSweb1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will the Binghamton Mets Become the Stud Muffins? The Internet Will Decide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': 