yline': {'original': 'By Kerry Hannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9045718a-48b4-5c03-b343-3c107b6a5701', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9045718a-48b4-5c03-b343-3c107b6a5701'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Belgium will vote on an extension of the right of suffrage, in 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/20/1891-universal-suffrage-in-belgium/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Belgium will vote on an extension of the right of suffrage, in 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — An important political event has occurred today [May 20]. The Section Centrale, or Special Committee of the House of Representatives, has unanimously voted for a revision of the Belgian Constitution. This means that the House will ultimately vote for an extension of the right of suffrage, but it does not follow that the Senate will give its sanction to the suffrage reform, or that the reform will go even so far as halfway towards universal suffrage. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retrospective-Belgium/21iht-retrospective-Belgium-jumbo.png', 'height': 654, 'width': 517, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retrospective-Belgium/21iht-retrospective-Belgium-superJumbo.png', 'height': 654, 'width': 517, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retros