h battle German troops in Crete, in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — German troops in gliders, with parachutes and in transport planes, invaded the Greek island of Crete early this morning [May 20], but Prime Minister Winston Churchill, who announced the new Nazi blow at the island stronghold commanding the eastern Mediterranean, told the House of Commons tonight that British, New Zealand and Greek forces had succeeded in mopping up all but one ‘‘fairly solid’’ unit of invaders, 1,500 of whom, he said, were wearing New Zealand uniforms. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retrospective-Crete/21iht-retrospective-Crete-articleLarge.png', 'height': 482, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retrospective-Crete/21iht-retrospective-Crete-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 482}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retrospective-Crete/21iht-retrospective-Crete-jumbo.png', 'height': 633, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retrospective-Crete/21iht-retrospective-Crete-superJumbo.png', 'height': 633, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retrospective-Crete/21iht-retrospective-Crete-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/21/blogs/21iht-retrospective-Crete/21iht-retrospective-Crete-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'