 None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99fe1761-0102-5a0b-862b-76abde52e159', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99fe1761-0102-5a0b-862b-76abde52e159'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities in Madrid had tried to prohibit the Estelada, a Catalan flag that has become a symbol of a pro-independence movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/21/world/europe/ban-on-catalan-flag-at-spanish-soccer-final-is-overturned.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities in Madrid had tried to prohibit the Estelada, a Catalan flag that has become a symbol of a pro-independence movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — A Spanish judge on Friday overruled a decision by the authorities in Madrid to ban Catalan flags from the Copa del Rey soccer final, helping to defuse a dispute that had spilled the country’s territorial and political tensions into its favorite sport.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ban on Catalan Flag at Spanish Soccer Final Is Overturned', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Rules Catalan Flag  May Fly at Final After All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catalonia (Spain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-20T17:49:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d761da87-95d7-514c-8b03-e0bd8e5d142e', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d761da87-95d7-514c-8b03-e0bd8e5d142e'}, {'abstract': 'A new lodge from the Mumbai, India-based Taj Safaris, Meghauli Serai, and Mendocino County in Northern California will open two new hiking trails.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/travel/in-brief-wildlife-safaris-in-nepal-new-trails-in-california.html', 'snippet': 'A new lodge from the Mumbai, India-based Taj Safaris, Meghauli Serai, and Mendocino County in Northern California will open two new hiking trails.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nepal may be known for being home to Mount Everest, but its wildlife is an attraction as much as the snow peaks. A new lodge from the Mumbai, India-based Taj Safaris, Meghauli Serai, is situated in Chitwan National Park in south-central Nepal and has 30 rooms and an infinity pool overlooking the Rapti River. The park is home to 550 native bird species including the great hornbill and more than 60 species of mammals such as leopards, wild dogs and Bengal tigers; a greater one-horned rhinoceros is also a big draw. In addition to safaris, guests have the option to take guided jungle walks, canoe on the Rapti River and hike in the Himalayan foothills. Prices from $535 per person, per day, including meals and most activities.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/travel/22BRIEF2/22BRIEF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/travel/22BRIEF2/22BRIEF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/travel/22BRIEF2/22BRIEF2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/travel/22BRIEF2/22BRIEF2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/travel/22BRIEF2/22BRIEF2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/22/travel/22BRIEF2/22BRIEF2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/travel/22BRIEF2/22BRIEF2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Brief: Wildlife Safaris in Nepal; New Trails in California', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hikes and Hiking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Safaris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-20T17:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62d869d5-8471-54a7-a1a9-1993d6de3190', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62d869d5-8471-54a7-a1a9-1993d6de3190'}, {'abstract': 'The song, by Blue Öyster Cult, has been used in dozens of films and television shows over the years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/movies/dont-fear-the-reaper-blue-oyster-cult-creepy-tune.html', 'snippet': 'The song, by Blue Öyster Cult, has been used in dozens of films and television shows over the years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you hear the riff, something deadly is on the way. Blue Öyster Cult’s biggest hit single, “(Don’t Fear) the Reaper,” has been spooking film audiences for nearly 40 years, ever since its release in May 1976.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22REAPER1/22REAPER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22REAPER1/22REAPER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22REAPER1/22REAPER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22REAPER1/22REAPER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1219, 'width': 1798, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22REAPER1/22REAPER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22REAPER1/22REAPER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/arts/22REAPER1/22REAPER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘(Don’t Fear) the Reaper’ Is a Creepy Tune, Even With the Cowbell', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Creepy Tune, Even With the Cowbell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "(Don't Fear) the Reaper (Song)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Oyster Cult', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-20T17:52:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Spitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cefe2ce1-b15a-5487-9074-34d2f159f36b', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cefe2ce1-b15a-5487-9074-34d2f159f36b'}, {'abstract': 'Simona Halep, Madison Keys, Kei Nishikori and Dominic Thiem are among the players who could take a turn in the spotlight in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/22/sports/tennis/french-open-players-to-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Simona Halep, Madison Keys, Kei Nishikori and Dominic Thiem are among the players who could take a turn in the spotlight in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French Open, which begins Sunday, will be without one of tennis’s biggest stars, Roger Federer, who withdrew Thursday. Belinda Bencic, Caroline Wozniacki and the local favorite Gaël Monfils are out, too. Beyond top-ranked Novak Djokovic and Serena Williams, who are both seeking personal milestones at Roland Garros, here are players who could take a turn in the spotlight in Paris.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/sports/22PLAYERSweb1/22PLAYERSweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/22/sports/22PLAYERSweb1/22PLAYERSweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/sports/22PLAYERSweb1/22PLAYERSweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/sports/22PLAYERSweb1/22PLAYERSweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1485, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/sports/22PLAYERSweb1/22PLAYERSweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/22/sports/22PLAYERSweb1/22PLAYERSweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/sports/22PLAYERSweb1/22PLAYERSweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'French Open Players to Watch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Top Seeds Have Plenty of Reasons to Be on Their Guard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major'