 when he began playing “Wilburrrr,” who could talk to a horse, of course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/21/arts/television/alan-young-the-affable-owner-on-mister-ed-dies-at-96.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Young was an established radio and television personality when he began playing “Wilburrrr,” who could talk to a horse, of course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan Young, a comedian and veteran supporting actor who found wide fame as an unlikely sort of second fiddle — the hapless straight man to a talking horse in the 1960s sitcom “Mister Ed” — died on Thursday in Woodland Hills, Calif. He was 96.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/arts/21YOUNGsub-obit/21YOUNGsub-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/21/arts/21YOUNGsub-obit/21YOUNGsub-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 585}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/arts/21YOUNGsub-obit/21YOUNGsub-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/arts/21YOUNGsub-obit/21YOUNGsub-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1998, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/arts/21YOUNGsub-obit/21YOUNGsub-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/21/arts/21YOUNGsub-obit/21YOUNGsub-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0