a missing, drilled for fishing perhaps. A closer look revealed the ice to actually be shattered glass, the round hole left by a bullet.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23CRIMESCENE1/23CRIMESCENE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23CRIMESCENE1/23CRIMESCENE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23CRIMESCENE1/23CRIMESCENE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23CRIMESCENE1/23CRIMESCENE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1326, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23CRIMESCENE1/23CRIMESCENE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23CRIMESCENE1/23CRIMESCENE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23CRIMESCENE1/23CRIMESCENE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Couple Sees Art in the Bullet Holes Piercing a Public Housing Complex', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Queens Couple Sees Art in a Sign of Danger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Queensbridge Houses (Queens, NY, Apartments)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Normandeau, Rita Frazier', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Normandeau, Raymond', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-22T15:48:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42eca0bc-2f08-5973-9574-1b51210bd0f6', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42eca0bc-2f08-5973-9574-1b51210bd0f6'}, {'abstract': 'If Hillary Clinton is elected president, the nonprofit foundation’s collecting of donations from wealthy interests could raise ethical concerns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/23/us/politics/election-clinton-foundation.html', 'snippet': 'If Hillary Clinton is elected president, the nonprofit foundation’s collecting of donations from wealthy interests could raise ethical concerns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Clintons have been targeted by accusations of wrongdoing from Whitewater to Benghazi. There also are self-inflicted wounds: President Bill Clinton’s dalliance with Monica Lewinsky and Hillary Clinton’s use of private email servers while secretary of state.', 'source': 'Th