rld and a trick for testing ribs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The outdoor cooking season inevitably starts off with a crop of grilling and barbecuing guides. “The Total Grilling Manual” includes solid advice on equipment and safety, how much charcoal to light for various situations, and different cuts of meat and how best to prepare them. There’s a global array of recipes, a trick for testing ribs and another for using a mayonnaise slather so fish won’t stick. But cook chicken to an internal temperature of 170 to 180 degrees? I disagree; 160 is more like it: “The Total Grilling Manual,” edited by Lisa Atwood (Welden Owen, $29).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-BOOK/25BURNER-BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-BOOK/25BURNER-BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 894}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-BOOK/25BURNER-BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-BOOK/25BURNER-BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 910, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-BOOK/25BURNER-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-BOOK/25BURNER-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-BOOK/25BURNER-BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Solid Grilling Advice and a Host of Tips', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Consult: Tips for the Outdoor  Cooking Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T09:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70d1c7be-9323-588c-96f8-9fc09e5f715e', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70d1c7be-9323-588c-96f8-9fc09e5f715e'}, {'abstract': 'Yak steak, beef sirloin cap or heritage pork collar compete with the rib-eye.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/25/dining/yak-steaks.html', 'snippet': 'Yak steak, beef sirloin cap or heritage pork collar compete with the rib-eye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rib-eyes have interesting new competition this grilling season. Consider yak steaks. Tasty and extremely lean, the boneless yak strip loin (shown) should be seared rare or medium-rare, then sliced sashimi thin. Or try a beef sirloin cap, called culotte in France and picanha in Brazil. Trim back the top layer of fat and grill it over medium heat, then slice it. Finally, the collar of Mangalitsa heritage pork makes for a luscious couple of portions if you don’t mind some fat. You can also trim out the lean portion, uncooked, to use for kebabs: Yak steaks, $85 for four, heritagefoodsusa.com; picanha, $17 a pound at Le District, in the store only, ledistrict.com, and $17.99 at Fleishers, in the store only, fleishers.com; Mangalitsa pork collar, $16.50 for 10 to 12 ounces, mangalitsa.com. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-STEAK/25BURNER-STEAK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-STEAK/25BURNER-STEAK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-STEAK/25BURNER-STEAK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-STEAK/25BURNER-STEAK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1276, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-STEAK/25BURNER-STEAK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-STEAK/25BURNER-STEAK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-STEAK/25BURNER-STEAK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Something New for the Grill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'p