ype': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23NYTODAY2/23NYTODAY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23NYTODAY2/23NYTODAY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/nyregion/23NYTODAY2/23NYTODAY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: Rule-Bending Buildings', 'kicker': 'New York Today', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T09:57:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra S. Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0bb0fad-29e7-5ccb-879d-79ae6dc4abe4', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0bb0fad-29e7-5ccb-879d-79ae6dc4abe4'}, {'abstract': 'Or for clams, shrimp, bacon-wrapped sea scallops and escargots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/25/dining/cast-iron-oyster-pan.html', 'snippet': 'Or for clams, shrimp, bacon-wrapped sea scallops and escargots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heat this imposing cast-iron pan on the grill, then fill it with oysters on the half shell topped with butter or pesto, and in five minutes they will be cooked to tender succulence. Try it with unshucked oysters, and in 10 minutes they will be open, warm and ready to serve. What the pan will not do is burnish the oysters to look like the photograph on the package; they will be delicious nonetheless. The pan also works for clams, shrimp, bacon-wrapped sea scallops and escargots for a crowd: Cast Iron Oyster Grill Pan, $39.95, Crate & Barrel, crateandbarrel.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 1969, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN/25BURNER-OYSTERPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Oyster Pan for the Grill', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sizzle: A Pan to Cook Succulent Seafood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oysters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T09:58:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/852e1bb3-e2cc-5faf-90f9-5f1573738010', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/852e1bb3-e2cc-5faf-90f9-5f1573738010'}, {'abstract': 'A architect-designed grill, and pizza ovens, rotisseries and planchas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/25/dining/pirch-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'A architect-designed grill, and pizza ovens, rotisseries and planchas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to high-end outdoor appliances, those who may be planning to upgrade, or would simply enjoy ogling equipment priced north of $10,000, will find plenty to see in the sprawling new Pirch Manhattan kitchen and bath showroom. Shiny stainless-steel units, including one designed by the architect David Rockwell, and pizza ovens, rotisseries and an oversize circular flat-top Mongolian grill are all on display. The company, based in San Diego with branches elsewhere, has chefs on hand to demonstrate, and the store offers cooking classes: Pirch, 200 Lafayette Street (Broome Street), pirch.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/dining/25BURNER-