enre through one figure — but who might that be?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classifying anyone as the “most successful” at anything tends to reflect more on the source than the subject. So keep that in mind when I make the following statement: John Philip Sousa is the most successful American musician of all time.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29rocknroll-1/29rocknroll-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29rocknroll-1/29rocknroll-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 727}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29rocknroll-1/29rocknroll-1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 846, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29rocknroll-1/29rocknroll-1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1691, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29rocknroll-1/29rocknroll-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29rocknroll-1/29rocknroll-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29rocknroll-1/29rocknroll-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Which Rock Star Will Historians of the Future Remember?', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rock of Ages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klosterman, Chuck', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berry, Chuck', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sousa, John Philip', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Klosterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klosterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c80575-d367-5bd8-a11c-d43d14cdd930', 'word_count': 3559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c80575-d367-5bd8-a11c-d43d14cdd930'}, {'abstract': 'The museum has begun an extended windup for the exhibit, a blockbuster that will try to define the clothes that have defined us, set to open in December — of 2017.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/21/fashion/moma-finally-embraces-fashion-with-plans-for-is-fashion-modern.html', 'snippet': 'The museum has begun an extended windup for the exhibit, a blockbuster that will try to define the clothes that have defined us, set to open in December — of 2017.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fashion in the museum, traditionally a subject of some tension (is fashion art? and so on), has become something of a trend in recent years: Consider the astounding success of the Metropolitan Museum Costume Institute blockbusters — and the attention paid to the opening gala — and assorted ballyhooed smaller shows, like the Isaac Mizrahi exhibition at the Jewish Museum in New York or the Iris van Herpen show at the High Museum in Atlanta. So it probably shouldn’t be a big surprise that MoMA has finally gotten in on the act.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/fashion/23-OTR/23-OTR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/23/fashion/23-OTR/23-OTR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/fashion/23-OTR/23-OTR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/fashion/23-OTR/23-OTR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/fashion/23-OTR/23-OTR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/23/fashion/23-OTR/23-OTR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/23/fashion/23-OTR/23-OTR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'MoMA Finally Embraces Fashion With Plans for ‘Is Fashion Modern?’', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ''