, 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Citizens Sue Over Climate Change?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T12:02:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf233702-70a1-55e7-8553-aa118363e94d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf233702-70a1-55e7-8553-aa118363e94d'}, {'abstract': 'If the Oscars red carpet features celebrities as pawns in a high-fashion game, this event revealed rock stars dressed — well, seemingly by themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/fashion/at-billboard-awards-a-red-carpet-thats-more-vegas-strip-than-runway.html', 'snippet': 'If the Oscars red carpet features celebrities as pawns in a high-fashion game, this event revealed rock stars dressed — well, seemingly by themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Be true to yourself.” So Serayah McNeill, the “Empire” actress and singer, summed up Taylor Swift’s words of advice in response to a question from the E! host Sibley Scoles, who was reporting on the Billboard Music Awards red carpet Sunday night in Las Vegas.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Billboard Awards, a Red Carpet That’s More Vegas Strip Than Runway', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Las Vegas Aesthetic: Lots of Skin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Billboard (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Soci