 a state of emergency, in 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/23/1966-strike-emergency-in-u-k/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Seamen’s strike forces Britain to proclaim a state of emergency, in 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Britain formally proclaimed a state of emergency today [May 23] as a paralyzing seamen’s strike entered its eighth day with no sign of truce visible on the waterfront. Prime Minister Harold Wilson told Parliament that the emergency powers — which involve controlling food prices, clearing ports, internal transport and maintenance of essential supplies — will be held in reserve until needed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Strike Emergency in U.K.', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T16:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8baa1a8-366c-5dd8-b728-f8fe91640be6', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8baa1a8-366c-5dd8-b728-f8fe91640be6'}, {'abstract': 'Follow 12 men to Miami from the mountains of central Cuba, as they make a five-day voyage using a handmade sailboat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000004427843/a-journey-from-cuba-to-florida.html', 'snippet': 'Follow 12 men to Miami from the mountains of central Cuba, as they ma