th many rules but no limits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/25/dining/braai.html', 'snippet': 'They call it braai, an outdoor cooking ritual with many rules but no limits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAPE TOWN — Katlego Sebastian Mlambo, a chef who grew up in a township outside Johannesburg and has worked in some of South Africa’s most prestigious kitchens, says it is easy to explain the nation’s near-universal love of braai. Braai means grill in Afrikaans, the Dutch-Malay-Zulu-Xhosa-English mash-up language that has evolved here since 1652, when the first Europeans arrived from the Netherlands.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Africa, One Nation United by the Grill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Make It a Habit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moskin, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T18:35:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42261aac-e34a-5e65-9a40-fd13188ec449', 'word_count': 1649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42261aac-e34a-5e65-9a40-fd13188ec449'}, {'abstract': 'Colum McCann, an award-winning author, talks with Pulitzer-prize winning New York Times reporter Dan Barry about Mr. Barry’s new book: “The Boys in the Bunkhouse.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com