g made.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/health/zika-virus-puerto-rico.html', 'snippet': 'As Congress and President Obama argue over funds for combating the virus, donations of things like cash, condoms and mosquito repellent are being made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Congress and the Obama administration argue over funds for fighting the Zika virus, private donations — in cash, condoms and mosquito repellent, for example — are helping fill the gap in Puerto Rico.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Private Sector Is Helping Puerto Rico Fight Zika', 'kicker': 'Global Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Private Sector Helping Puerto Rico Fight Zika', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zika Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson, S C, & Son Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T20:42:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/628315ac-7187-574f-a4e5-30a59fb9cc1e', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/628315ac-7187-574f-a4e5-30a59fb9cc1e'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Clinton’s campaign rejected a Fox News offer and said her priority was addressing “the threat a Donald Trump presidency poses.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/us/politics/hillary-clinton-donald-trump-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Clinton’s campaign rejected a Fox News offer and said her priority was addressing “the threat a Donald Trump presidency poses.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Eager to move on from the Democratic primary race, Hillary Clinton has turned down an invitation to debate Senator Bernie Sanders ahead of California’s primary, her campaign said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Clinton Declines Invitation to Debate Bernie Sanders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clinton Declines Offer to Debate Sanders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-23T20:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/508393ad-d1f5-5330-8c2b-308fc5ce6690', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/508393ad-d1f5-5330-8c2b-308fc5ce6690'}, {'abstract': 'Janine di Giovanni describes the horror and terror Syrians have endured in the five years since a government crackdown on protests erupted into a civil war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/books/review-the-morning-they-came-for-us-reports-on-the-hell-of-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Janine di Giovanni describes the horror and terror Syrians have endured in the five years since a government crackdown on protests erupted into a civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of Janine di Giovanni’s devastating new book, “The Morning They Came for Us,” refers to those terrible moments in ordinary Syrians’ lives when the war in their country becomes personal. Those moments when there is a knock on the door and the police or intelligence services take a family member away. Those moments when a government-delivered barrel bomb falls on your home, your school, your hospital, and daily life is forever ruptured.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/arts/24BOOKDIGOVANNI/24BOOKDIGOVANNI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 932, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/24/arts/24BOOKDIGOVANNI/24BOOKDIGOVANNI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 932}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/arts/24BOOKDIGOVANNI/24BOOKDIGOVANNI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/arts/24BOOKDIGOVANNI/24BOOKDIGOVANNI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1324, 'width': 852, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/arts/24BOOKDIGOVANNI