 marks the 50th anniversary of the beginning of the Cultural Revolution in China, a decade-long explosion of chaos and political intrigue that was the brainchild of one man: Mao Zedong. Mao’s successors, especially Deng Xiaoping, successfully pulled the Communist Party away from personalized, arbitrary rule by one leader, rebuilding China’s bureaucracy and introducing market-oriented economic policies that brought about decades of world-beating economic growth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/world/24CHINAMINZNER/24CHINAMINZNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/24/world/24CHINAMINZNER/24CHINAMINZNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/world/24CHINAMINZNER/24CHINAMINZNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/world/24CHINAMINZNER/24CHINAMINZNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/world/24CHINAMINZNER/24CHINAMINZNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/24/world/24CHINAMINZNER/24CHINAMINZNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/world/24CHINAMINZNER/24CHINAMINZNER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Carl Minzner on the Shift to Personalized Rule in China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minzner, Carl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cultural Revolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng Xiaoping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T06:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Forsythe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forsythe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b854f33-d229-5642-b35a-95876e9eea1e', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b854f33-d229-5642-b35a-95876e9eea1e'}, {'abstract': 'Marcel Sternberger’s portraits of the famed Mexican artists manage to show his ability to deeply delve into the emotions and thoughts of his subjects.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/capturing-the-love-and-psyches-of-frida-kahlo-and-diego-rivera/', 'snippet': 'Marcel Sternberger’s portraits of the famed Mexican artists manage to show his ability to deeply delve into the emotions and thoughts of his subjects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marcel Sternberger and his wife, Ilse, traveled to Mexico in 1951 to photograph President Miguel Alemán Valdés and other prominent politicians and businessmen. But the highlight of the trip came when they befriended two Communist radicals: Diego Rivera and Frida Kahlo. Mr. Sternberger eventually photographed them using his portrait approach, which was a unique blend of psychological and photographic techniques. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Capturing the Love, and Psyches, of Frida Kahlo and Diego Rivera', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahlo, Frida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Diego', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sternberger, Marcel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T07:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rena Silverman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silverman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63918ff4-4916-52d8-9c98-f891f4a21846', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63918ff4-4916-52d8-9c98-f891f4a21846'}, {'abstract': 'A nocturnal vision revealed what led me into psychiatry in the first place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/opinion/dream-me-a-river.html', 'snippet': 'A nocturnal vision revealed what led me into psychiatry in the first place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY schedule was packed with therapy patients back to back until 7 p.m. I wanted to make sure that everyone was seen and everything was taken care of before I left for vacation: medications refilled, phone calls returned, medical documentation completed. I was in a state of flow. Then I got a call from a former patient’s wife, informing me he had died. It stopped me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/opinion/24couchWeb/24couchWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/24/opinion/24couchWeb/24couchWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 605}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/opinion/24couchWeb/24couchWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1016, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/opinion/24couchWeb/24couchWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2031, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/opinion/24couchWeb/24couchWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/24/opinion/24couchWeb/24couchWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/opinion/24couchWeb/24couchWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dream Me a River', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name