{'abstract': 'About 8,000 migrants were living in squalid conditions in the encampment, hoping to be allowed to cross the border and head to Northern or Western Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/25/world/europe/greece-idomeni-refugee-camp.html', 'snippet': 'About 8,000 migrants were living in squalid conditions in the encampment, hoping to be allowed to cross the border and head to Northern or Western Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — The Greek authorities began moving hundreds of refugees on Tuesday out of a sprawling makeshift camp near the village of Idomeni, on the border with Macedonia, a crucial point on the so-called Balkan trail for migrants that has been closed off for months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Begins Moving Refugees Out of Idomeni Camp', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece Begins Moving Refugees Out of Camp Along ‘Balkan Trail’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, Niki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Idomeni (Greece)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T08:31:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ba1ae4f-8520-52b3-9103-eb06a5a9e942', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ba1ae4f-8520-52b3-9103-eb06a5a9e942'}, {'abstract': 'The White House had requested the meeting as a signal to Vietnam’s Communist government that the United States cares about human rights in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/25/world/asia/vietnam-us-obama-human-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The White House had requested the meeting as a signal to Vietnam’s Communist government that the United States cares about human rights in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANOI, Vietnam — President Obama won enthusiastic applause here on Tuesday with a supportive reference to Vietnam’s disputes with China, saying in a speech that “big nations should not bully smaller ones.” But several activists who had been scheduled to meet with him before the speech were prevented from doing so, underscoring the gulf with Hanoi on human rights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Obama Presses Vietnam on Rights, Activists Are Barred From Meeting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rights Activists Are Blocked From Meeting With Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlez, Jane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T08:44:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris and Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': Non