 Cultural Revolution', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breaking the Silence About the Cultural Revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cultural Revolution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T14:36:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc688215-ee9f-5dc5-9fab-bd2ea94b27b9', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc688215-ee9f-5dc5-9fab-bd2ea94b27b9'}, {'abstract': 'It’s been more than a decade since Carlotta Gall moved on to her next assignment. “But you never quite leave a country behind.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/insider/a-reporter-returns-to-kosovo-15-years-later.html', 'snippet': 'It’s been more than a decade since Carlotta Gall moved on to her next assignment. “But you never quite leave a country behind.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times Insider delivers behind-the-scenes insights into how news, features and opinion come together at The New York Times. In this article, Carlotta Gall, a reporter in Pakistan and Afghanistan, shares the personal back story to her recent news analysis of how Kosovo has changed since she set eyes on it in 1999.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/21/insider/21-Insider-Kosovo-Image4/21-Insider-Kosovo-Image4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/21/insider/21-Insider-Kos