perJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25NYQUISTweb/25NYQUISTweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25NYQUISTweb/25NYQUISTweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25NYQUISTweb/25NYQUISTweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25NYQUISTweb/25NYQUISTweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Understandable Absence from the Belmont for Nyquist', 'kicker': 'On Horse Racing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Understandable Absence for Nyquist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nyquist (Race Horse)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Douglas F", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T15:49:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Horse Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebc64366-7987-5e7b-842d-e2697ec47dce', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebc64366-7987-5e7b-842d-e2697ec47dce'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: HMS Hood, Britain’s largest warship is sunk by the German Navy, 1941.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/1941-hood-sunk-in-naval-battle/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: HMS Hood, Britain’s largest warship is sunk by the German Navy, 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Great Britain’s battle cruiser Hood, the largest warship in the world, was sunk today [May 24] in an engagement off Greenland between British and German naval forces. The battle, which may well prove the most tremendous naval encounter of the war, was still going on at a late hour tonight, with the British forces in pursuit of the Nazi warships, which included the battleship Bismarck, already damaged in the action by guns of the Royal Navy. The 42,100-ton Hood, reputedly one of the heaviest protected of all warships, suffered a direct hit in a magazine and blew up. It was feared that few, if any, of the complement of 1,341 men survived, an Admiralty communiqué admitted in giving meagre details of the disaster. — New York Herald Tribune, May 25, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/blogs/25iht-retrospective-hood/25iht-retrospective-hood-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/25/blogs/25iht-retrospective-hood/25iht-retrospective-hood-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/blogs/25iht-retrospective-hood/25iht-retrospective-hood-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/blogs/25iht-retrospective-hood/25iht-retrospective-hood-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/blogs/25iht-retrospective-hood/25iht-retrospective-hood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/25/blogs/25iht-retrospective-hood/25iht-retrospective-hood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/blogs/25iht-retrospective-hood/25iht-retrospective-hood-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1941: Hood Sunk in Naval Battle', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T15:52:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d01732bf-3449-56b9-b1b0-d6e13e2ac805', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d01732bf-3449-56b9-b1b0-d6e13e2ac805'}, {'abstract': 'While invoking Hiroshima has become a universal shorthand f