: 'nyt://article/d534e994-25e4-594f-b26e-03ea4756f01f'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican committee’s financial vice chairmen include Woody Johnson, the New York Jets football owner, and former Ambassador Mel Sembler of Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/25/us/politics/rnc-names-people-to-help-shore-up-donald-trumps-coffers.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican committee’s financial vice chairmen include Woody Johnson, the New York Jets football owner, and former Ambassador Mel Sembler of Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican National Committee has named six people to its finance committee to help raise money for the party and for its presumptive presidential nominee, Donald J. Trump, as it looks to raise roughly $1 billion over the next six months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/us/25fd-rnc/25fd-rnc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/25/us/25fd-rnc/25fd-rnc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/us/25fd-rnc/25fd-rnc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/us/25fd-rnc/25fd-rnc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/us/25fd-rnc/25fd-rnc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/25/us/25fd-rnc/25fd-rnc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/us/25fd-rnc/25fd-rnc-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'R.N.C. Names People to Help Shore Up Donald Trump’s Coffers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T16:29:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/302298eb-4a68-50cf-a60d-f38b2b98db3e', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/302298eb-4a68-50cf-a60d-f38b2b98db3e'}, {'abstract': 'Gaming out a Mitt-as-independent bid, because the next five months are too miserable to contemplate.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/a-last-look-at-the-romney-dream/', 'snippet': 'Gaming out a Mitt-as-independent bid, because the next five months are too miserable to contemplate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I intended my column last week on the dying third-party dream to be the last word on the Mitt Romney as anti-Trump white knight scenario, since it seems clear enough that Romney doesn’t intend to get in and there’s no need to beat a dead white horse prophecy. But then there was the polling showing\xa0Romney pulling a relatively robust 22 percent to Hillary’s 37 percent and Trump’s 35 percent … and the same poll showing that 44 percent of Americans want a third option … and the quotes from Newt Gingrich basically daring the “pathetic” Romney to get into the race … and, oh, the fact that Trump is now (totally predictably) adding Vince Foster to his list of conspiratorial forays … and well, look, let’s just game this out for a minute, because the dream will be officially dead soon enough and we’ll have five months to talk about whatever Trump decides should lead the cable news broadcasts that night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Last Look at the Romney Dream', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T16:32:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4806e22e-5db7-5734-9c64-df0cfe2d49d3', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4806e22e-5db7-5734-9c64-df0cfe2d49d3'}, {'abstract': 'Mirra, who won 14 gold medals at the X Games and popularized the dangerous sport of freestyle BMX, killed himself in February.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/25/sports/dave-mirra-cte-bmx.html', 'snippet': 'Mirra, who won 14 gold medals at the X Games and popularized the dangerous sport of freestyle BMX, killed himself in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dave Mirra, a star BMX rider who killed himself in February, had chronic traumatic encephalopathy, a brain disease linked to head trauma.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25mirra-web/25mirra-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25mirra-web/25mirra-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25mirra-web/25mirra-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25mirra-web/25mirra-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25mirra-web/25mirra-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25mirra-web/25mirra-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/25/sports/25mirra-web/25mirra-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The BMX Rider Dave Mirra, Who Died in a Suicide, Had C.T.E.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BMX Rider Who Died in a Suicide Had C.T.E.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mather, Victor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mirra, Dave (1974-2016)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chronic Traumatic Encephalopathy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycle Motocross', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-24T16:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0efd735b-ec5d-5b66-ae0a-919b1f4b3a31', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0efd735b-ec5d-5b66-ae0a-919b1f4b3a31'}, {'abstract': 'Famous photographers’ recipes were gathered in the late ’70s, but never published — until now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/24/t-magazine/food/photographers-cookbook-key-lime-pie-stephen-shore.html', 'snippet': 'Famous photographers’ recipes were gathered in the late ’70s, but never published — until now.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Photographer’s Cookbook” seems an especially timely tome, given our hunger-inducing Instagram feeds and voyeuristic appetites. Yet curiously enough, its contents — 50 or so recipes, including Ansel Adams’s breakfast eggs poached in beer, Richard Avedon’s Royal Pot Roast and Stephen Shore’s Key Lime Pie Supreme — originate from a late-1970s cookbook project that never resulted in publication, until now. The recipes were first collected by an assistant registrar at what is now the George Eastman Museum, drawn from an array of contributions by over 120 notable photographers of that era, most of whom included photographs or imagery with their submissions. As telling as they are of trends and cultural backgrounds — like Arnold Newman’s dieter’s choice of cottage cheese salad, or Betty Hahn’s kolacky (an Eastern European cookie) — the dishes offer a unique snapshot of the artists’ personalities. Some, like Joseph Jachna’s potato chip cookies — which predated Momofuku Milk Bar’s famous compost cookies by about 40 years — could even be considered visionary.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/t-magazine/24tmag-photographer01/24tmag-photographer01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/24/t-magazine/24tmag-photographer01/24tmag-photographer01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/t-magazine/24tmag-photographer01/24tmag-photographer01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/t-magazine/24tmag-photographer01/24tmag-photographer01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/24/t-magazine/24tmag-photographer01/24tmag-photographer01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/24/t-magazine/24tmag-photographer01/24tmag-photographer01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth'