 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/29/magazine/bj-novak-thinks-actors-are-bad-at-playing-writers.html', 'snippet': 'The actor and app developer on democratizing writing, why Ethan Hawke is too hot to be a writer and avenging his ghostwriter father’s anonymity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most people know you from “The Office,” but your big current project is an app for lists, which seems a little bit like something Ryan Howard would invent. On first glance, it’s the kind of thing people shouldn’t need an app to do. Are you “disrupting” list \xadmaking? I think it’s too simple an idea for Ryan Howard. It’s not trying to prove how brilliant and deep it is. The idea is that we’re surrounded by lists even more than we realize, because our internal monologues are in list form.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1057, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1057}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-jumbo.j