e bank to seek new investment and shape a deal with automakers on sharing the cost of replacing defective equipment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Takata, the Japanese airbag maker embroiled in a huge recall, has hired the investment bank Lazard and is seeking a cash infusion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Takata Hires Lazard as Airbag Maker Bids to Remain ‘Viable’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Takata, Short of Cash, Wants Carmakers to Share Costs of Its Recall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lazard LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Merced, Michael J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Takata Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-25T23:24:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa02b817-9735-5c6e-9633-aee01eb11978', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa02b817-9735-5c6e-9633-aee01eb11978'}, {'abstract': 'News and updates from around the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/us/national-briefing.html', 'snippet': 'News and updates from around the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Nikki R. Haley, a Republican, signed legislation Wednesday that immediately outlaws most abortions in South Carolina at 20 weeks beyond fertilization. The only exceptions are if the mother’s life is in jeopardy or a doctor determines the fetus cannot survive outside the womb. Doctors face up to $10,000 in fines and three years in prison for each violation; prison time is mandatory on a third conviction. These bans are now in effect in at least 13 states and blocked by court challenges in several others. Supporters cite the disputed claim that a fetus can feel pain at 20 weeks. Opponents say later-term abortions usually happen with wanted pregnancies that go horribly wrong. (AP)', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Briefing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haley, Nikki R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Phoenix (Ariz)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-25T23:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89bc9f81-0b14-546d-9bd9-84227b699256', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89bc9f81-0b14-546d-9bd9-84227b699256'}, {'abstract': 'Smith, entering his fourth season with the team, said he deserved “a fair opportunity” to retain the role, though Coach Todd Bowles said he was hopeful Fitzpatrick would be back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/sports/football/geno-smith-practices-as-jets-starter-with-ryan-fitzpatrick-unsigned.html', 'snippet': 'Smith, entering his fourth season with the team, said he deserved “a fair opportunity” to retain the role, though Coach Todd Bowles said he was hopeful Fitzpatrick would be back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — For now, Geno Smith is the starting quarterback of a team that has been candid about wanting to displace him, and he dresses among prominent veterans who have lobbied for his successor to return.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/sports/26jets-web1/26jets-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/26/sports/26jets-web1/26jets-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/sports/26jets-web1/26jets-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/sports/26jets-web1/26jets-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/sports/26jets-web1/26jets-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/26/sports/26jets-web1/26jets-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'r