eat way to keep up your gray matter’s full range of movement, so to speak.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Be That Way', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-26T02:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa75a287-3b13-5cf7-b0da-af1c12c1bb5e', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa75a287-3b13-5cf7-b0da-af1c12c1bb5e'}, {'abstract': 'A past president of the National Cartoonists Society and a Reuben Award winner, Mr. Lazarus helped secure ownership rights for comic strip creators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/arts/design/mell-lazarus-cartoonist-of-miss-peach-and-momma-dies-at-89.html', 'snippet': 'A past president of the National Cartoonists Society and a Reuben Award winner, Mr. Lazarus helped secure ownership rights for comic strip creators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mell Lazarus, who dropped out of high school in Brooklyn to become a successful cartoonist, creating two popular comic strips, one about a mythically sweet schoolteacher and another modeled on his own demanding mother, died on Tuesday at his home in Los Angeles. He was 89.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/arts/26lazarus-obit-1/26lazarus-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/201