 protests and the likelihood of their resolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/27/world/asia/china-xinjiang-tibet-ethnic-unrest.html', 'snippet': 'In an interview, Mr. Hillman and Mr. Tuttle discussed the grievances behind recent protests and the likelihood of their resolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since violent ethnic protests and riots erupted in the western borderlands of China in 2008 and 2009, many scholars have been trying to pinpoint the sources of the unrest. They include Ben Hillman, a senior lecturer in comparative politics at Australian National University, and Gray Tuttle, associate professor of East Asian languages and cultures at Columbia University. They have edited a volume of papers and essays looking at the roots of these tensions, “Ethnic Conflict and Protest in Xinjiang and Tibet: Unrest in China’s West,” recently published by Columbia University Press. The issues explored range widely, be it environmental degradation in Tibet or economic disparities between ethnic Uighurs in their homeland of Xinjiang and Han migrants from other parts of China. In an interview, Mr. Hillman and Mr. Tuttle discussed the grievances behind recent protests and the likelihood of their resolution.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/world/26CHINAETHNIC01/26CHINAETHNIC01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/26/world/26CHINAETHNIC01/26CHINAETHNIC01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/world/26CHINAETHNIC01/26CHINAETHNIC01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/world/26CHINAETHNIC01/26CHINAETHNIC01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/world/26CHINAETHNIC01/26CHINAETHNIC01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/26/world/26CHINAETHNIC01/26CHINAETHNIC01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/world/26CHINAETHNIC01/26CHINAETHNIC01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Ben Hillman and Gray Tuttle on Ethnic Unrest in Xinjiang and Tibet', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hillman, Benjamin T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuttle, Gray', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-26T06:38:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Feng and Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feng', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/239b69b9-0d06-5314-9ea0-9a1c1450f3a4', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/239b69b9-0d06-5314-9ea0-9a1c1450f3a4'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by family portraits, Ayana Jackson set out to “fight photography with photography” and honor the lives of middle-class African-American women of a century ago.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/honoring-the-legacy-of-african-american-women/', 'snippet': 'Inspired by family portraits, Ayana Jackson set out to “fight photography with photography” and honor the lives of middle-class African-American women of a century ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as a little girl Ayana Jackson was entranced by the formal portraits of generations of relatives that held a place of honor in her grandparents’ living room in East Orange, N.J. The photos were comforting, hand-painted presences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honoring the Legacy of African-American Women', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-26T07:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a5bb515-6bf7-5881-8015-40b60beb1e1e', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a5bb515-6bf7-5881-8015-40b60beb1e1e'}, {'abstract': 'The Danish utility expects to sell 15.1 percent to 17.4 percent of its shares in an offering on Nasdaq in Copenhagen next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/27/business/dealbook/dong-energy-ipo.html', 'snippet': 'The Danish utility expects to sell 15.1 percent to 17.4 percent of its shares in an offering on Nasdaq in Copenhagen next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Dong Energy, the Danish utility and the world’s largest offshore wind energy operator, said on Thursday that it could be valued at up to 106.5 billion Danish kroner, or about $16 billion, in its initial public offering in Copenhagen next month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dong Energy May Be Valued at Up to $16 Billion in I.P.O.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dong Energy AS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-26T07:19:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1442d7da-6721-59c2-9522-114a2a7c0c4f', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1442d7da-6721-59c2-9522-114a2a7c0c4f'}, {'abstract': 'The current Supreme Court setup may actually be preferable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/opinion/eight-justices-are-enough.html', 'snippet': 'The current Supreme Court setup may actually be preferable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Malibu, Calif. — LAST week the Supreme Court took an unusual step: It declined to issue a ruling in a case, Zubik v. Burwell, and instead unanimously ordered the lower courts to consider a compromise that the justices themselves suggested. The case, which concerned access to contraceptive coverage under the Affordable Care Act, raised a controversial issue about religious freedom. But by proposing a practical solution that might be amenable to all parties involved, the court avoided addressing that issue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26mcdonaldWeb/26mcdonaldWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26mcdonaldWeb/26mcdonaldWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26mcdonaldWeb/26mcdonaldWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26mcdonaldWeb/26mcdonaldWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26mcdonaldWeb/26mcdonaldWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26mcdonaldWeb/26mcdonaldWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26mcdonaldWeb/26mcdonaldWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eight Justices Are Enough', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eight Justices Are Enough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, Barry P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-26T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry P. McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8358abf0-6eca-55e0-87a7-2d7f1dcd5688', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8358abf0-6eca-55e0-87a7-2d7f1dcd5688'}, {'abstract': 'The first L.G.B.T. envoy has been surprised by his respectful reception even in some conservative countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/opinion/americas-global-campaign-for-gay-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The first L.G.B.T. envoy has been surprised by his respectful reception even in some conservative countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Randy Berry joined the State Department in 1993, a time when gays and lesbians in the federal work force tended to lie low. He was circumspect about his personal life early in his career — with good reason.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26tue3web/26tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26tue3web/26tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xl