ject', 'value': 'Editorial Observer', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-26T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ernesto Londoño', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ernesto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Londoño', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1489724-a985-54d3-804f-0b2a9a314db5', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1489724-a985-54d3-804f-0b2a9a314db5'}, {'abstract': 'Why low-watt anxiety, not total catastrophe, could open the way to the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/opinion/campaign-stops/the-fears-trump-needs.html', 'snippet': 'Why low-watt anxiety, not total catastrophe, could open the way to the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So we’ve established that Donald Trump can lead Hillary Clinton in a poll, indeed in several polls. This should concern liberals and Democrats and anyone who fears a Trump presidency, but it shouldn’t inspire raw panic. Trump is benefiting from having clinched his nomination; Clinton is suffering through the last stand of Bernie Sanders. Trump has climbed to about 43 percent, not 50 percent; Hillary has lost support that she should be able to win back once it’s just the two of them. Barring the unforeseen, Trump’s path to the presidency is still obscure, his likely coalition insufficient, his chances of losing by a comfortable margin quite high.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26douthatWeb/26douthatWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26douthatWeb/26douthatWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26douthatWeb/26douthatWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26douthatWeb/26douthatWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26douthatWeb/26douthatWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26douthatWeb/26douthatWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/26/opinion/26douthatWeb/26douthatWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gray Swan Theory of Trump', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-26T07:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/304f766d-84ca-59b8-9c39-203e7a8b1eee', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/304f766d-84ca-59b8-9c39-203e7a8b1eee'}, {'abstract': 'It’s easy to see why young people are having a make-me-want-to-holler moment, but you don’t want to strengthen your enemies and weaken your cause.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/opinion/violence-is-never-the-answer.html', 'snippet': 'It’s easy to see why young people are having a make-me-want-to-holler moment, but you don’t want to strengthen your enemies and weaken your cause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I watched violence erupt on television among anti-Donald Trump protesters in Albuquerque, on Tuesday, my heart sank. This outbreak came on the heels of the chaotic scene at the state Democratic convention in Nevada and death threats against the state party chairwoman there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/blow-circular/blow-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/blow-circular/blow-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/blow-circular/blow-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/blow-circular/blow-circular-superJumbo-v5.