in': 'Ebola Training in Guinea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jhpiego Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ghana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-26T10:58:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ea2cf3d6-b85d-5650-9f50-a1dce46d18cf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ea2cf3d6-b85d-5650-9f50-a1dce46d18cf'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on how to handle encounters with family members who have rejected you on religious grounds and whether you should step in when a mother leaves her child alone in a park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/29/magazine/how-do-i-explain-to-my-evangelical-relatives-why-i-avoid-family-functions.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on how to handle encounters with family members who have rejected you on religious grounds and whether you should step in when a mother leaves her child alone in a park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I grew up in a strict evangelical home and participated in our church as a child without fully understanding its principles. As an adult, I don’t subscribe to any religion. My immediate family, however, continues to be deeply religious and very much adheres to what I now believe are extreme views. They are, of course, free to worship as they please. I, however, take issue with the hypocrisy in their own lives. For example, they are strongly anti-choice, yet one had an abortion during a complicated pregnancy. They are “pro-family,” yet gave up an adopted child that became “too difficult.” They boycotted a parental wedding because the bride and groom were each previously married; participating would have “blessed the sin.” There is also a personal aspect for me in that they openly oppose L.G.B.T. rights, support politicians and groups that are extremely anti-gay, attend schools that require opposition to gay civil liberties in their codes of conduct and belong to anti-gay churches. I’m openly gay. I have been told that I am not welcome in certain family members’ homes because of my “lifestyle choice.” ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 923}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 954, 'width': 620, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 954, 'width': 620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ethicist/29mag-29ethi