 tables and electrified by portable generators; repurposed soda bottles holding gasoline-ethanol mixtures in hues from fruit punch to orangeade to apple juice. Grimy bills pass from hand to hand: 1,500 Guinean francs for a sweet potato, 2,000 for an onion, 5,000 for a SIM card, 8,000 for a liter of gasohol, 9,275 for a kilo of rice, 45,000 for a live chicken. According to 2012 figures from the government’s bureau of statistics, the most recent available, a troubling 55 percent of Guineans survive on less than 8,815 francs, or $1.20, a day, and the average per capita daily income nationwide is just over $3.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ebola1/29ebola1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ebola1/29ebola1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ebola1/29ebola1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ebola1/29ebola1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ebola1/29ebola1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/29/magazine/29ebola1/29ebola1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None,