 Nations, but a panel including Azerbaijan, China and Pakistan rejected it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — The countries that rendered a verdict Thursday on whether an advocacy group for press freedom can freely roam the halls of the United Nations included those that have jailed and harassed journalists: Azerbaijan, China, Pakistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Press Freedom Group’s Application for U.N. Accreditation is Rejected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee to Protect Journalists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCREDITATION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-27T01:26:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4027c02-02aa-55bf-813b-e8fe748755f4', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4027c02-02aa-55bf-813b-e8fe748755f4'}, {'abstract': 'Starr was stripped of his presidency after a report on mishandled accusations of sexual misconduct, but he will remain as chancellor, raising questions of accountability.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/27/sports/ncaafootball/at-baylor-charity-toward-kenneth-starr-after-sex-assault-report.html', 'snippet': 'Starr was stripped of his presidency after a repor