 the Navy says. (AP)', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Briefing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauner, Bruce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-27T01:53:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d330de87-da6e-59f6-9bda-18a2c37fd43d', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d330de87-da6e-59f6-9bda-18a2c37fd43d'}, {'abstract': 'A crunchy Friday themeless from Damon Gulczynski.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/goal-of-some-drives/', 'snippet': 'A crunchy Friday themeless from Damon Gulczynski.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY PUZZLE — It’s a holiday weekend and you’d think that Will Shortz would ease up on us, but no. Today’s crossword by Damon Gulczynski has some crunch (unexpected and lively entries) to it, and I had to work for my completed puzzle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goal of Some Drives', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-27T02:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/393ee17b-2611-5415-9421-13b7f4875a20', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/393ee17b-2611-5415-9421-13b7f4875a20'}, {'abstract': 'The truck, whose architecture has remained mostly the same since its inception in 1979, is a combination of luxury, utility, capability and status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/27/automobiles/autoreviews/video-review-the-mercedes-g550s-primal-appeal-endures.html', 'snippet': 'The truck, whose architecture has remained mostly the same since its inception in 1979, is a combination of luxury, utility, capability and status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MERCEDES-BENZ makes vehicles with cutting-edge design. The G550 isn’t one of them, and that gives it a war horse appeal. With an architecture that has remained much the same since its inception in 1979, the G-Class, also known as the Gelandewagen, could be the touchstone that spawned the phrase “old school.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Review: The Mercedes G550’s Primal Appeal Endures', 'kicker': 'Driven', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mercedes G550: Primal Appeal Endures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-27T02:06:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c109917-fba1-5d69-935c-c63d4b7aa34b', 'word_