hiroshima-japan.html', 'snippet': '“Technological progress without an equivalent progress in human institutions can doom us,” said Mr. Obama, the first sitting American president to visit the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HIROSHIMA, Japan — President Obama laid a wreath at the Hiroshima Peace Memorial on Friday, telling an audience that included survivors of America’s atomic bombing in 1945 that technology as devastating as nuclear arms demands a “moral revolution.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Hiroshima Memorial, Obama Says Nuclear Arms Require ‘Moral Revolution’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Hiroshima, Summoning Better Angels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hiroshima (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-27T05:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eedc69d5-03b4-563c-9e3b-5ee7f09338a7',