y-27/', 'snippet': 'Photos from The New York Times and photographers from around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from The New York Times and photographers from around the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Pictures: May 27', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andrew Testa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doug Mills', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-27T07:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79f46622-f383-57e3-b5e7-82bfa39b3464', 'word_count': 18, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79f46622-f383-57e3-b5e7-82bfa39b3464'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a catch-22: The longer we live, the more people will get the disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/27/opinion/obamas-pointless-cancer-moonshot.html', 'snippet': 'It’s a catch-22: The longer we live, the more people will get the disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oslo — EVER since Neil Armstrong walked on the moon, American politicians have promised “moonshots” — huge programs, stocked with technology and experts, to solve presumably intractable problems. A common target is cancer: Earlier this year President Obama announced the National Cancer Moonshot Initiative, a $1 billion program led by Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/27/opinion/27breivikWeb/27breivikWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articl