', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c6e603b-ae4e-5c44-a803-5bed710f3377', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c6e603b-ae4e-5c44-a803-5bed710f3377'}, {'abstract': 'Saudi Arabia has spent heavily to promote the radical form of Islam that inspired 9/11 and now inflames the Islamic State. Tiny Kosovo is a victim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/28/opinion/the-world-reaps-what-the-saudis-sow.html', 'snippet': 'Saudi Arabia has spent heavily to promote the radical form of Islam that inspired 9/11 and now inflames the Islamic State. Tiny Kosovo is a victim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saudi Arabia has frustrated American policy makers for years. Ostensibly a critical ally, sheltered from its enemies by American arms and aid, the kingdom has spent untold millions promoting Wahhabism, the radical form of Sunni Islam that inspired the 9/11 hijackers and that now inflames the Islamic State.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/28/opinion/28sat1/28sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/28/opinion/28sat1/28sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 643}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/28/opinion/28sat1/28sat1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 956, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/28/opinion/28sat1/28sat1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1649, 'width': 1539, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', '