l/from-a-middling-infielder-to-a-kindred-spirit.html', 'snippet': 'Forty-five years later, a fan of Mets shortstop Bud Harrelson reflects on what made an 11-year-old boy want a lifetime .236 hitter at his bar mitzvah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time not so long ago when young sports fans wrote actual letters to their heroes and sometimes received a photo or even a note or letter in return — not from an agent or public relations firm, but from the athlete himself. Sometimes the response came autographed, no invoice attached.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/sports/29wallach-web1/29wallach-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/29/sports/29wallach-web1/29wallach-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/sports/29wallach-web1/29wallach-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/sports/29wallach-web1/29wallach-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/sports/29wallach-web1/29wallach-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/29/sports/29wallach-web1/29wallach-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/sports/29wallach-web1/29wallach-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Middling Infielder to a Kindred Spirit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kindred Spirits With a Middling Infielder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrelson, Bud', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-28T16:40:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Wallach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b76a77e0-4afd-5b92-b1de-94bff7119528', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b76a77e0-4afd-5b92-b1de-94bff7119528'}, {'abstract': 'The superrich have stashed millions of works in tax-free storage. So what does that mean for the art?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/29/arts/design/one-of-the-worlds-greatest-art-collections-hides-behind-this-fence.html', 'snippet': 'The superrich have stashed millions of works in tax-free storage. So what does that mean for the art?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The drab free port zone near the Geneva city center, a compound of blocky gray and vanilla warehouses surrounded by train tracks, roads and a barbed-wire fence, looks like the kind of place where beauty goes to die. But within its walls, crated or sealed cheek by jowl in cramped storage vaults, are more than a million of some of the most exquisite artworks ever made.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times