: 'World leaders seem more interested in barricading their nations from the fallout of conflict than in dealing with its root causes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/29/opinion/sunday/as-rich-nations-turn-their-backs.html', 'snippet': 'World leaders seem more interested in barricading their nations from the fallout of conflict than in dealing with its root causes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world is witnessing the largest exodus of refugees in generations, spawned by armed conflicts in the Middle East, North Africa and South Asia. But “witnessing” is perhaps the wrong word. Many world leaders, including those who run most of the richest countries, are choosing to look the other way. They are more interested in barricading their nations from the fallout of conflict than in investing in peacekeeping and stability.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/opinion/sunday/29sun1/29sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/29/opinion/sunday/29sun1/29sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/opinion/sunday/29sun1/29sun1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/opinion/sunday/29sun1/29sun1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1134, 'width': 1823, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/29/opinion/sunday/29sun1/29sun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', '