4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television Sets and Media Devices', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-30T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/57ab9779-9774-559a-b453-671d4254fe96', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57ab9779-9774-559a-b453-671d4254fe96'}, {'abstract': 'Guidelines that allow former service members to transfer college credit are intended to help. They be may hurting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/30/opinion/veterans-deserve-a-chance-in-college-not-a-free-pass.html', 'snippet': 'Guidelines that allow former service members to transfer college credit are intended to help. They be may hurting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY six years in the Marine Corps taught me the importance of learning the basics. When the Marines teach a young recruit to shoot, they don’t skip parts of the training. Whether you have never touched a gun in your life or grew up hunting every weekend, the Marines drill you in how to steady your sights, master your breathing and control recoil. Every recruit is taught and then tested in the fundamentals of marksmanship before he or she advances in basic training.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/30/opinion/30mccoy/30mccoy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 869, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/30/opinion/30mccoy/30mccoy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 869}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/30/opinion/30mccoy/30mccoy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 707, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/30/opinion/30mccoy/30mccoy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1440, 'width': 994, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/30/opinion/30mccoy/30mccoy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/30/opinion/30mccoy/30mccoy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/30/opinion/30mccoy/30mccoy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Veterans Deserve a Chance in College, Not a Free Pass', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Shortchange Vets in College', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN COUNCIL ON EDUCATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-30T07:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Mccoy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlenam