'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-31T14:27:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By RON NIXON and MICHAEL LESTER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'NIXON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LESTER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/d854d131-515b-54a3-819e-b8b597b5892b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/d854d131-515b-54a3-819e-b8b597b5892b'}, {'abstract': 'Explosives from household chemicals can be hard even for dogs to detect, but a Transportation Security Administration center in Texas is determined to teach them how.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/06/01/us/tsa-trains-dogs-to-stay-one-sniff-ahead-of-bomb-makers.html', 'snippet': 'Explosives from household chemicals can be hard even for dogs to detect, but a Transportation Security Administration center in Texas is determined to teach them how.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANTONIO — Just after dawn on a recent May morning, Ajax, a 2-year-old black Labrador retriever, eagerly worked his way through a sparsely furnished room sniffing for explosives. On his third try, he picked up a scent behind a piece of furniture near the front of the room.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'T.S.A. Trains Dogs to Stay One Sniff Ahead of Bomb Makers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'T.S.A. Is Training Dogs to Stay  One Sniff Ahead of Bomb Makers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smell (Olfaction)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jeh C', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-31T14:27:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46305c08-af23-5dbe-8a93-0d6cb7f7b68d', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46305c08-af23-5dbe-8a93-0d6cb7f7b68d'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s visit to Hiroshima highlights a slow dismantling of Japan’s pacifist legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/06/01/opinion/why-obama-is-shinzo-abes-enabler.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s visit to Hiroshima highlights a slow dismantling of Japan’s pacifist legacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TSURUGA, Japan — Visiting Hiroshima last Friday, President Obama warned that overcoming the perils of global conflict and nuclear weapons will require a “moral revolution” sustained by “the radical and necessary notion that we are part of a single human family.” He omitted to mention that this notion has been the constitutional basis of Japan’s foreign policy since 1947. Future historians may conclude that Mr. Obama’s visit to Hiroshima provided a spectacle to help remilitarize the world’s wealthiest, most populous pacifist country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/opinion/01richard/01richard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/06/01/opinion/01richard/01richard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/opinion/01richard/01richard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/opinion/01richard/01richard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/opinion/01richard/01richard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/06/01/opinion/01richard/01richard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/opinion/01richard/01richard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Obama Is Shinzo Abe’s Enabler', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-05-31T14:28:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dreux Richard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dreux', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/732b1d65-a1ab-536b-b7dd-5ea0c0b27451', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/732b1d65-a1ab-536b-b7dd-5ea0c0b27451'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The Trianon Palace at Versailles to reopen in 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/05/31/1916-palace-at-versailles-to-reopen/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The Trianon Palace at Versailles to reopen in 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The Herald has been informed that the Trianon Palace at Versailles would reopen on May 31. At the outbreak of war the Trianon was taken over by the British Red Cross Society as a hospital for the wounded soldiers. Last February, M. Rey took the Trianon and undertook to renovate it completely. The hotel contains 150 rooms, each one of which looks out upon a fine view. Many of the employés have been heroes in the war.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, June 1, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/blogs/01-iht-retrospective-Trianon/01-iht-retrospective-Trianon-jumbo.png', 'height': 397, 'width': 509, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 