rian amber beads sourced from an antique store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Paris-based jeweler Alessandro Sabbatini insists he doesn’t search for materials to realize the one-of-a-kind pieces he dreams up for his two-year-old line called Sabba. (He makes fewer than 40 pieces a year.) Instead, he says, they find him. After months of staring at a Victorian necklace of graduated amber beads that called out to the 28-year-old from an antique shop, inspiration struck. It is now a towering pair of earrings resembling a dangling Chinese temple. Fashioned with a series of delicate but complex titanium armatures, the pieces are hinged with elongated diamond baguettes, much like a string of twinkling paper lanterns.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/12/t-magazine/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t_CA0/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/06/12/t-magazine/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t_CA0/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 717}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/12/t-magazine/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t_CA0/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 857, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/12/t-magazine/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t_CA0/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1714, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/12/t-magazine/12tmag-06qual_thing_sabba-t